hadiths[1710]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1838","Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mudhhib al-Waiz informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Himdan ibn Malik informed us, recited to him: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me from his book: Hushaym narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal and Mughirah informed us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank from Zamzam while standing."
"1839","Hushaym narrated to us, Ajlah informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whatever Allah wills and you will. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you made me and Allah equals? Rather, whatever Allah alone wills."
"1840","Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped my head and supplicated for me for wisdom."
"1841","Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House while upon his camel, and touched the Stone with a curved staff that was with him. He said: And he came to the drinking place and said: Give me to drink. They said: The people wade into this, but we will bring you from the house. He said: I have no need of that; give me to drink from what the people drink."
"1842","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A report is not like eyewitnessing."
"1843","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent a night at my maternal aunt Maymunah bint al-Harith, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with her on her night. He stood praying at night, so I stood to his left to pray with his prayer. He said: So he took hold of a forelock of mine, or my head, until he placed me on his right."
"1844","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When Barirah was given the choice, I saw her husband following her in the streets of Madinah with his tears flowing upon his beard. So Abbas was spoken to to speak to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Barirah: He is your husband. She said: Are you commanding me with him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I am only an intercessor. He said: So he gave her the choice, and she chose herself. And he was a slave of the family of al-Mughirah called Mughith."
"1845","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists. He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"1846","Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while he was sixty-five years old."
"1847","Hushaym narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The food which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade to be sold until it is taken possession of. Ibn Abbas said: And I consider everything like it."
"1848","Hushaym narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed and said: When the pilgrim in ihram does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers, and when he does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks."
"1849","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram and fasting."
"1850","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his she-camel broke his neck while he was in ihram, and he died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection uttering the Talbiyah."
"1851","Hushaym narrated to us, Awf informed us, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of Jam: Come, gather pebbles for me. So I gathered for him pebbles of Khadhf, and when I placed them in his hand he said: Yes, with the likes of these. And beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were only destroyed by extremism in religion."
"1852","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled from Madinah fearing none but Allah Almighty, and prayed two rakahs, two rakahs, until he returned."
"1853","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: This verse was revealed while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in hiding in Makkah: And do not recite loudly in your prayer nor lower it therein. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions he raised his voice with the Quran, and when the polytheists heard that they reviled the Quran, reviled the One who sent it down and the one who brought it. He said: So Allah Almighty said to His Prophet: And do not recite loudly in your prayer, meaning your recitation, lest the polytheists hear and revile the Quran, and do not lower it therein from your companions so that you do not let them hear the Quran until they take it from you, but seek between that a way."
"1854","Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Wadi al-Azraq and said: Which valley is this? They said: This is Wadi al-Azraq. He said: It is as if I am looking at Musa, peace be upon him, descending from the pass with a loud supplication to Allah Almighty with the Talbiyah. Until he came to Thaniyyat Harsha and said: Which pass is this? They said: Thaniyyat Harsha. He said: It is as if I am looking at Yunus ibn Matta upon a red curly-haired she-camel, wearing a woolen cloak, the halter of his she-camel of palm fiber. Hushaym said, meaning fiber, while he is uttering the Talbiyah."
"1855","Hushaym narrated to us, our companions informed us, among them Shubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked his sacrificial camel on the right side, then wiped the blood from it, and hung two sandals upon it."
"1856","Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Sab ibn Jaththamah al-Asadi gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a leg of wild donkey while he was in ihram, so he returned it and said: We are in ihram."
"1857","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about one who shaved before slaughtering and the like, and he began saying: No harm, no harm."
"1858","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He was asked about one who brought forward something of his rites before something, and he began saying: No harm."
"1859","Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man said: And those who shorten? He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. The man said: And those who shorten? He said on the third or fourth: And those who shorten."
"1860","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat with Usamah riding behind him, and poured forth from Jam with Al-Fadl ibn Abbas riding behind him. He said: And he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1861","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman traveled by sea and vowed that if Allah Blessed and Almighty saved her she would fast a month. So Allah Almighty saved her, but she did not fast until she died. So a relative of hers came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Fast."
"1862","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah who said: We were with Ibn Abbas in Makkah, and I said: When we are with you we pray four, and when we return to our lodgings we pray two. He said: That is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1863","Ishaq, meaning Ibn Yusuf, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking a living soul as a target."
"1864","Ishaq, meaning Ibn Yusuf, narrated to us, from Sharik, from Khusayf, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The sun eclipsed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions stood, and he recited a long surah, then bowed, then raised his head and recited, then bowed and prostrated twice, then stood and recited and bowed, then prostrated twice: four bowings and four prostrations in two rakahs."
"1865","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was expelled from Makkah, Abu Bakr said: They expelled their prophet; to Allah we belong and to Him we return; they will surely perish. Then was revealed: Permission is given to those who are fought because they were wronged, and Allah is indeed able to grant them victory. He said: So it was known that there would be fighting. Ibn Abbas said: It is the first verse revealed concerning fighting."
"1866","Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes an image will be punished on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes spirit into it, and he will not breathe; whoever pretends to have seen a dream will be punished on the Day of Resurrection until he ties two barley grains, and he will not tie; and whoever listens to the talk of people fleeing from him with it, punishment will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection."
"1867","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad al-Ghatafani, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of them, when he approaches his wife, says: In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep Satan away from me and keep Satan away from what You provide us, then if a child is decreed between them in that, Satan will never harm that child."
"1868","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah while the people were advancing payment for dates for one year and two years, or he said two years and three. He said: Whoever advances payment for dates, let him advance payment for a known measure and a known weight."
"1869","Ismail informed us, Abu al-Tayyah informed us, from Musa ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent eighteen sacrificial camels with a man and gave him instruction concerning them. He went then returned to him and said: What if some of them become exhausted for us? He said: Slaughter it, then dye its sandal in its blood, then place it upon its side, and do not eat from it, neither you nor anyone of your traveling companions. And Ismail Ibn Ulayyah heard nothing from Abu al-Tayyah except this hadith."
"1870","He said: Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I do not know whether I heard it from Said ibn Jubayr or was informed of it from him, he said: I came upon Ibn Abbas at Arafah while he was eating pomegranate. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast at Arafah, and Umm al-Fadl sent him milk and he drank it. And he said: May Allah curse so-and-so; they deliberately took the greatest day of Hajj and effaced its adornment, and the adornment of Hajj is only the Talbiyah."
"1871","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, that Ali burned people who apostatized from Islam. That reached Ibn Abbas and he said: I would not have burned them with fire, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not punish with the punishment of Allah. And I would have killed them, for the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever changes his religion, kill him. That reached Ali, may Allah ennoble his face, and he said: Woe to Ibn Umm Ibn Abbas."
"1872","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have no evil example: the one who takes back his gift is like the dog returning to its vomit."
"1873","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Ata narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: When: When the help of Allah and the victory comes was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My soul has been announced to me that I am to be taken in that year."
"1874","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the two prayers while traveling: Maghrib and Isha, and Zuhr and Asr."
"1875","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed is he who reviles his father; cursed is he who reviles his mother; cursed is he who slaughters for other than Allah; cursed is he who alters the landmarks of the earth; cursed is he who leads a blind man astray from the road; cursed is he who commits intercourse with an animal; cursed is he who does the deed of the people of Lut."
"1876","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Zaynab his daughter to her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi with the first marriage, and did not initiate anything."
"1877","Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he circumambulated with Muawiyah around the House, and Muawiyah began touching all the corners. Ibn Abbas said to him: Why do you touch these two corners when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not touch them? Muawiyah said: Nothing of the House is abandoned. Ibn Abbas said: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example. Muawiyah said: You spoke the truth."
"1878","Marwan narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining between a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt, and between two paternal aunts and two maternal aunts."
"1879","Marwan narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade the wholly silk garment of raw silk. Ibn Abbas said: As for the warp and the emblem, we see no harm in it."
"1880","Mamar, meaning Ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi, narrated to us, he said: Khusayf said, more than one narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade the wholly silk thereof; as for the emblem, then no."
"1881","Aththam ibn Ali al-Amiri narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs at night, then leave and use the tooth-stick."
"1882","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar informed us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among a group of his companions, Abd al-Razzaq said, from the Ansar, when a great star was shot and lit up. He said: What did you say when the like of this occurred in the Jahiliyyah? He said: We used to say a great one is born or a great one dies. I said to al-Zuhri: Were they shot in the Jahiliyyah? He said: Yes, but they were intensified when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not shot for the death of anyone nor for his life, but our Lord, Blessed is His name, when He decrees a matter the bearers of the Throne glorify, then the people of heaven who are next to them glorify, until the glorification reaches this lowest heaven. Then the people of heaven who are next to the bearers of the Throne inquire, and those next to the bearers of the Throne say to the bearers of the Throne: What did your Lord say? And they inform them, and the people of each heaven inform a heaven, until the report ends at this heaven. And the jinn snatch the hearing and are shot. What they bring as it is, is true, but they cast and add. Abd al-Razzaq said: And the jinn snatch and are shot."
"1883","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas: Men from the Ansar, from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that they were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night when a star was shot, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: When our Lord decrees a matter, the bearers of the Throne glorify Him, then those next to them, then those next to them, until the glorification reaches the lowest heaven. And those next to the bearers of the Throne say to the bearers of the Throne: What did your Lord say? And they say: The truth, and He is the Most High, the Most Great. And they say such-and-such. And the people of the heavens inform one another until the report reaches the lowest heaven. He said: And the devils come and listen to the report and cast it to their allies and are shot with it to them. What they bring as it is, is true, but they add to it and fabricate and omit."
"1884","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas and from Aishah, that they both said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was overcome, he began casting a woolen garment over his face, and when distressed we lifted it from him while he says: May Allah curse the Jews and Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. Aishah says: He warns them against the like of what they did."
"1885","Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Hakam, from Ibn Abbas, that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The month is completed at twenty-nine."
"1886","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I prayed Zuhr at al-Batha behind a foolish old man, and he pronounced twenty-two Takbirs, pronouncing Takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head. He said: So Ibn Abbas said: That is the prayer of Abu al-Qasim, upon him prayer and peace."
"1887","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, and Ibn Jafar, Said narrated to us with the meaning, and Ibn Abi Adi said: From Said, from Abu Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in prayers and was silent, so we recite in what the Prophet of Allah recited in and are silent in what he was silent in. It was said to him: Perhaps he used to recite to himself, and he became angry at it and said: Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accused? And Ibn Jafar and Abd al-Razzaq said: Do you accuse the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"1888","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and a virgin is to be consulted concerning herself, and her permission is her silence."
"1889","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab narrated to me, that Ibn Abbas used to perform ablution once once, and he ascribed that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1890","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Sulayman ibn Yasar heard, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman from Khatham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of Jam while Al-Fadl ibn Abbas was riding behind him. She said: The obligation of Allah in Hajj upon His servants has overtaken my father, a very old man who cannot hold upon the saddle. Do you see that I should perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"1891","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Abbas: I came, I and Al-Fadl, while we were upon a donkey, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying with the people at Arafah. So we passed by part of the row, dismounted from it, left it grazing, and entered into the row, and the Messenger of Allah said nothing to me."
"1892","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the Day of the Conquest fasting, until when he was at al-Kadid he broke his fast. And only the later of the deed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is to be taken. It was said to Sufyan: The statement, only the later is to be taken, is it from the statement of al-Zuhri or the statement of Ibn Abbas? He said: So it is in the hadith."
"1893","Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, that Sad ibn Ubadah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow that was upon his mother who died before fulfilling it. He said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"1894","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, that Abu Bakr swore an oath upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not swear."
"1895","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Walah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any skin that is tanned has become pure."
"1896","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Move away from the belly of Muhassir, and you must use the like of the pebbles of Khadhf."
"1897","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and a virgin, her father consults her concerning herself, and her permission is her silence."
"1898","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Rawha when he met riders. He greeted them and said: Who are the people? They said: Muslims. He said: Then who are you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then a woman was startled and took the arm of a boy and brought him out of her litter and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is reward."
"1899","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, with its meaning."
"1900","Sufyan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Suhaym narrated to us, Sufyan said: I retained nothing from him besides it, he said: I heard it from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr. He said: O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream which a Muslim sees or which is seen for him. Then he said: Verily I have been forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, glorify therein the Lord, and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is likely to be answered for you."
"1901","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not punish with the punishment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1902","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Ata from Ibn Abbas: I bear witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he prayed before the sermon on Eid, then he delivered the sermon, then he saw that he had not made the women hear, so he went to them and reminded them and exhorted them and commanded them to give charity, so the woman began to cast the earring and the ring and the thing."
"1903","Sufyan narrated to us from Asim from al-Shabi from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank from a bucket of Zamzam standing. Sufyan said: Thus I presume."
"1904","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Judan from Amr ibn Harmalah from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, with Ibn Abbas on his right and Khalid ibn al-Walid on his left, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: The drink is yours, and if you wish you may prefer Khalid with it. He said: I would not prefer anyone over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1905","Sufyan narrated to us from Mamar from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, Allah willing, meaning: Ibn Abbas sought permission to visit Aishah, and her nephews kept pressing her. She said: I fear he will praise me. When she gave him permission, he said: There is nothing between you and meeting the beloved ones except that the soul parts from the body. You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved none but one who is good, and your necklace fell on the night of al-Abwa, so verses of the Quran were revealed concerning you, so there is no mosque among the mosques of the Muslims except your vindication is recited in it during hours of the night and hours of the day. She said: Leave me be from your praise, O Ibn Abbas. By Allah, I would have wished."
"1906","Sufyan narrated to us from Layth from a man from Ibn Abbas that he said to her: You were only named Mother of the Believers so that you may be made fortunate, and it is your name before you were born."
"1907","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Karim from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, Allah willing: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breathing into the vessel or blowing into it."
"1908","Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Salim from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If one of them, when he comes to his wife, says: In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep me away from Satan and keep Satan away from what You provide us, then if a child is decreed between them, Satan will not harm him."
"1909","Sufyan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay narrated to us, he said: Shaddad ibn Maqil and I entered upon Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left nothing except what is between these two covers. And we entered upon Muhammad ibn Ali and he said the like of that. He said: And al-Mukhtar used to say: the revelation."
"1910","Sufyan narrated to us, he said, and Musa ibn Abi Aishah said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: Ibn Abbas said: When Quran was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he wanted to memorize it. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Do not move your tongue with it to hasten with it. Indeed upon Us is its collection and its recitation, and when We recite it then follow its recitation."
"1911","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr, he said: Kurayb informed me from Ibn Abbas that he said: When he prayed the two rakahs of Fajr, he lay down until he snored. And we used to say to Amr: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."
"1912","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at night. He said: So he performed a light ablution, then stood, and Ibn Abbas did as he had done, then he came and stood and prayed, so he moved him and placed him on his right, then he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he lay down until he snored, then the caller to prayer came to him, then he stood for the prayer and did not perform ablution."
"1913","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon while saying: You will meet Allah barefoot, naked, walking, uncircumcised."
"1914","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, he says: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man fell from his camel and his neck was broken and he died while in ihram. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves and bury him in his two garments and do not cover his head, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah. And he said once: uttering the talbiyah."
"1915","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: And do not bring perfume near him."
"1916","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas concerning His statement, Mighty and Majestic: And We did not make the vision which We showed you except as a trial for the people. He said: It is a vision of the eye which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw on the night he was taken by night."
"1917","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he said once: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon saying: Whoever does not find two sandals, let him wear two leather socks, and whoever does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers."
"1918","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, Jabir ibn Zayd informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight together and seven together. He said: I said to him: O Abu al-Shahta, I think he delayed the noon prayer and hastened the afternoon, and delayed the sunset prayer and hastened the night prayer. He said: And I think that too."
"1919","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr said: Abu al-Shahta said: Who is she? He said: I said: They say Maymunah. He said: Ibn Abbas informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram."
"1920","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas: I am among those whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead on the night of Muzdalifah among the weak of his family. And he said once: Indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the weak of his family."
"1921","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only ran around the Kabah to show the polytheists his strength."
"1922","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr first, then we memorized from Tawus, and he said once: Tawus informed me from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"1923","And Sufyan narrated it to us, and he said: Amr from Ata and Tawus from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"1924","My father said, and Sufyan said from Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked."
"1925","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas who said: Al-Muhassab is nothing; it is only a place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted."
"1926","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Ata and Ibn Jurayj from Ata from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed it until as much of the night as Allah willed had passed. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, the women and children have slept. So he came out and said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them to pray it at this hour."
"1927","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Tawus from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven and was forbidden to tuck up his hair and his garments."
"1928","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Tawus who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: As for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade to be sold until it is taken possession of, it is food. And Ibn Abbas said by his own opinion: And I do not think everything except to be the like of it."
"1929","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Madinah, resident and not traveling, seven and eight."
"1930","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Awsajah from Ibn Abbas: A man died at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving no heir except a slave whom he had freed, so he gave him his inheritance."
"1931","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Muhammad ibn Hunayn from Ibn Abbas: I wonder at one who anticipates the month, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast until you see it. Or he said: Fast upon seeing it."
"1932","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Said ibn al-Huwayrith: He heard Ibn Abbas say: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went to relieve himself, then he came out and called for food. And he said once: Then food was brought, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not perform ablution? He said: I have not prayed that I should perform ablution."
"1933","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Abu Mabad from Ibn Abbas who said: I did not know the end of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by the takbir. Amr said: I said to him: Did you narrate to me? He said: No, I did not narrate to you of it."
"1934","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Abu Mabad from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man should be alone with a woman, and no woman should travel except with a mahram with her. And a man came and said: My wife has gone out for Hajj while I have been enlisted in such and such expedition. He said: Go and perform Hajj with your wife."
"1935","Sufyan narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim, the maternal uncle of Ibn Abi Najih: He heard Said ibn Jubayr say: Ibn Abbas said: Thursday, and what is Thursday? Then he wept until his tears wet, and he said once: his tears, the pebbles. We said: O Abu al-Abbas, and what is Thursday? He said: The pain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became severe, so he said: Bring me that I may write for you a writing after which you will never go astray. So they disputed, and dispute is not proper in the presence of a prophet. So they said: What is the matter with him, has he become delirious? Sufyan said: meaning he is raving. Ask him to make it understood. So they went repeating to him, and he said: Leave me, for what I am in is better than what you call me to. And he commanded three things, and Sufyan said once: He enjoined three things. He said: Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula, and honor the delegations with the like of what I used to honor them with. And Said was silent about the third, so I do not know whether he was silent about it deliberately, and he said once: or he forgot it, and Sufyan said once: or that he left it or forgot it."
"1936","Sufyan narrated to us from Sulayman from Tawus from Ibn Abbas: People used to depart in every direction, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none depart until his last covenant is with the House."
"1937","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Abi Najih from Abdullah ibn Kathir from Abu al-Minhal from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while they were advancing loans for dates for two and three years, so he said: Whoever advances a loan, let him advance it in a known measure and a known weight until a known term."
"1938","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me for seventy years, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I did not know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted a day seeking its merit over other days except the day of Ashura. And Sufyan said another time: Except this day, meaning Ashura, and this month, the month of Ramadan."
"1939","Sufyan narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I am among those whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead on the night of Muzdalifah among the weak of his family."
"1940","He said: Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven and was forbidden to tuck up hair or garment."
"1941","Sufyan narrated to us from Ammar from Salim: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who killed a believer then repented and believed and did righteous deeds then was guided. He said: Woe to you, and how could he attain guidance? I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The slain will come holding on to the killer saying: O Lord, ask this one for what he killed me. By Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed it to your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not abrogate it after He revealed it. He said: Woe to you, and how could he attain guidance?"
"1942","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Yazid informed us from Ibn Miqsam from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments: in his shirt in which he died and a Najrani cloak; the cloak is two garments."
"1943","Ibn Idris narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped between Makkah and Madinah while fasting and in ihram."
"1944","Ismail, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the mukatab: He is freed to the extent of what he has paid, with the blood-money of a free man, and to the extent of what remains enslaved of him, with the blood-money of a slave."
"1945","Ismail narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha: Ammar, freedman of Banu Hisham, narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-five years old."
"1946","Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: The last hardship the believer meets is death. And concerning His saying: A day when the sky will be like molten brass, he said: Like the dregs of oil. And concerning His saying: hours of the night, he said: the depth of the night. And he said: Do you know what the departure of knowledge is? He said: It is the departure of the scholars from the earth."
"1947","Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the man in whose interior there is nothing of the Quran is like the ruined house."
"1948","Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in Makkah, then he was commanded with the migration, and there was revealed to him: And say: My Lord, admit me with a truthful admission and bring me out with a truthful departure and grant me from Yourself a supporting authority."
"1949","Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two qiblahs are not proper in one land, and there is no jizyah upon a Muslim."
"1950","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Sufyan, he said: al-Mughirah ibn al-Numan narrated to me from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People will be gathered barefoot, naked, uncircumcised, so the first to be clothed is Ibrahim, peace be upon him. Then he recited: As We began the first creation We shall repeat it."
"1951","Yahya narrated to us from al-Awzai: al-Zuhri narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk then rinsed his mouth and said: It has fat."
"1952","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas who said: The daughter of Hamzah was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding."
"1953","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the noon and afternoon prayers and the sunset and night prayers in Madinah without fear or rain. It was said to Ibn Abbas: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to impose hardship upon his nation."
"1954","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Zabyan from Ibn Abbas who said: A man from Banu Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, show me the seal between your shoulders, for I am among the most skilled of people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shall I not show you a sign? He said: Yes. So he looked at a palm tree and said: Call that cluster. So he called it and it came hopping until it stood before him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to it: Return. So it returned to its place. So the Amiri said: O family of Banu Amir, I have never seen a man more sorcerous than today."
"1955","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Masud ibn Malik from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by the easterly wind, and Ad were destroyed by the westerly wind."
"1956","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Ziyad ibn al-Husayn from Abu al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas concerning His statement, Mighty and Majestic: The heart did not lie about what it saw. He said: Muhammad saw his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with his heart twice."
"1957","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from Abu Malik al-Ashjai from Ibn Hudayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a daughter born to him and does not bury her alive nor humiliate her nor prefer his child over her, meaning the male, Allah will admit him to Paradise through her."
"1958","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and stayed nineteen, praying two rakahs, two rakahs. Ibn Abbas said: So when we travel and stay nineteen, we pray two rakahs, two rakahs, and if we stay more than that, we pray four."
"1959","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed on the day of Taif whoever came out to him of the slaves of the polytheists."
"1960","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah. And Ikrimah used to dislike selling the young camel."
"1961","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Shaybani, narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the people of Jurash forbidding them to mix raisins and dates."
"1962","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us from al-Shabi from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the occupant of a grave after he was buried."
"1963","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Umar from Ibn Abbas who said: Raisins used to be soaked for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he would drink it on the day and the morrow and the day after the morrow until the evening of the third, then it would be ordered and given to drink or poured away."
"1964","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ajlah narrated to us from Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: What Allah wills and you will. So he said: Rather, what Allah wills alone."
"1965","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Hakam from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in an open space with nothing before him."
"1966","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abdullah ibn Rawahah in a detachment, and that coincided with Friday. He said: So he sent his companions ahead and said: I shall stay behind and pray Friday with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I shall catch up with them. He said: When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he said: What prevented you from going forth with your companions? He said: So he said: I wanted to pray Friday with you, then catch up with them. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if you spent what is on earth, you would not attain their going forth."
"1967","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us from Ata from Ibn Abbas who said: Najdah al-Haruri wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about killing children, and about the fifth, to whom it belongs, and about the child, when orphanhood ends for him, and about women, whether they used to go out with him or attend fighting, and about the slave, whether he has a share in the spoils. He said: So Ibn Abbas wrote to him: As for children, if you are al-Khidr, knowing the disbeliever from the believer, then kill them. And as for the fifth, we used to say it is ours, but our people claimed it is not ours. And as for women, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out with women with him, and they would treat the sick and attend to the wounded, and they did not attend fighting. And as for the child, orphanhood ends for him when he reaches puberty. And as for the slave, he has no share of the spoils, but something used to be granted to them."
"1968","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Muslim al-Batin from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than these days, meaning the ten days. He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, except a man who went out with himself and his wealth then did not return from that with anything."
"1969","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih, he said, and al-Amash narrated to us from Mujahid, without Ibn Abbas in it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, meaning: There are no days in which deeds are done."
"1970","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Muslim al-Batin from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died owing a month of fasting, shall I make it up for her? He said: So he said: Tell me, if your mother owed a debt, would you not settle it? She said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more deserving."
"1971","Abu Muawiyah narrated to me, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Abbas from Abdullah ibn Umayr, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I remain until next year, I shall surely fast the ninth day."
"1972","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran in his Hajj and in all his Umrahs, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and the caliphs."
"1973","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to us from Mihran Abu Safwan from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends Hajj, let him hasten."
"1974","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Muharibi, narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us from Mahran Abu Safwan, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends Hajj, let him hasten."
"1975","Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Tawus from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at the eclipse of the sun eight bowings and four prostrations."
"1976","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir wrote to me narrating from Ikrimah that Umar used to say concerning the prohibited: it is an oath to be expiated. He said: Hisham said: And Yahya wrote to me narrating from Yala ibn Hakim from Said ibn Jubayr that Ibn Abbas used to say concerning the prohibited: it is an oath to be expiated. So Ibn Abbas said: You have had in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"1977","Ismail narrated to us, Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas narrated to us: He heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a commanded servant. He conveyed, by Allah, what he was sent with, and he did not single us out apart from people with anything, except three: He commanded us to perfect ablution, and not to eat charity, and not to mate a donkey upon a mare. Musa said: Then I met Abdullah ibn Hasan and said: Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me such and such. So he said: Horses were few among Banu Hashim, so he wished they would increase among them."
"1978","Ismail narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Harmalah narrated to me from Ibn Abbas who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid and I entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Maymunah bint al-Harith. She said: Shall we not feed you of a gift that Umm Hufayd gifted to us? He said: So two roasted lizards were brought. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat. So Khalid said to him: As if you find it distasteful? He said: Yes. She said: Shall I not give you to drink of milk gifted to us? So he said: Yes. He said: So a vessel of milk was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, with me on his right and Khalid on his left. So he said to me: The drink is yours, and if you wish you may prefer Khalid with it. So I said: I would not prefer anyone over your leftover. So he said: Whoever Allah feeds with food, let him say: O Allah, bless it for us and feed us better than it. And whoever Allah gives milk to drink, let him say: O Allah, bless it for us and increase us of it. For there is nothing that suffices in place of food and drink except milk."
"1979","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Umar ibn Abi Harmalah from Ibn Abbas from Umm Hufayd: She gifted to her sister Maymunah two lizards, then he mentioned it."
"1980","Abu Muawiyah and Waki, in meaning, narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Mujahid, he said, and Waki: I heard Mujahid narrating from Tawus from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves and said: They are being punished, and they are not being punished for a great matter. As for one of them, he used not to guard himself from urine. Waki said: from his urine. And as for the other, he used to go about with tale-bearing. Then he took a palm stalk and split it in two halves and planted one in each grave. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do this? He said: Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry. Waki said: they dry."
"1981","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Mansur from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a wall of the walls of Madinah and heard the sound of two persons being punished in their graves, then he mentioned it, and said: Until they dry, or: as long as they do not dry."
"1982","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the effeminate among men and the masculine among women, and said: Expel them from your houses. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled so-and-so, and Umar expelled so-and-so."
"1983","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Ata from Ibn Abbas who said: I bear witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed before the sermon, then he delivered the sermon, then he saw that he had not made the women hear, so he went to them, with Bilal with him spreading his garment, and he exhorted them and commanded them to give charity. So the woman began to cast, and Ayyub pointed to his ear and to his throat, as if meaning the earring and the necklace."
"1984","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the mukatab: He is freed to the extent of what he has paid, with the blood-money of a free man, and to the extent of what remains enslaved of him, with the blood-money of a slave."
"1985","Ismail narrated to us, Hatim ibn Abi Saghir informed us from Simak ibn Harb from Ikrimah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it, and if clouds come between you and it, complete the number thirty, and do not anticipate the month by fasting ahead. Hatim said: meaning the count of Shaban."
"1986","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Abd al-Malik: Ata narrated to us from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah with Usamah ibn Zayd behind him. The camel swerved with him while he raised his hands not exceeding his head. So he traveled gently until he came to Jam, then he poured forth the next morning with al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him, and he kept reciting the talbiyah until he stoned the Aqabah pillar."
"1987","Yahya narrated to us from Habib ibn Shihab: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day he addressed the people at Tabuk: There is none among people like a man holding the head of his horse, striving in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and avoiding the evils of people, and like another dwelling in a blessing, honoring his guest and giving his due."
"1988","Yahya narrated to us from Malik: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me from Ata ibn Yasar from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder then prayed without performing ablution."
"1989","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham: Qatadah narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the milk of the sheep that feeds on filth, and the animal made a target, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"1990","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: al-Hasan ibn Muslim narrated to me from Tawus who said: I was with Ibn Abbas when Zayd ibn Thabit said to him: Do you give a fatwa to the menstruating woman to depart before her last covenant is with the House? He said: Yes. He said: Then do not give fatwa to that effect. He said: If not, then ask so-and-so the Ansari woman whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her with that. So Zayd returned to Ibn Abbas laughing and said: I see you have spoken the truth."
"1991","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Mujahid from Tawus from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no migration after the conquest, but jihad and intention, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth."
"1992","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ibn Abbas who said: Sufyan said: I do not know it except from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or a trace of knowledge. He said: The line."
"1993","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Mukhawwal narrated to me from Muslim al-Batin from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and Has there come, and in Friday prayer Surah al-Jumuah and When the hypocrites come to you."
"1994","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate of what fire had touched, then prayed without performing ablution."
"1995","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us from Muhammad from Ibn Abbas who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between Makkah and Madinah, and he prayed two rakahs, fearing none but Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1996","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham: Qatadah narrated to us from Musa ibn Salamah who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: When you do not catch the prayer in the mosque, how much do you pray at al-Batha? He said: Two rakahs; that is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1997","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan dictated it to me to Shubah, he said: I heard Amr ibn Murrah: Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Muallim narrated to me: Taliq ibn Qays al-Hanafi, brother of Abu Salih, narrated to me from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: My Lord, aid me and do not aid against me, and support me and do not support against me, and plan for me and do not plan against me, and guide me and facilitate guidance to me, and support me against one who transgresses against me. My Lord, make me grateful to You, remembering of You, fearful of You, obedient to You, humble to You, oft-returning, turning to You. My Lord, accept my repentance and wash my sin and answer my supplication and establish my proof and guide my heart and make my tongue truthful and remove the rancor of my heart."
"1998","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Abu Bishr narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast until we would say: He will not break fast, and break fast until we would say: He will not fast. And he did not fast a complete month since he came to Madinah except Ramadan."
"1999","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: These and these are equal: the little finger and the thumb."
"2000","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas, he said: al-Walid ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Yusuf ibn Mahak from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whatever knowledge a man acquires from the stars, he acquires thereby a branch of sorcery; whatever he increases, he increases."
"2001","Yahya narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Abu Raja, Ibn Abbas narrated to me, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If one intends a good deed and does it, it is written tenfold, and if he does not do it, one good deed is written, and if he intends an evil deed and does it, one evil deed is written, and if he does not do it, a good deed is written."
"2002","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said, and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said, and al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate meat or a bone with meat on it, then prayed and did not touch water."
"2003","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that a domestic sheep belonging to Maymunah died, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why did you not make use of its skin, why did you not tan it, for its tanning is its purification."
"2004","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, al-Hasan ibn Muslim narrated to me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the Eid prayer without adhan and without iqamah."
"2005","Yahya narrated to us, I heard al-Amash, Muslim narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother had the fasting of a month incumbent upon her, then she died, shall I fast it on her behalf. He said: If your mother had a debt, would you pay it off. She said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more deserving to be paid off."
"2006","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed masculinized women and effeminate men, and said: Expel them from your houses. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, expelled so-and-so, and Umar expelled so-and-so."
"2007","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Awzai, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank milk, then rinsed his mouth and said: It has greasiness."
"2008","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Sulayman, meaning al-Amash, narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Umarah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Talib fell ill, so Quraysh came to him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him visiting him, and at his head was the sitting place of one man, so Abu Jahl stood and sat in it. They said: Your brother's son disparages our gods. He said: What is the matter with your people complaining about you. He said: O uncle, I want them to accept one word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay jizyah to them. He said: What is it. He said: There is no god but Allah. So they stood and said: Has he made the gods one god. He said: And there was revealed Sad, By the Quran full of reminder, and he recited until he reached Indeed this is a wondrous thing. And Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it. And my father said: al-Ashjai said: Yahya ibn Abbad."
"2009","Yahya narrated to us, from Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, my father narrated to me, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I am a man of the people of Khurasan, and our land is a cold land, and he mentioned kinds of drink. He said: Avoid what intoxicates, of raisin or dates or other than that. He said: What do you say about nabidh of the jar. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the nabidh of the jar."
"2010","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me that Ibn Abbas informed him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: As if I am looking at him, black, bow-legged, demolishing it stone by stone, meaning the Kabah."
"2011","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, Qariz narrated to me, from Abu Ghatfan, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas perform ablution. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Blow water out of the nose twice thoroughly, or three times."
"2012","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say at times of distress: There is no god but Allah, the Tremendous, the Forbearing, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Tremendous Throne, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth, Lord of the Noble Throne."
"2013","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, al-Hakam narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I was aided by al-Saba, the east wind, and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur, the west wind."
"2014","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Shatha informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married while in ihram."
"2015","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Shatha informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering the khutbah, saying: Whoever does not find a waist-wrapper and finds trousers, let him wear them, and whoever does not find sandals and finds leather socks, let him wear them. I said: He did not say: Let him cut them. He said: No."
"2016","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Said ibn al-Huwayrith narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, relieved himself, then ate food and did not touch water."
"2017","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: It was revealed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was forty-three years old, so he remained in Makkah ten years and in Madinah ten years, and he was taken in death when he was sixty-three years old."
"2018","Yahya narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prescribed this charity, such-and-such, and half a sa of wheat."
"2019","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed thirteen rakahs at night."
"2020","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Jamrah narrated to me, and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: When the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to Madinah to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: From which delegation, or he said: people. They said: Rabiah. He said: Welcome to the delegation, or he said: people, neither disgraced nor regretful. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to you from a distant land, and between us and you is this tribe of the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot come to you except in a sacred month, so inform us of a matter by which we shall enter Paradise and inform those behind us of it. And they asked him about drinks. So he commanded them with four and forbade them from four. He commanded them with faith in Allah. He said: Do you know what faith in Allah is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you give the fifth of the war booty. And he forbade them from al-dubba, gourds, al-hantam, green jars, al-naqir, hollowed stumps, and al-muzaffat, varnished vessels. He said: And perhaps he said: and al-muqayyar. He said: Memorize them and inform those behind you of them."
"2021","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, Abu Jamrah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"2022","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he finished at Badr: Go after the caravan, there is nothing short of it. So al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib called out to him: That is not right for you. He said: Why. He said: Because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, only promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"2023","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man of Bani Sulaym passed by a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, driving his sheep, and he greeted them. They said: He only greeted us to seek protection from us. So they went to him and killed him, and brought his sheep to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then the verse was revealed: O you who believe, when you go forth in the cause of Allah, verify."
"2024","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah narrated to me, from Tawus, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and asked him, and Sulayman ibn Dawud said: Shubah informed us, Abd al-Malik informed me, he said: I heard Tawus say: A man asked Ibn Abbas, the meaning, about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: Say: I ask you no reward for it except love for kinship. Said ibn Jubayr said: The kinship of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ibn Abbas said: You have hastened. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, there was no clan of Quraysh but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had kinship among them. So there was revealed: Say: I ask you no reward for it except love for kinship, except that you maintain the kinship between me and you."
"2025","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a woman of the Ansar, Ibn Abbas named her and I forgot her name: What prevented you from performing Hajj with us this year. She said: O Prophet of Allah, we only had two water-camels, so Abu so-and-so and his son, her husband and her son, rode one water-camel, and left one water-camel on which we draw water. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Ramadan comes, perform Umrah in it, for an Umrah in it equals a Hajj."
"2026","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah, from Aishah and Ibn Abbas, that Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was dead."
"2027","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Mughirah ibn al-Numan narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: People will be gathered barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. So the first to be clothed will be Ibrahim, upon him prayer and peace. Then he recited: As We began the first creation, We shall repeat it."
"2028","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the nabidh of the jar. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the nabidh of the jar and al-dubba. And he said: Whoever wishes to forbid what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden, let him forbid nabidh."
"2029","Yahya narrated to us, from Fitr, Abu al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, jogged around the House, and that it is a sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and they erred. I said: How did they speak truth and err. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did jog around the House, but it is not a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his Companions jogged while the polytheists were on Mount Quayqian, and it reached him that they were saying that they were emaciated, so he ordered them to jog to show them that they had strength."
"2030","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, and Waki said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, he said: I heard Abu Salih narrating, after he grew old, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed women who visit graves and those who take mosques and lamps over them."
"2031","Yahya narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me that Umar ibn Mutib informed him that Abu Hasan, freed slave of Abu Nawfal, informed him that he sought a fatwa from Ibn Abbas about a slave under whom is a slave-woman, and he divorced her twice, then both were freed, is it right for him to propose to her. He said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged so."
"2032","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, and Muhammad ibn Jafar, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about one who comes to his wife while she is menstruating: He gives in charity a dinar or half a dinar. And Abd al-Rahman and Bahz did not raise it as marfu."
"2033","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the khutbah is like the example of the donkey carrying books, and the one who says to him: Be quiet, has no Jumuah."
"2034","Ibn Numayr narrated to me, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: If only people would reduce from the third to the quarter, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The third is much."
"2035","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, that a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: Ten were revealed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Makkah and ten in Madinah. He said: Who says that. There were revealed upon him in Makkah ten and five and sixty and more."
"2036","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Fudayl, meaning Ibn Ghazwan, narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the Farewell Hajj: O people, what day is this. They said: This is a sacred day. He said: What land is this. They said: A sacred land. He said: What month is this. They said: A sacred month. He said: Your wealth and your blood and your honor are sacred to you, like the sacredness of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Then he repeated it many times. Then he raised his head to the sky and said: O Allah, have I conveyed, many times. Ibn Abbas says: By Allah, it is indeed a bequest to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. Then he said: Let the witness convey to the absent. Do not return after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others."
"2037","He said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Muslim al-Tahhan al-Saghir narrated to us, he said: I heard Ikrimah raising the hadith, as I see, to Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever leaves snakes out of fear of seeking them out is not from us. We have not made peace with them since we fought them."
"2038","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yasar informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in Fajr, in the first rakah: We believe in Allah and what was sent down to us and what was sent down to Ibrahim, to the end of the verse, and in the second rakah: We believe in Allah and bear witness that we are Muslims."
"2039","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Kinanah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out humbled, supplicating, modest, lowly, walking deliberately, and prayed two rakahs with the people as one prays in Eid, and he did not deliver a khutbah like this khutbah of yours."
"2040","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left Makkah, Ali left with the daughter of Hamzah, then Ali and Jafar and Zayd disputed about her before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ali said: The daughter of my uncle, and I brought her out. Jafar said: The daughter of my uncle, and her maternal aunt is with me. Zayd said: The daughter of my brother, and Zayd had been made a brother to Hamzah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had made brotherhood between them. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Zayd: You are my freed slave and hers. And he said to Ali: You are my brother and my companion. And he said to Jafar: You resemble my creation and my character. And she was given to her maternal aunt."
"2041","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Walah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about selling wine. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a friend of Thaqif or of Daws, and he met him in Makkah in the year of the Conquest with a rawhide of wine as a gift to him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu so-and-so, do you not know that Allah has forbidden it. So the man turned to his slave-boy and said: Go and sell it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu so-and-so, what did you order him. He said: I ordered him to sell it. He said: The One who forbade its drinking has forbidden its selling. So he ordered that it be poured out in al-Batha."
"2042","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to present the Book to Jibril, upon him peace, in every Ramadan. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rose in the morning after the night in which he presents what he presents, he rose in the morning more generous than the sent wind, not asked about anything but he gave it. When it was the month after which he died, he presented to him twice."
"2043","Yala narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from his father, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Jibril: What prevents you from visiting us more than you visit us. He said: Then there was revealed: And we descend not except by the order of your Lord, to the end of the verse."
"2044","Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: We were present with Ibn Abbas at the funeral of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Sarif. He said: Ibn Abbas said: This is Maymunah. When you lift her bier, do not shake it and do not jolt it, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had nine wives, and he used to divide his time among eight, and one he did not use to divide for. Ata said: The one he did not use to divide for was Safiyyah."
"2045","Yala narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, from Said, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The most frequent of what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, the two rakahs before Fajr, were: We believe in Allah and what was sent down to us and what was sent down to Ibrahim and Ismail, to the end of the verse, and the other: We believe in Allah and bear witness that we are Muslims."
"2046","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: I asked Said ibn Jubayr about fasting Rajab, what do you think of it. He said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast until we would say: He will not break his fast, and break his fast until we would say: He will not fast."
"2047","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Uthman, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of your kohl is ithmid, it clears the sight and grows the hair."
"2048","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas met me and said: Have you married. I said: No. He said: Marry. Then he met me after that and said: Have you married. I said: No. He said: Marry, for the best of this ummah are those with most wives."
"2049","Asbat narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you send the dog and it eats from the game, do not eat, for it only caught for itself, and if you send it and it kills and does not eat, then eat, for it only caught for its owner. Abdillah said: And it was in my father's book: From Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, then my father struck it out, so Asbat said."
"2050","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Three are obligatory upon me and are voluntary for you: al-Witr, sacrifice, and the Duha prayer."
"2051","Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, poured forth from Muzdalifah before sunrise."
"2052","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek it in the last ten, in a ninth remaining, or a fifth remaining, or a seventh remaining."
"2053","Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fought a people until he called them."
"2054","Hafs narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command his daughters and his wives to go out on the two Eids."
"2055","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell ill, he ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then he felt some relief and came out. When Abu Bakr sensed him, he wanted to step back, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured to him, and sat beside Abu Bakr on his left, and began reciting from the verse where Abu Bakr had stopped."
"2056","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu al-Qasim, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned the Jamrah, the Jamrat al-Aqabah, on the Day of Sacrifice, riding."
"2057","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not blame one who fasts while traveling nor one who breaks his fast. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted while traveling and broke his fast."
"2058","Waki narrated to us, from Israil or other than him, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to a village four farsakhs away, or he said: two farsakhs, on the day of Ashura, and ordered whoever had eaten not to eat the rest of his day, and whoever had not eaten to complete his fast."
"2059","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came as a Muslim in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then his wife came as a Muslim after him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, she embraced Islam along with me, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned her to him."
"2060","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Jahdam, from Abdillah ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to complete the ablution."
"2061","Waki narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, and Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed on a mat."
"2062","Waki narrated to me, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Did you attend the Eid with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes, and were it not for my place with him I would not have attended it, due to my young age. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and prayed two rakahs near the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt, then delivered the khutbah. He did not mention an adhan nor an iqamah."
"2063","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm ibn Sukhayr, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the fear prayer at Dhu Qarad, a land of the land of Bani Sulaym. The people lined up behind him in two rows, one row facing the enemy and one row behind him. So he prayed one rakah with the row next to him, then these stepped back to the positions of those, and those to the positions of these, and he prayed another rakah with them."
"2064","Waki narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I asked Tawus about supererogatory prayer while traveling. He said: And al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq was sitting. So al-Hasan ibn Muslim said, with Tawus listening: Tawus narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prescribed the prayer of residence and travel. So as you pray before it and after it in residence, pray before it and after it in travel. Waki once said: And pray it in travel."
"2065","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was commanded with the two rakahs of Duha and with al-Witr, and they were not written as obligatory."
"2066","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
"2067","Waki narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed through Wadi Usfan on his Hajj, he said: O Abu Bakr, which valley is this. He said: Wadi Usfan. He said: Hud and Salih have passed through it, on red young camels, their halters of fiber, their waist-wrappers of aba cloaks, and their cloaks of striped wool, chanting labbayk, performing Hajj to the Ancient House."
"2068","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would have nabidh made for him on Thursday night, and he would drink it on Thursday and on Friday. He said: And I think he said: And on Saturday. When it was late afternoon, if any of it remained, he gave it to the servants to drink or ordered that it be poured out."
"2069","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever speaks about the Quran without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2070","Waki narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from Adam ibn Sulayman, freed slave of Khalid ibn Khalid, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When this verse was revealed: Whether you disclose what is in yourselves or hide it, Allah will reckon you for it, something entered their hearts the like of which had never entered their hearts. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: We hear and we obey and we submit. So Allah cast faith into their hearts. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and the believers, all believe in Allah and His angels and His books and His messengers, we make no distinction between any of His messengers, and they said: We hear and we obey, Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return. Allah burdens no soul except its capacity, for it what it earned and against it what it acquired. Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err. Our Lord, and do not lay upon us a burden as You laid upon those before us. Our Lord, and do not burden us with what we have no strength for. Pardon us and forgive us and have mercy on us. You are our Protector, so aid us against the disbelieving people. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Adam is the father of Yahya ibn Adam."
"2071","Waki narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq al-Makki narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Sayfi, from Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sent Muadh ibn Jabal to Yemen, said: You are coming to a people of the People of the Book. Invite them to testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. If they obey you in that, inform them that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has prescribed upon them five prayers in every day and night. If they obey in that, inform them that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has prescribed upon them a charity on their wealth, taken from their rich and returned to their poor. If they obey you in that, beware of the precious of their wealth, and fear the supplication of the oppressed, for there is no veil between it and Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"2072","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution once each."
"2073","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Shubah, freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"2074","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people wearing a greasy headband."
"2075","Waki narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from his mother Fatimah bint Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, and Safwan, Abdillah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from his mother Fatimah bint Husayn, that she heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not keep looking at lepers."
"2076","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I wish people would reduce from the third to the quarter in bequests, because the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The third is much, or large."
"2077","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Amir ibn Wathilah, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, jogged, and that it is a sunnah. He said: My people spoke truth and erred. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did jog, but it is not a sunnah. He came while the polytheists were on Mount Quayqian, and they spoke of him and his Companions being emaciated, strained and in hardship, so he ordered them and they jogged around the House, to show them that no hardship had befallen them."
"2078","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Dharr narrated to us, from his father, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Jibril, upon him peace: Will you not visit us more than you visit us. Then there was revealed: And we descend not except by the order of your Lord, to Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us, to the end of the verse."
"2079","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gifted among his sacrificial camels a camel that had belonged to Abu Jahl, its nose-ring of silver."
"2080","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought cheese. He said: His Companions began beating it with sticks. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Put down the knife, mention the name of Allah, and eat."
"2081","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Jafar and Ata, they said: The sacrifice is a sunnah. And Ikrimah said, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was commanded with sacrifice and al-Witr, and they were not written as obligatory."
"2082","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan and Misar narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us forward, the young children of Bani Abd al-Muttalib, on our donkeys, from Jam. Sufyan said: At night. He began patting our thighs and saying: My little sons, do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises. And Sufyan added: Ibn Abbas said: I do not think anyone with sense stones until the sun rises."
"2083","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at night, relieved himself, then washed his face and his hands, then came and slept."
"2084","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slept until he snored, then stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
"2085","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, from al-Hasan, meaning al-Urani, he said: Ibn Abbas said: We do not know whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in Zuhr and Asr, but we recite."
"2086","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Najih narrated to us, he heard it from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women."
"2087","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: We used to sharecrop and saw no harm in that, until Rafi ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. Amr said: I mentioned it to Tawus. Tawus said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only said: One of you granting his brother the land is better for him than taking a fixed rent for it."
"2088","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, what about our brothers who died while drinking it. Then there was revealed: No blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, to the end of the verse."
"2089","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us forward, the young children of Bani Abd al-Muttalib, from Jam at night, on our donkeys. He began patting our thighs and saying: My little sons, do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises."
"2090","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you have stoned the Jamrah, all things have become lawful to you except women. A man said: And perfume. Ibn Abbas said: As for me, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, anointing his head with musk, is that perfume or not."
"2091","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders."
"2092","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Jahdam, from Abdillah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade breeding a donkey upon a horse."
"2093","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A caravan came to Madinah, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought from it and profited awaqi of silver, and divided it among the widows of Bani Abd al-Muttalib. And he said: I do not buy anything for which I do not have its price."
"2094","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the dowry of the prostitute, the price of the dog, and the price of wine."
"2095","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, then two slave-girls of Bani Abd al-Muttalib came until they took hold of his knees, so he separated between them."
"2096","Waki narrated to us, and Ibn Jafar, the meaning, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Numan, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us with an admonition and said: You will be gathered to Allah, Mighty, barefoot, naked, uncircumcised, As We began the first creation, We shall repeat it, a promise upon Us, indeed We shall do it. The first of creation to be clothed will be Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. He said: Then a group of you will be taken to the left. Ibn Jafar said: And men of my ummah will be brought and taken to the left, so I shall say: O Lord, my companions. It will be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you. They kept turning back on their heels since you left them. So I shall say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them while I remained among them, the verse, to: Indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise."
"2097","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Dharr ibn Abdillah al-Hamdani, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I speak to myself of a thing, to fall from the sky is dearer to me than to speak of it. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, praise be to Allah who reduced his plot to whispering."
"2098","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you differ about the road, make it seven cubits, and whoever builds a building, let him support it on his neighbor's wall."
"2099","Waki narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he poured forth from Arafah, a people hastened. He said: Proceed calmly and keep together. Righteousness is not in urging horses nor mounts. He said: I never saw a hand raised, galloping, until we came to Jam."
"2100","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Water, nothing makes it impure."
"2101","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Simak ibn Harb from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that a woman among the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bathed from major impurity, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bathed or performed ablution from her leftover water."
"2102","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Simak from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that one of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bathed from major impurity, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution with its leftover water, so she mentioned that to him, and he said: Water, nothing makes it impure."
"2103","Amr ibn Muhammad Abu Said al-Anqazi narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Imran from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept away from his wives for a month, then when twenty-nine days had passed Jibril came to him and said: Your oath has been fulfilled, and the month is complete."
"2104","Waki narrated to us from Fitr, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Fitr narrated to us from Shurahbil Abu Sad from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever has two sisters and treats them well as long as they are with him will enter Paradise with them. And Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Two daughters come under his care and he treats them well as long as they are with him, except that Allah the Exalted will admit him to Paradise."
"2105","Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Abi Najih from his father from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fought any people without first calling them."
"2106","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Abbas from Abdullah ibn Umayr, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If I live - Rawh said: If I am safe - until next year, I will surely fast the ninth, meaning Ashura."
"2107","Yazid narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which religions are most beloved to Allah? He said: The upright, tolerant Hanifiyyah."
"2108","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, and Ibn Jafar said: Hisham narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while in ihram, a cupping on his head. Yazid said: Because of an ailment he had."
"2109","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died while his armor was mortgaged with a Jewish man for thirty sa of barley which he had taken as provision for his family."
"2110","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, and Ibn Jafar said: Hisham narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sent, or the Quran was revealed to him, when he was forty years old, then he stayed in Mecca thirteen years and in Medina ten years. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died when he was sixty-three years old."
"2111","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to free any slaves who came to him before their masters if they embraced Islam, and he freed two men on the day of Taif."
"2112","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Mansur from al-Minhal from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek protection for Hasan and Husayn, saying: I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and poisonous pest and from every envious eye. And he used to say: Ibrahim my father used to seek protection with them for Ismail and Ishaq."
"2113","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man saw a dream and came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I saw as if a canopy was dripping honey and ghee, and as if the people were taking from it, some taking much and some taking little and some in between, and as if a rope was connected to the sky - and Yazid once said: As if a rope was let down from the sky - then you came and took hold of it and rose, so Allah raised you. Then a man came after you and took hold of it and rose, so Allah raised him. Then a man came after you both and took hold of it and rose, so Allah raised him. Then a man came after you all and took hold of it, but it was cut off with him, then it was joined for him, so he rose and Allah raised him. Abu Bakr said: Permit me, O Messenger of Allah, to interpret it for him, so he permitted him. He said: As for the canopy, it is Islam, and as for the honey and ghee, they are the sweetness of the Quran, some taking much and some taking little and some in between. As for the rope, it is what you are upon; you rise and Allah raises you. Then there will be after you a man upon your path, so he will rise and Allah will raise him. Then there will be after you both a man who follows your way, so he will rise and Allah will raise him. Then there will be after you all a man with whom it will be cut off, then it will be joined for him, so he will rise and Allah will raise him. He said: Did I get it right, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You got part right and part wrong. He said: I swear, O Messenger of Allah, you must tell me. He said: Do not swear."
"2114","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from Ibn Abbas that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the same meaning."
"2115","Yazid narrated to us, Shuba informed us, and Muhammad said: Shuba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: This is an Umrah which we have enjoyed, so whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram completely, for Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"2116","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us from Said ibn Khalid from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Dhuayb from Ata ibn Yasar from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to them while they were sitting and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people in rank? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the rein of his horse in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed. Shall I then tell you of the one next to him? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving zakat, and keeping away from the evils of people. Shall I then tell you of the worst of people in rank? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The one who is asked by Allah and does not give for His sake."
"2117","Yazid narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam informed us from Amr ibn Murra from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from his brother from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the skins of dead animals, he said: Its tanning has removed its filth, or its impurity."
"2118","Yazid narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam informed us from Amr ibn Murra from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from his brother from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he circumambulated the House on his she-camel, touching the Stone with his cane, and between al-Safa and al-Marwa. And Yazid once said: On his mount, touching the Stone."
"2119","Yazid narrated to us, Husayn ibn Dhakwan informed us from Amr ibn Shuayb from Tawus that Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas attributed it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift and then take it back, except a father regarding what he gives his child. And the likeness of one who gives a gift and takes it back is like the dog which ate until it was full, then vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"2120","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us from Amr ibn Shuayb from Tawus from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said, and he mentioned the same."
"2121","Yazid narrated to me, Said informed us from Qatada from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded one who approaches his wife while she is menstruating to give a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"2122","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us from Said from Qatada from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the same, and Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya narrated it the same with its chain."
"2123","Yazid narrated to me, Hisham informed us from Yahya from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed effeminate men and masculinized women, and said: Expel them from your houses. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, expelled so-and-so, and Umar expelled so-and-so."
"2124","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Awana informed us, Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas: Allah the Mighty and Majestic obligated prayer through the tongue of your Prophet upon the resident four, upon the traveler two, and upon the fearful one."
"2125","Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to me, Sharik ibn Abdullah informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Tamimi from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was commanded with the siwak until I thought, or supposed, that Quran would be revealed about it."
"2126","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, Ata narrated to us from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the Kaaba while it had six pillars, so he stood at each pillar and did not pray."
"2127","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Ali ibn Zayd from Yusuf ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Uthman ibn Mazun died, a woman said: Congratulations to you, Paradise, Uthman ibn Mazun. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at her with an angry look and said: What makes you know? She said: O Messenger of Allah, your horseman and your companion. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, yet I do not know what will be done with me. So the people became anxious about Uthman. Then when Zaynab the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Join our righteous good predecessor Uthman ibn Mazun. So the women wept, and Umar began beating them with his whip. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took his hand and said: Gently, O Umar. Then he said: Weep, but beware of the croaking of Satan. Then he said: Whatever comes from the eye and the heart is from Allah the Mighty and Majestic and from mercy, and whatever comes from the hand and the tongue is from Satan."
"2128","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed for the people of Medina Dhu al-Hulayfa, for the people of Sham al-Juhfa, for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, and for the people of Najd Qarn, and said: They are times for their people and for others who pass by them intending Hajj and Umrah. Whoever lives beyond the miqat, his entering ihram is from where he starts out, and likewise even the people of Mecca enter ihram from where they start out."
"2129","Yazid narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us from Yala ibn Hakim from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Maiz ibn Malik when he came to him and confessed adultery before him: Perhaps you kissed or touched? He said: No. He said: Did you have intercourse with her? He said: Yes. So he ordered him stoned."
"2130","Yazid narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum Abu Amir narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka from Ibn Abbas, he said: The dawn prayer was established, then a man stood praying the two rakahs, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pulled his garment and said: Do you pray Fajr as four?"
"2131","Yazid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur informed us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, he said: When those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses, so flog them eighty lashes and never accept their testimony was revealed, Sad ibn Ubada, who was the chief of the Ansar, said: Was it revealed like this, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O company of Ansar, do you not hear what your chief says? They said: O Messenger of Allah, do not blame him, for he is a jealous man. By Allah, he never married any woman except a virgin, and he never divorced any of his wives so that any man among us would dare to marry her, because of his intense jealousy. So Sad said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I know it is true and from Allah the Exalted, but I am amazed that if I found a wicked woman with a man lying with her, I would have no right to disturb him or move him until I bring four witnesses. By Allah, I would not bring them until he had fulfilled his need. He said: They had only waited a short while until Hilal ibn Umayya came, and he was one of the three whose repentance was accepted. He came from his land in the evening and found a man with his wife, so he saw with his eyes and heard with his ears, and he did not disturb him until morning. Then he went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to my wife in the evening and found a man with her, and I saw with my eyes and heard with my ears. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disliked what he brought and it weighed heavily on him. And the Ansar gathered and said: We have been afflicted with what Sad ibn Ubada said. Now the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will strike Hilal ibn Umayya and nullify his testimony among the Muslims. So Hilal said: By Allah, I hope Allah will make for me a way out of it. Then Hilal said: O Messenger of Allah, I see how heavily what I brought weighs upon you, and Allah knows I am truthful. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was about to order him struck when Allah sent down revelation upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And when revelation came down upon him they recognized it by the trembling of his skin, so they held back from him until he finished the revelation. Then those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves, the testimony of one of them was revealed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was relieved and said: Rejoice, O Hilal, for Allah has made for you relief and a way out. So Hilal said: I had hoped for that from my Lord the Mighty and Majestic. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Send for her. So they sent for her and she came. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited it to them both, and reminded them, and told them that the punishment of the Hereafter is more severe than the punishment of this world. So Hilal said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I have told the truth about her. And she said: He lied. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Carry out mutual cursing between them. So it was said to Hilal: Bear witness. So he bore four testimonies by Allah that he was among the truthful. Then when it was the fifth, it was said: O Hilal, fear Allah, for the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter, and this is the decisive one which makes punishment due upon you. He said: By Allah, Allah will not punish me for it just as He did not have me flogged for it. So in the fifth he testified that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was among the liars. Then it was said to her: Bear witness, four testimonies by Allah that he is among the liars. Then when it was the fifth, it was said to her: Fear Allah, for the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter, and this is the decisive one which makes punishment due upon you. So she hesitated for a moment, then said: By Allah, I will not disgrace my people. So in the fifth she testified that the anger of Allah be upon her if he was among the truthful. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, separated them, and judged that her child is not attributed to a father, and she is not to be accused because of him nor her child accused, and whoever accuses her or accuses her child is subject to the hadd. And he judged that she has no lodging from him nor provision, because they separate without divorce and without her husband having died. And he said: If she gives birth to him small, light-skinned, thin in the legs, then he is for Hilal, and if she gives birth to him dark, curly, bulky, thick in the legs, full in the buttocks, then he is for the one she was accused with. So she gave birth to him dark, curly, bulky, thick in the legs, full in the buttocks. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not for the oaths, there would have been a different matter between me and her. Ikrimah said: Afterwards he became a leader over Egypt, and he was attributed to his mother and not attributed to his father."
"2132","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Sallam from al-Hakam ibn Mina from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas that they both testified against the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said while upon the sticks of the minbar: Peoples must stop neglecting the Friday prayers, or Allah the Mighty and Majestic will surely seal their hearts and they will surely be written among the heedless."
"2133","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Farqad al-Sabakhi from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that a woman brought her child to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has madness, and it seizes him at our meals and spoils our food for us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped his chest and supplicated for him, then he retched, and there came out of his mouth something like a black pup, then he was relieved."
"2134","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam informed us, Qatada narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that Uqba ibn Amir asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: His sister vowed to walk to the House, and he complained to him of her weakness. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is free of need of your sister's vow, so let her ride and offer a she-camel."
"2135","Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, Hajib ibn Umar narrated to us, my uncle al-Hakam ibn al-Araj narrated to me, he said: I came to Ibn Abbas while he was reclining near Zamzam, so I sat with him, and he was an excellent companion. I said: Tell me about the day of Ashura. He said: About which matter of it do you ask? I said: About its fasting. He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram, count, then when you wake on the ninth, wake fasting from it. I said: Did Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fast it so? He said: Yes."
"2136","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth, I heard Tawus narrating from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Teach, make easy, do not make difficult, and when one of you becomes angry, let him be silent."
"2137","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Yazid Abu Khalid, he said: I heard al-Minhal ibn Amr narrating from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no Muslim servant who visits a sick person whose time has not come and says seven times: I ask Allah the Great, Lord of the Great Throne, to heal you, except that he is cured."
"2138","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Ibn Abbas, he said - Abu Muawiya thought he raised it - he said: Whoever visits a sick person and says: I ask Allah the Great, Lord of the Great Throne, to heal you, seven times, Allah will heal him if his time has been delayed, meaning in his lifespan. And Yazid narrated to me without doubting its being raised, and he agreed on the chain."
"2139","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us from Qatada from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that Uqba ibn Amir came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that his sister vowed to walk to the House. He said: Order your sister to ride and to offer a she-camel."
"2140","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas that a woman vowed to perform Hajj but died, so her brother came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about that. He said: Tell me, if your sister had a debt, would you pay it? He said: Yes. He said: Then pay Allah the Mighty and Majestic, for He is most deserving of fulfillment."
"2141","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Shuba narrated to us, Rawh said: I heard Muslim al-Qurri, Muhammad said: From Muslim al-Qurri, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for Umrah, and his companions entered ihram for Hajj. Rawh said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions entered ihram for Hajj, so whoever did not have a sacrificial animal with him exited ihram, and among those who did not have a sacrificial animal were Talha and another man, so they both exited ihram."
"2142","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, I heard Yahya ibn al-Mujabbir al-Taymi narrating from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Ibn Abbas that a man came to him and said: Tell me about a man who killed a man deliberately. He said: His recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him and curses him and has prepared for him a great punishment. He said: It was revealed among the last revealed, nothing abrogated it until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, and no revelation came down after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Tell me, if he repents and believes and does righteous deeds then is guided? He said: And how can he attain repentance, when I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: May his mother lose him, a man who killed a man deliberately will come on the Day of Resurrection holding his killer by his right or his left and holding his head by his right or his left, with his jugular veins gushing blood before the Throne, saying: O Lord, ask Your servant why he killed me."
"2143","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Yahya Abu Umar, he said: Nabidh was mentioned before Ibn Abbas, so he said: Nabidh used to be made for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a waterskin. Shuba said: Like Monday night, then he would drink it Monday and Tuesday until Asr, then if anything remained he would give it to the servants or pour it out. Shuba said: And I think he only said: And Wednesday until Asr, then if anything remained he would give it to the servants or pour it out."
"2144","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit and Ata ibn al-Saib from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, he said: One of them raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Jibril used to stuff mud into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing he would say: There is no god but Allah."
"2145","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning advance payment for habal al-habala: It is usury."
"2146","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Habib, meaning Ibn al-Shahid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr and Ibn Abbas, and Ibn al-Zubayr said to Ibn Abbas: Do you remember when we met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he had come from a journey? He said: Yes. So he carried me and so-and-so, a boy from Banu Hashim, and left you."
"2147","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man will enter upon you looking with the eye of Satan, or with the two eyes of Satan. He said: Then a blue-eyed man entered and said: O Muhammad, for what did you revile me, or insult me, or something like this. He said: And he began swearing. He said: Then this verse in al-Mujadila was revealed: And they swear to a lie while they know, and the other verse."
"2148","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning the Dajjal: One-eyed, fair-complexioned, glowing, as if his head were a snake, most resembling Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan. So if the perishing perish, your Lord the Exalted is not one-eyed. Shuba said: So I narrated it to Qatada, and he narrated to me something like this."
"2149","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me from Qatada from Ikrimah from Abdullah ibn Abbas that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I am an old, ill man, standing is hard for me, so command me with a night through which Allah may grant me success in Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Upon you is the seventh."
"2150","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Abu Hamzah, I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was playing with the boys, so I hid from him behind a door. Then he called me, patted me once, then sent me to Muawiya."
"2151","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to me, Shuba narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast until we would say he does not intend to break fast, and break fast until we would say he does not intend to fast. And he did not fast any month consecutively except Ramadan since he came to Medina."
"2152","Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for Hajj, then when he arrived he circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa, and did not shorten nor exit ihram because of the sacrificial animal. And he ordered whoever had not driven the sacrificial animal to circumambulate, to run, and to shorten or shave, then exit ihram."
"2153","Hushaym narrated to us, Jabir al-Jufi informed us, Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a pot, took from it a bone and a shoulder, ate it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"2154","Hushaym said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us from Dawud ibn Ali from his father from his grandfather Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fast the day of Ashura and differ from the Jews in it; fast a day before it or a day after it."
"2155","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Jabir from al-Shabi from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was cupped, was cupped in the two jugular veins. He said: So he called a boy of Banu Bayada, who cupped him, and he gave the cupper his wage a mudd and a half. He said: And he spoke to his masters, so they reduced half a mudd from him, while two mudds were due upon him."
"2156","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Jabir, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrating from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, established prayer in travel as two rakahs, and it is complete, and witr in travel is sunnah."
"2157","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Jabir from Ammar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even like the nesting place of a sandgrouse for its eggs, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"2158","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Jamra al-Dubai, he said: I performed tamattu, then people forbade me that, so I came to Ibn Abbas and asked him about that, and he ordered me with it. He said: Then I went to the House and slept, then a visitor came to me in my sleep and said: An accepted Umrah and a righteous Hajj. He said: So I came to Ibn Abbas and told him what I saw, so he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And he said concerning the sacrificial animal: A camel, a cow, a sheep, or a share in blood. Abdullah said: Shuba narrated as musnad from Abu Jamra only one, and Abu Jamra is more trustworthy than Abu Hamzah."
"2159","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Safar from Said ibn Shufayy from Ibn Abbas, he said: The people began asking him about prayer in travel, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he left his family, prayed only two rakahs until he returned to his family."
"2160","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Said ibn Shufayy, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas, and he mentioned the hadith."
"2161","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatada from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the tied animal, the jallala, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"2162","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us from al-Nadr ibn Anas, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas while he was giving fatwa to the people, not attributing anything of his fatwa to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until a man from the people of Iraq came to him and said: I am a man from the people of Iraq, and I make these images. So Ibn Abbas said to him: Come near - either twice or thrice - so he came near. So Ibn Abbas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever makes an image in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the spirit into it, and he will not breathe."
"2163","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Malik from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The previously married woman is more entitled to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is asked permission concerning herself, and her permission is her silence."
"2164","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Makhrama ibn Sulayman from Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, that Abdullah ibn Abbas told him that he spent the night at Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who was his maternal aunt. He said: So I lay across the pillow, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his family lay along it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slept until when it was midnight, or shortly before or after, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke up and sat wiping sleep from his face with his hand. Then he read the ten verses, the endings of Sura Al Imran. Then he stood to a hanging waterskin and performed ablution from it, perfecting his ablution. Then he stood praying. Ibn Abbas said: So I stood and did the same as he did, then I went and stood beside him. So he placed his hand upon my head and took my right ear and twisted it. Then he prayed two rakahs, then two rakahs, then two rakahs, then two rakahs, then two rakahs, then two rakahs, then performed witr. Then he lay down until the muezzin came to him, so he stood and prayed two light rakahs, then went out and prayed Fajr."
"2165","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a dream at midday, disheveled and dusty, with a bottle in which there was blood which he was collecting, or tracking something in it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: The blood of Husayn and his companions; I have continued tracking it since today. Ammar said: So we remembered that day and found he had been killed that day."
"2166","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Imran Abu al-Hakam from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Ask your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold for us, and we will believe in you. He said: And will you do so? They said: Yes. He said: So he supplicated, and Jibril came to him and said: Your Lord the Mighty and Majestic sends peace upon you and says: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold for them, then whoever disbelieves after that among them, I will punish him a punishment with which I punish no one among the worlds. And if you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance and mercy. He said: Rather, the door of repentance and mercy."
"2167","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Qatada, he said: I heard Abu al-Aliya saying: The cousin of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, meaning Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one should say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, and he attributed him to his father."
"2168","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki from Tawus al-Yamani from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach them the supplication as he used to teach them the sura of the Quran, saying: Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death."
"2169","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us from Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, from Ibrahim from Ata from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with the people on Fitr day two rakahs without adhan or iqama, then delivered the sermon after prayer. Then he took Bilal by the hand and went to the women and addressed them. Then after he turned away from them, he ordered Bilal to go to them and command them to give charity."
"2170","My father Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal narrated to me from his book, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Tariq from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, You made the early ones of Quraysh taste punishment, so make the later ones taste bounty."
"2171","Muhammad ibn Rabia narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn Abbas, he said: I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and all of them prayed before the sermon without adhan or iqama."
"2172","Muhammad ibn Rabia narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata from Jabir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the same."
"2173","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the Eid then delivered the sermon, and Abu Bakr prayed then delivered the sermon, and Umar then delivered the sermon, and Uthman then delivered the sermon, without adhan or iqama."
"2174","Al-Qasim ibn Malik Abu Jafar narrated to us from Hanzala al-Sadusi from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the Eid two rakahs, reciting in them only the Mother of the Book, adding nothing to it."
"2175","Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, al-Hakam, meaning Ibn Aban, narrated to us, he said: I heard Ikrimah saying: Ibn Abbas said: A short spear was planted before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Arafat, so he prayed toward it while the donkey passed beyond the spear."
"2176","Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, besieged the people of Taif, then two slaves came out to him and he freed them, one of them Abu Bakra. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to free the slaves when they came out to him."
"2177","Al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani Abu Jafar narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Aidh from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic obligated prayer through the tongue of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in residence four, in travel two, and in fear one."
"2178","Ammar ibn Muhammad, the nephew of Sufyan al-Thawri, narrated to us from Mansur from Salim from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is one of you unable, when he comes to his wife, to say: In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep me away from Satan and keep Satan away from what You provide us? Then if Allah decrees a child between them from that, Satan will never harm him."
"2179","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from Ata from Said, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: O Said, do you have a wife? He said: I said: No. He said: When you return, marry. He said: So I returned to him, and he said: O Said, have you married? He said: I said: No. He said: Marry, for the best of this ummah are those with the most wives."
"2180","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Rahabi narrated to us from Ikrimah, Ibn Abbas told us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bathed from major impurity, then when he came out he saw a spot on his left shoulder which the water had not touched, so he took from his hair and wetted it, then went on to prayer."
"2181","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Thalaba ibn Muslim al-Khathami from Abu Kab, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Jibril has been slow in coming to you. He said: And why would he not be slow toward me while around me you do not use the siwak, nor trim your nails, nor shorten your mustaches, nor clean your knuckles."
"2182","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Abu Khalid Yazid from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever visits a sick person whose time has not come and says seven times: I ask Allah the Great, Lord of the Noble Throne, to heal him, except that he is cured."
"2183","Hashim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Asim from al-Shabi from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me near Zamzam, so he asked for water and sought drink. So I brought him a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."
"2184","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan and the nephew of Ibn Shihab both narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from Ibn Abbas - and Yaqub said: My father narrated to me from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah told me that Ibn Abbas told him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Abdullah ibn Hudhafa with his letter to Kisra. He said: So he gave it to the chief of Bahrain to deliver, the chief of Bahrain to Kisra. Yaqub said: So the chief of Bahrain delivered it to Kisra, then when he read it he tore it. Ibn Shihab said: So I thought Ibn al-Musayyab said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against them to be torn utterly."
"2185","Hashim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted on the day of the conquest of Mecca until he reached Qudayd, then he was brought a cup of milk, so he broke fast and ordered the people to break fast."
"2186","Hashim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped at al-Qaha while fasting."
"2187","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna and Yunus, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salama, narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Uqba from Kurayb, the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed a woman with a boy of hers in a litter, so she took hold of his forearm and said: O Messenger of Allah, does this one have Hajj? He said: Yes, and you have reward."
"2188","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin that Ibn Abbas told him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate shoulder meat, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"2189","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Abu al-Tayyah from Musa ibn Salama, he said: I went out with Sinan ibn Salama, and with us were two sacrificial camels, but they became exhausted on the road. So Sinan said to me: Would you like to go to Ibn Abbas? So we came to him, and Sinan asked him, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: Al-Juhani asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who did not perform Hajj. He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"2190","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wala, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, saying: We are in a land with vineyards, and most of its produce is wine. He said: A man from Daws came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a wineskin of wine which he gifted him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Do you not know that Allah has prohibited it after you? Then the owner of the wineskin turned to a man with him and ordered him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What did you order him? He said: To sell it. He said: Do you not know that the One who prohibited drinking it prohibited selling it and consuming its price? He said: Then he ordered the waterskin poured out."
"2191","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa al-Mana narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from Ibn Abbas, he said - I only know he raised it - he said: When he camped at a place and the place pleased him, he delayed Zuhr until combining Zuhr and Asr. And when he traveled and no camping place was ready for him, he delayed Zuhr until reaching the camp, then combining Zuhr and Asr. Hasan said: When he traveled, whether he camped at a place."
"2192","Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Maymun ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade every fanged beast and every clawed bird."
"2193","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Kathir ibn Shinzhir from Ata from Ibn Abbas, he said: The beginning of rushing was from the desert people. They used to stand at the edges of the people until they tied sticks, quivers, and cups, then when they dispersed those rattled and they rushed the people. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was seen with the sides of his she-camel touching its hump, while saying with his hand: O people, upon you is calm, O people, upon you is calm."
"2194","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Humayd and Ayyub from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slept until snoring was heard from him, then stood and prayed without performing ablution. So Ikrimah said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was protected."
"2195","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Ayyub - Affan said: Hammad said: Ayyub and Qays informed us - from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed Isha one night until the people slept, then woke, then slept, then woke. Qays said: So Umar ibn al-Khattab came and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he went out and prayed with them, and he did not mention that they performed ablution."
"2196","Yunus and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Kurayb ibn Abi Muslim from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the house of Maymuna bint al-Harith, then stood praying at night. He said: So I stood on his left, then he took my hand and placed me on his right. Then he prayed, then slept until he breathed heavily. Then Bilal came to him with the adhan, so he stood and prayed without performing ablution. Hasan said, meaning in his hadith: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the house of Maymuna, then when he finished his prayer he slept until he snored."
"2197","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us from Abu al-Aliya, the cousin of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Ibn Abbas, narrated to us, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw on the night I was taken Musa ibn Imran, a dark, tall, curly man as if among the men of Shanuah, and I saw Isa son of Maryam of medium build, inclining to redness and whiteness, lank-headed."
"2198","Husayn narrated to us in the Tafsir of Shayban from Qatada, he said: Abu al-Aliya narrated to us, the cousin of your Prophet Ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and he mentioned the same."
"2199","Muhammad ibn Rabia narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged concerning the son of the mulaina that he is not attributed to a father, and whoever accuses her or accuses her child will be flogged the hadd. And he judged that she has no provision nor lodging, because they separate without divorce and without her husband having died."
"2200","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Humayd from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymuna bint al-Harith while they were both in ihram."
"2201","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata al-Attar, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He should give charity of a dinar, and if he cannot find then half a dinar, meaning the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating."
"2202","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Maiz ibn Malik and said: Is what has reached me about you true? He said: And what has reached you about me? He said: It has reached me that you committed adultery with the slave girl of the family of so-and-so. He said: Yes. So he turned him away until he testified four times, then he ordered that he be stoned."
"2203","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that Jibril, peace be upon him, said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you had seen me while I was taking from the mud of the sea and stuffing it into the mouth of Pharaoh."
"2204","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with the baggage from Muzdalifa at night."
"2205","Yunus narrated from Hammad meaning Ibn Salama, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it whatever you wish."
"2206","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, Affan said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to Umar and said: A woman came to pledge allegiance to him, so I took her into the passageway and I got from her what is less than intercourse. He said: Woe to you, perhaps she is one whose husband is absent in the path of Allah. He said: Yes. He said: Go to Abu Bakr and ask him. So he went to him and asked him, and he said: Perhaps she is one whose husband is absent in the path of Allah. He said the like of what Umar said. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said the like of that to him. He said: Perhaps she is one whose husband is absent in the path of Allah. And the Quran was revealed: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night, indeed good deeds remove evil deeds, to the end of the verse. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for me in particular or for the people in general? So Umar struck his chest with his hand and said: No, nor the delight of the eye, rather for the people in general. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar has spoken the truth."
"2207","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with his companion rider Usama ibn Zayd, so we gave him to drink from this drink, and he said: You have done well, do like this."
"2208","Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, he said: I remember it only as Salim al-Aftas al-Jazari Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Healing is in three: a drink of honey, an incision of a cupping instrument, and branding with fire, and I forbid my community from branding."
"2209","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibrahim meaning Ibn Sad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, and Yaqub narrated to me: my father narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The polytheists used to part their hair, and the People of the Book used to let theirs hang down, Yaqub said: their hair, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love and like agreeing with the People of the Book, Yaqub said: in some of what he had not been commanded, Ishaq said: in what he had not been commanded concerning, so he let his forelock hang down, then he parted it afterwards."
"2210","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Khaythama narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I saw Muawiya circumambulating the House with Abdullah ibn Abbas on his left, and I was following them behind them hearing their speech, and Muawiya began touching the corner of the Stone, so Ibn Abbas said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not touch these two corners. So Muawiya would say: Leave me alone, O Ibn Abbas, for none of it is abandoned. And Ibn Abbas kept adding nothing each time he placed his hand on anything of the two corners except saying that to him."
"2211","Yunus narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umra four times: an Umra from al-Hudaybiya, the Umra of fulfillment in Dhu al-Qada the next year, the third Umra from al-Jirrana, and the fourth which was with his Hajj."
"2212","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the disbelievers, and those are the wrongdoers, and those are the defiantly disobedient. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Allah revealed it concerning the two parties of Jews, and one of them had overpowered the other in the pre-Islamic period until they agreed and settled that for every slain person killed by the mighty one from the humble one his blood money is fifty wasqs, and for every slain person killed by the humble one from the mighty one his blood money is a hundred wasqs. So they remained upon that until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, and both parties were humbled by the coming of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and on that day he had not prevailed and had not imposed upon them, while he was in a truce. Then the humble one killed a slain person from the mighty one, so the mighty one sent to the humble one: Send to us a hundred wasqs. So the humble one said: And was this ever in two clans whose religion is one and whose lineage is one and whose land is one, that the blood money of some of them is half the blood money of others? We only gave you this as oppression from you to us and out of fear of you. But now that Muhammad has come, we will not give you that. War almost flared between them, then they agreed to make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge between them. Then the mighty one mentioned and said: By Allah, Muhammad will not give you from them double what he gives them from you, and they spoke the truth, they only gave us this as oppression from us and overpowering of them. So they secretly sent to Muhammad one who would find out his opinion for them: if he gives you what you want you will make him judge, and if he does not give you you will beware and not make him judge. So they secretly sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some people of the hypocrites to find out for them the opinion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah informed His Messenger of all their affair and what they intended. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: O Messenger, let not those grieve you who hasten into disbelief from those who said we believe, to His saying: And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the defiantly disobedient. Then he said concerning them: By Allah, it was revealed, and them Allah the Mighty and Majestic meant."
"2213","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever listens to the talk of a people while they dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ear, and whoever pretends a dream will be punished until he ties a grain of barley and he is not one to tie it, and whoever makes an image will be tasked to breathe into it and he is not one to breathe."
"2214","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr ibn Ghallab informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Abdullah ibn al-Araj, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas in the house of the watering place while he was pillowed on a cloak of his. He said: So I said: O Abu Abbas, inform me about Ashura. He said: About which aspect of it? He said: I said: About its fasting. He said: When you sight Muharram, count nine, then wake on the ninth day fasting. I said: Is that how Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast it? He said: Yes."
"2215","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Stone will come on the Day of Resurrection having two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, testifying for whoever touched it in truth."
"2216","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Dawud said: Ikrima narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Some of the captives on the day of Badr had no ransom, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made their ransom that they teach the children of the Ansar writing. He said: One day a boy came weeping to his father, so he said: What is the matter with you? He said: My teacher beat me. He said: The wicked one seeks the revenge of Badr. By Allah, you will never go to him again."
"2217","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered on the day of Uhud concerning the martyrs that the iron and skins be removed from them, and said: Bury them with their blood and their clothes."
"2218","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that a man from the Ansar apostatized from Islam and joined the polytheists, so Allah the Exalted revealed: How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their belief, to the end of the verse. So his people sent it to him, and he returned repentant, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted that from him and let him go."
"2219","Ali informed us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white from your clothes, for it is among the best of your clothes, and shroud your dead in it, and among the best of your kohl is ithmid, it clears the sight and grows the hair."
"2220","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Tufayl, and Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, both from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted three circuits around the House when he reached the Yemeni corner, and walked until he came to the Stone, then he trotted, and he walked four circuits. He said: Ibn Abbas said: And it was a practice."
"2221","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Hadhdha informed us, from Baraka Abu al-Walid, Ibn Abbas informed us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque facing the chambers. He said: So he looked to the sky and laughed, then said: Allah curse the Jews, fats were forbidden to them so they sold them and ate their prices, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic, when He forbids a people to eat something, He forbids them its price."
"2222","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu al-Mualla al-Attar informed us, al-Hasan al-Urani narrated to us, he said: It was mentioned in the presence of Ibn Abbas that the dog and the donkey and the woman cut off the prayer. He said: Evil is what you have likened a Muslim woman to, a dog and a donkey. I saw myself coming on a donkey while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with the people, until when I was near him facing him I dismounted from it and left it and entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into his prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not repeat his prayer nor forbid me what I did. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with the people, then a young slave girl came slipping through the rows until she sought refuge with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not repeat his prayer nor forbid her what she did. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in a mosque, then a young goat came out from one of the chambers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and went to pass in front of him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevented it. Ibn Abbas said: Will you then not say the young goat cuts off the prayer?"
"2223","Abdullah ibn Maymun Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan meaning Abu al-Malih informed us, from Habib meaning Ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever comes as a pilgrim and circumambulates the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa, his Hajj has concluded and become an Umra. Thus is the practice of Allah the Mighty and Majestic and the practice of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2224","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sayf informed us, Qays ibn Sad al-Makki informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with one witness and an oath."
"2225","Ismail ibn Yazid al-Raqqi Abu Yazid narrated to us, Furat narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Jahl said: If I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at the Kaaba I will surely come to him until I tread upon his neck. He said: He said: If he did, the angels would have seized him openly. And if the Jews had wished for death they would have died and seen their seats in the Fire. And if those who invoke curses with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone out, they would have returned finding neither wealth nor family."
"2226","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Jahl said, and he mentioned its meaning."
"2227","Nasr ibn Bab Abu Sahl narrated to us, in Shawwal of the year one hundred eighty-one, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House while touching the Stone with his staff, then he came to the watering place after he finished, with his cousins drawing from it, and said: Hand me some. So the bucket was lifted to him and he drank. Then he said: Were it not that the people would take it as a rite and overpower you over it, I would have drawn with you. Then he went out and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwa."
"2228","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in pilgrim sanctity, so he fainted. He said: That is why cupping was disliked for the fasting person. Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed on the day of al-Taif whoever of the slaves came out to him."
"2229","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Taif: Whoever comes out to us from the slaves is free. So slaves from the slaves came out, among them Abu Bakra, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them."
"2230","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Muslims killed on the day of the Trench a man from the polytheists, so they were offered money for his corpse. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand over to them their corpse, for foul is its corpse and foul is its blood money. And he accepted nothing from them."
"2231","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the pillars at the decline of the sun or after the decline of the sun."
"2232","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The people of Badr were three hundred and thirteen men, and the Emigrants were seventy-six, and the defeat of the people of Badr was on the seventeenth gone by, on Friday, in the month of Ramadan."
"2233","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Walid meaning Ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Show tolerance, you will be shown tolerance."
"2234","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Walid meaning Ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Musab, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever increases seeking forgiveness, Allah will make for him from every worry a relief, and from every strait an exit, and will provide for him from where he does not expect."
"2235","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, Qays ibn Sad informed us, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, he said: Najda ibn Amir wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about things, and I witnessed Ibn Abbas when he read his letter and when he wrote his answer. So Ibn Abbas said: By Allah, were it not that I turn him back from an evil he would fall into, I would not have written to him, nor the delight of the eye. He said: So he wrote to him: You asked me about the share of the near relatives which Allah the Mighty and Majestic mentioned, who they are, and we used to consider the relatives of the Messenger to be them, but our people refused that to us. And he asked him about the orphan, when his orphanhood ends, and that when he reaches marriageable age and sound judgment is perceived in him, his wealth is handed to him, and his orphanhood has ended. And he asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kill any of the children of the polytheists? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not kill any of them, and you, do not kill unless you know what al-Khadir knew of the boy he killed. And he asked him about the woman and the slave, did they have a known share when they attended battle, and that they had no known share except to be gifted from the spoils of the Muslims."
"2236","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach leaning against a trunk before taking the pulpit. When he took the pulpit and moved to it, it yearned for him, so he came to it and embraced it, and it calmed. He said: And had I not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection."
"2237","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2238","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Salim Abu Jahdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: I and some youths of Quraysh entered upon Ibn Abbas. He said: So they asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: No. He said: So they said: Perhaps he used to recite to himself. He said: A scratch, this is evil. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a commanded servant, he conveyed what he was sent with, and he did not single us out apart from the people except with three: he ordered us to perfect ablution, and not to eat charity, and not to breed a donkey upon a mare."
"2239","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent some people of Banu Hashim by night. Shuba said: I think he said: their weak ones. And he ordered them not to stone the pillar until the sun rises. Shuba doubted concerning their weak ones."
"2240","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Medina Dhu al-Hulayfa, and for the people of Syria al-Juhfa, and for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam. He said: They are for them and for whoever comes upon them from other than them, from whoever intends Hajj and Umra, from where he begins, until that reaches the people of Mecca."
"2241","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat from heads while he was fasting."
"2242","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was forty years old, and he stayed in Mecca thirteen years and in Medina ten years, then he died while he was sixty-three years old."
"2243","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped with a cupping in his head while he was in pilgrim sanctity."
"2244","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a drink. He said: So I brought him a bucket of Zamzam water, and he drank standing."
"2245","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that he came to his maternal aunt Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night to a waterskin and performed ablution, then he stood and prayed. He said: And I rose and performed ablution, then I stood on his left. He said: So he took me by my hand and turned me from behind him until he set me on his right."
"2246","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I have memorized the whole practice except that I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and Asr or not, and I do not know how he used to recite this letter, and I have reached extreme old age."
"2247","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, that Ibn Abbas used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fruit is not sold until it becomes fit to eat."
"2248","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Nahik, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks refuge in Allah, grant him refuge, and whoever asks you by the Face of Allah, give him."
"2249","Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Zamaa, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"2250","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A life grant is for the one to whom it is granted, and a death grant is for the one to whom it is granted, and the one who returns in his gift is like the one who returns in his vomit."
"2251","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a life grant, it is valid for the one to whom he granted it, and whoever grants a death grant, it is valid for the one to whom he granted it, and whoever gives a gift then returns in it is like the one who returns in his vomit."
"2252","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, then the direction of prayer was turned afterwards."
"2253","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artat informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abu al-Qasim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the pillar of al-Aqaba, then slaughtered, then shaved."
"2254","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Nuwayfi, the freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, narrated to me, from Kurayb, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that Dimam ibn Thalaba, the brother of Banu Sad ibn Bakr, when he became Muslim, asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the obligations of Islam of prayer and other than it. So he enumerated to him the five prayers, adding nothing to them, then charity, then fasting Ramadan, then pilgrimage to the House, then he informed him what Allah has forbidden him. When he finished he said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I will do what you ordered me, neither adding nor decreasing. He said: Then he turned away. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the one with the two braids is truthful, he will enter Paradise."
"2255","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed over Khaybar, its land and its palms, for sharing on half."
"2256","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given five which no one before me was given, and I do not say it in pride: I was sent to every red and black, and there is none of red nor black who enters my community but is of them, and the earth has been made for me a mosque."
"2257","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz meaning al-Dabbagh narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Danaj, Ikrima the freedman of Ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurayra. He said: When he bowed and when he prostrated he said the takbir. He said: So I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: May you have no mother, is that not the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"2258","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Two young slave girls from Banu Hashim passed and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and they took hold of his knees, and he did not turn away. Ibn Abbas said: And I and a man from the Ansar passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, while we were on a donkey, so we came and entered into the prayer."
"2259","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried some young boys of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, one behind him and one in front of him."
"2260","Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"2261","Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2262","Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, Humayd ibn Ali al-Uqayli narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed when he traveled two rakahs and when he stayed four. He said: Ibn Abbas said: So whoever prays in travel four is like whoever prays in residence two. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: The prayer was shortened only once, where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs and the people prayed one rakah each."
"2263","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahia informed us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined, and the men who imitate women and the women who imitate men."
"2264","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat, the people hurried. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller to call: O people, righteousness is not in urging horses nor mounts. He said: So I never saw a raised hand running until he descended to Muzdalifa."
"2265","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Shuba, from Ibn Abbas, that Usama ibn Zayd was the companion rider of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafa. So he entered the ravine, then descended and poured the water, then performed ablution and rode, and did not pray."
"2266","Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that a woman from Khatham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling in the Farewell Hajj, with al-Fadl ibn Abbas as the companion rider of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: O Messenger of Allah, the obligation of Allah in Hajj has overtaken my father as a very old man unable to sit upright on the mount, so will it fulfill for him if I perform Hajj for him? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Yes. Then al-Fadl ibn Abbas began turning toward her, and she was a beautiful woman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took al-Fadl and turned his face to the other side."
"2267","Husayn ibn Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, Abu Kudayna narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A Jew passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting. He said: How do you say, O Abu al-Qasim, on the day Allah puts the heaven upon this, and he gestured with the forefinger, and the earth upon this, and the water upon this, and the mountains upon this, and the rest of creation upon this, all of that gesturing with his fingers? He said: So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem."
"2268","Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, Abu Kudayna narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one day with no water in the camp. So a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no water in the camp. He said: Do you have anything? He said: Yes. He said: Bring it to me. He said: So he brought him a vessel with a little water in it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his fingers in the mouth of the vessel and spread his fingers. He said: So springs burst from between his fingers, and he ordered Bilal and said: Call among the people: The blessed ablution."
"2269","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zubayr meaning Ibn Khirrit, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: Ibn Abbas addressed us one day after Asr until the sun set and the stars appeared, and the people clung calling to him: The prayer. And among the people was a man from Banu Tamim who kept saying: The prayer, the prayer. He said: So he became angry. He said: Do you teach me the practice? I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) join Zuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha. Abdullah said: So I found something of that in myself, and I met Abu Hurayra and asked him, and he agreed with him."
"2270","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: When the verse of debt came down, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first who denied was Adam, peace be upon him, or: the first of denial was Adam. Allah the Mighty and Majestic, when He created Adam, wiped his back and brought forth from him what is of his offspring until the Day of Resurrection. So He began presenting his offspring to him, and he saw among them a man shining. So he said: O Lord, who is this? He said: This is your son Dawud. He said: O Lord, how long is his age? He said: Sixty years. He said: Lord, add to his age. He said: No, except that I add to him from your age. And the age of Adam was a thousand years. So he added to him forty years. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic wrote a book upon him with that and had the angels witness over him. When Adam was dying and the angels came to him to take him, he said: There remain forty years of my age. So it was said: You gifted them to your son Dawud. He said: I did not do it. And Allah the Mighty and Majestic brought forth the book against him, and the angels testified against him."
"2271","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not recite to the jinn nor see them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with a group of his companions heading to the market of Ukaz, while the devils had been barred from the news of heaven and meteors had been sent against them. He said: So the devils returned to their people and they said: What is the matter with you? They said: We have been barred from the news of heaven and meteors have been sent against us. He said: So they said: Nothing has come between you and the news of heaven except something that has happened, so strike the easts of the earth and its wests and look what this is that has come between you and the news of heaven. He said: So they set out striking the easts of the earth and its wests seeking what this is that has come between them and the news of heaven. He said: So the group who headed toward Tihama turned back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Nakhla heading to the market of Ukaz, while he was praying with his companions the dawn prayer. He said: When they heard the Quran they listened to it and said: By Allah, this is what has come between you and the news of heaven. He said: Then there, when they returned to their people, they said: O our people, we have heard a wondrous Quran guiding to right guidance, so we have believed in it, the verse. So Allah revealed to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say, it has been revealed to me that, and only the speech of the jinn was revealed to him."
"2272","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Medina Dhu al-Hulayfa, and for the people of Syria al-Juhfa, and for the people of Najd Qarn al-Manazil, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam. They are for them and for everyone coming who comes upon them from other than them, from whoever intends Hajj and Umra. So whoever is nearer than that is from where he begins, even the people of Mecca from Mecca."
"2273","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymuna while he was in pilgrim sanctity."
"2274","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: They used to consider Umra in the months of Hajj among the vilest wickedness on earth, and they made Muharram into Safar, and they said: When the back heals and the trace fades and Safar ends, Umra becomes lawful for whoever performs Umra. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions came on the morning of the fourth chanting Hajj, he ordered them to make it an Umra, and that was grave with them. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, what release? He said: The complete release."
"2275","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to sell food until he takes full possession of it. He said: So I said to him: How is that? He said: That is dirhams for dirhams while the food is deferred."
"2276","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from Ikrima ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night praying. So I rose and performed ablution, then I stood on his left. So he pulled me and drew me and set me on his right. Then he prayed thirteen rakahs, his standing in them being equal."
"2277","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Urwa said to Ibn Abbas: How long will you mislead the people, O Ibn Abbas? He said: What is that, O Urayya? He said: You order us to perform Umra in the months of Hajj though Abu Bakr and Umar forbade it. So Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it. So Urwa said: They were more following of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and more knowledgeable of him than you."
"2278","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that Uqba ibn Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: His sister vowed to walk to the House. So he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic is in no need of the vow of your sister. Let her perform Hajj riding and let her sacrifice an animal."
"2279","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has made Mecca sacred, so it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me, and it was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day: its fresh grass is not cut, nor its trees cut, nor its game chased, nor its lost property picked up except for one who announces it. So al-Abbas said: Except idhkhir, for our craft and our graves. He said: Except idhkhir."
"2280","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Yahya, from Ibn Abbas, that two men disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the claimant for proof, and he had no proof. So he made the defendant swear, and he swore by Allah besides whom there is no god. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You did it, but you have been forgiven for your sincerely saying: There is no god but Allah."
"2281","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, al-Mughira ibn al-Numan, a shaykh from Nakh, narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with an admonition and said: O people, you will be gathered to Allah barefoot, naked, uncircumcised: As We began the first creation We will repeat it, a promise upon Us, indeed We shall do it. And the first of creation to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection is Ibrahim. And people from my community will be brought and taken to the left. So I will surely say: My companions. So it will surely be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you. So I will surely say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them while I was among them, when You took me You were the Watcher over them and You are over all things Witness, to: They are Your servants, and if You forgive them then You are the Mighty the Wise. So it will be said: These kept turning back upon their heels since you left them. Shuba said: He dictated it to Sufyan, and Sufyan dictated it to me in place."
"2282","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Mughira ibn al-Numan, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with an admonition and mentioned it."
"2283","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, he said: What you call al-Mufassal is al-Muhkam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while I was ten years old, and I had read al-Muhkam."
"2284","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artat narrated to us, Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: meaning Hajjaj, and al-Hakam narrated to me, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in two white garments and in a red cloak."
"2285","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Ibrahim brought Ismail, peace be upon them both, and Hajar, and placed them in Mecca at the site of Zamzam. Then he mentioned the hadith. Then she came from al-Marwa to Ismail while the spring had gushed, and she began scooping the spring with her hand like this until the water gathered from its side, then she took it with her cup and put it in her waterskin. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on her, had she left it it would have been a flowing spring running until the Day of Resurrection."
"2286","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to us, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate either a roasted forearm or a shoulder, then he prayed and did not perform ablution nor touch water."
"2287","Affan narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, so he ordered them and they made it an Umra. Then he said: Had I faced of my affair what I have come to know, I would have done as they did, but Umra has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. Then he interlaced his fingers one in the other. So the people were released except whoever had a sacrificial animal with him. And Ali came from Yemen, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter pilgrim sanctity? He said: I entered sanctity with what you entered sanctity with. He said: Do you have a sacrificial animal with you? He said: No. He said: Stay as you are, and you have a third of my sacrificial animal. He said: And with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were a hundred camels."
"2288","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman came with a son of hers to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine has madness, and it seizes him at our lunch and our dinner and spoils them for us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his chest and supplicated, and he vomited a vomit. Affan said: So I asked a Bedouin and he said: Part upon part. And there came out of his belly like a black puppy, and he was healed."
"2289","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked a bone from a pot, then he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"2290","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Ibn Abbas and from Ibn Umar, that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will surely cease abandoning Fridays, or Allah will surely seal upon their hearts, then they will surely be written among the heedless."
"2291","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the effeminate from among men and the masculine from among women. He said: So I said: What are the masculine from among women? He said: Those women who imitate men."
"2292","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi."
"2293","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah obligated prayer upon the tongue of your Prophet: in residence four, and in travel two, and in fear one."
"2294","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none from the children of Adam but has erred or intended a sin, except Yahya ibn Zakariya. And it is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, peace be upon him."
"2295","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, that Ibn Abbas said: I and a boy from Banu Hashim passed on a donkey, and we left it eating from greens in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not turn away. And two young slave girls came running until they took hold of the knees of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not turn away."
"2296","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Qatada informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hassan narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr at Dhu al-Hulayfa, then he called for his sacrificial camel, or he was brought his sacrificial camel, and he marked the right side of its hump, then wiped the blood from it and garlanded it with two sandals. Then he came to his mount, and when he sat upon it and it rose with him upon the desert plain, he entered pilgrim sanctity for Hajj."
"2297","Affan narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliya al-Riyahi, from the cousin of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meaning Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these supplications at distress: There is no god but Allah, the All-Knowing, the Mighty. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the noble Throne."
"2298","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, he said: I heard Abu al-Aliya, he said: I heard the cousin of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Bahz said: Shuba narrated to us, Qatada informed me, from Abu al-Aliya, he said: The cousin of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a servant, Affan said: a servant, to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, and he traced him to his father."
"2299","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed me, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, that his maternal aunt Umm Hufayd gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter and mastigures and cottage cheese. He said: So he ate from the clarified butter and from the cottage cheese, and left the mastigures out of disgust. So it was eaten upon the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and had it been forbidden it would not have been eaten upon the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Who said: Had it been forbidden? Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said it."
"2300","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, Tawus informed me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was ordered to prostrate upon seven and not to gather hair nor garment. Then he said another time: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ordered to prostrate upon seven and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2301","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that Jibril said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it whatever you wish."
"2302","Affan narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Simak informed us, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: I was visited while I was asleep in Ramadan and it was said to me: tonight is Laylat al-Qadr. He said: So I got up while drowsy and clung to one of the tent ropes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was praying. I looked into that night, and it was the night of the twenty-third."
"2303","Affan narrated to us, Thabit, meaning Ibn Yazid, narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend successive nights folded up with hunger, and his family would find no supper. He said: And most of their bread was barley bread."
"2304","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir Abu Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab narrating, from Abu Sinan, from Ibn Abbas, he said: He addressed us, meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O people, Hajj has been prescribed for you. He said: So al-Aqra ibn Habis stood and said: Every year, O Messenger of Allah? He said: If I said it, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory you would not act upon it, or you would not be able to act upon it. Whoever adds more, it is voluntary."
"2305","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf seven times and performed the brisk walking, and he only walked briskly because he loved to show the people his strength."
"2306","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abu Zubayd informed us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Mina on the day of al-Tarwiyah the Zuhr prayer."
"2307","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his brother from placing his elbow beam upon his wall."
"2308","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Ibn Hubayrah, from Maymun al-Makki, that he saw Ibn al-Zubayr Abdullah praying with them, gesturing with his hands when he stood and when he bowed and when he prostrated and when he rose for standing, then he stands and gestures with his hands. He said: So I went to Ibn Abbas and said to him: I have seen Ibn al-Zubayr pray a prayer I have never seen anyone pray, and he described to him this gesturing. He said: If you wish to look at the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then follow the prayer of Ibn al-Zubayr."
"2309","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Dawud, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh said to the Jews: Give us something to ask this man about. They said: Ask him about the Ruh. So they asked him, and there was revealed: And they ask you about the Ruh; say: The Ruh is from the command of my Lord, and you have been given of knowledge only a little. They said: We have been given much knowledge, we have been given the Torah, and whoever is given the Torah has been given much good. He said: So Allah Almighty revealed: Say: If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord, the sea would be exhausted."
"2310","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Aslami: Perhaps you kissed, or touched, or looked."
"2311","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to go out on a journey, would say: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel and the gloom of return. O Allah, fold the earth for us and ease travel for us. And when he intended to return he would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord. And when he entered upon his family he would say: Repentance, repentance, a return to our Lord, leaving no sin upon us."
"2312","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall recite the Quran peoples from my ummah who pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game."
"2313","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go out to meet caravans, and do not withhold milk in udders, and let none of you cry out against one another."
"2314","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, he said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) affirmed Umayyah in something of his poetry. He said: A man and a bull beneath his right foot, and the vulture for the other, and a lion lying in wait. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth. And he said: And the sun rises every end of night, red, its color becoming rosy in the morning; it refuses and does not rise upon us at ease except tormented, or else flogged. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"2315","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ablution upon one who sleeps prostrating until he lies down, for when he lies down his joints relax."
"2316","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that a man seized a woman, or took her captive, and she struggled with the hilt of his sword and killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her and was informed of her affair, and he forbade killing women and children."
"2317","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Mutah and appointed Zayd, then if Zayd is killed then Jafar, then if Jafar is killed then Ibn Rawahah. Ibn Rawahah stayed behind and joined the congregation with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw him and said: What kept you back? He said: I join the congregation with you. He said: A morning going forth or an evening return is better than the world and what is in it."
"2318","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not from us who has intercourse with a pregnant woman."
"2319","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: On the day of al-Khandaq a man of the polytheists was struck down, and they asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to let them take his body. He said: No, and no honor for you. They said: Then we will pay you a price for that. He said: And that is more foul and more foul."
"2320","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from him, from Sharik, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment wrapped around himself, shielding himself with its excess from the heat of the ground and its cold."
"2321","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Dawud, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Jahl passed by and said: Did I not forbid you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked him. Abu Jahl said to him: Why do you rebuke me, O Muhammad? By Allah, you know there is no man here with a larger assembly than mine. He said: So Jibril, peace be upon him, said: Then let him call his assembly. He said: So Ibn Abbas said: By Allah, if he had called his assembly, the tormenting angels would have seized him."
"2322","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon."
"2323","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from Uthman ibn Muhammad, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of you but that a companion from the devils has been assigned to him. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted."
"2324","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: On the night the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he entered Paradise and heard a movement from its side. He said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is Bilal the caller to prayer. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he came to the people: Bilal has prospered; I saw such and such for him. He said: Then Musa, peace be upon him, met him and welcomed him and said: Welcome to the unlettered Prophet. He said: And he was a dark-skinned, tall man with lank hair down to his ears or above them. He said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Musa, peace be upon him. He said: Then he went on and Isa met him and welcomed him. He said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Isa. He said: Then he went on and met a venerable, awe-inspiring elder, and he welcomed him and greeted him, and all of them greeted him. He said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is your father Ibrahim. He said: Then he looked into the Fire, and there were people eating carrion. He said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are those who eat the flesh of people. And he saw a red, blue-eyed, curly-haired, disheveled man; when you saw him he said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is the hamstringer of the she-camel. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered al-Masjid al-Aqsa, he stood praying, then turned, then turned again, and there were all the prophets praying with him. When he finished, two cups were brought, one on the right and the other on the left; in one was milk and in the other was honey. He took the milk and drank from it, and the one who had the cup with him said: You have hit upon the fitrah."
"2325","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it from him, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I stood with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer on his left, and he placed me on his right."
"2326","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sumay al-Zayyat, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, the like of that."
"2327","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am your predecessor at the Hawd; whoever comes to it prospers. And peoples will be brought and seized to the left, and I will say: O Lord. And it will be said: They kept turning back on their heels after you."
"2328","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take good omens and would not take bad omens, and the good name pleased him."
"2329","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from Uthman ibn Muhammad, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not from us who does not honor the elder and have mercy on the young and enjoin the right and forbid the wrong."
"2330","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five, all of them harmful, the pilgrim in ihram kills them, and they are killed in the Haram: the mouse, the scorpion, the snake, the vicious dog, and the crow."
"2331","He narrated to us: [source text truncated at three words; remainder missing]."
"2332","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not establish anything but that I knew it, except three; I do not know whether he used to recite in Zuhr and Asr or not, and I do not know how he used to recite, and I have reached extreme old age. Husayn said: And I forgot the third. Abdullah said: I heard all of it myself from Uthman ibn Muhammad: extreme old age."
"2333","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said, and I heard it myself from him, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Jafar ibn Iyas, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to turn al-Safa into gold for them and to remove the mountains from them so they could cultivate. It was said to him: If you wish, you may be patient with them, and if you wish, you may be given what they asked, but if they disbelieve they will be destroyed as those before them were destroyed. He said: No, rather I will be patient with them. So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: And nothing prevented Us from sending the signs except that the former peoples denied them, and We gave Thamud the she-camel as a clear sign."
"2334","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The name of Juwayriyah was Barrah, and it was as if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that, so he named her Juwayriyah, out of dislike that it be said: He came out from Barrah. He said: And he went out after he had prayed, then came to her, and she said: I have remained after you, O Messenger of Allah, laboring. He said: So he said to her: I have said after you words that if weighed would outweigh what you said: Glory be to Allah as many times as the number of what Allah created; glory be to Allah to the pleasure of Himself; glory be to Allah to the weight of His Throne; glory be to Allah to the extent of His words."
"2335","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it, and if a cloud barrier comes between you and it, then complete the number; and the month is twenty-nine, meaning that it is short."
"2336","Muawiyah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and owed a month of fasting; shall I make it up for her? He said: If your mother had a debt, would you pay it for her? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving to be paid. Sulayman said: So al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl said, while we were all sitting when Muslim narrated this hadith: We heard Mujahid mention this from Ibn Abbas."
"2337","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb informed me, Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage and took snuff."
"2338","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb informed us, Ibn Tawus informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He was asked about slaughtering and stoning and shaving and doing first and last, and he said: No harm."
"2339","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr informed us, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He was brought a roasted shoulder and ate morsels from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution on account of that."
"2340","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, that he heard his father narrating from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Health and free time are two blessings from the blessings of Allah in which many people are cheated."
"2341","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, that he narrated to him that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat from a shoulder or a foreleg, then stand and pray and not perform ablution."
"2342","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them this supplication as he taught them the surah of the Quran: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of al-Masih al-Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death."
"2343","Ismail narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it, except that he said: From the trial of al-Masih al-Dajjal."
"2344","Abd al-Wahhab said: Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at distress: There is no god but Allah, the Mighty, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, You are the Lord of the mighty Throne; there is no god but You, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth and Lord of the noble Throne."
"2345","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, meaning the like of the supplication of distress."
"2346","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Zaidah ibn Abi al-Ruqad, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when Rajab entered, would say: O Allah, bless us in Rajab and Shaban and bless us in Ramadan. And he would say: The night of Friday is radiant and its day is bright."
"2347","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, Ibn Abbas, the cousin of your Prophet, narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw on the night I was taken by night Musa ibn Imran, peace be upon him, a dark-skinned, tall, curly-headed man as if from the men of Shanua, and I saw Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, of medium build, reddish-white, lank-haired."
"2348","Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Make it an Umrah, for if I were to face again of my affair what I have left behind, I would have commanded you with it; and whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sacrificial animal with him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection, and he interlaced his fingers."
"2349","Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and camped at night, then slept and did not wake except by the sun. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan and prayed two rakahs. He said: So Ibn Abbas said: The world and what is in it would not delight me as much as it, meaning the concession."
"2350","Abidah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Madinah intending Makkah and fasted until he reached Usfan. He said: So he called for a vessel and placed it on his hand until the people looked at him, then he broke fast. He said: And Ibn Abbas used to say: Whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break fast."
"2351","Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, and he mentioned it with its isnad or its meaning."
"2352","Abidah narrated to us, Qabus narrated to me, from Abu Zabyan, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came toward them hastening. He said: Until he startled us by his haste. When he reached us he said: I came hastening to inform you of Laylat al-Qadr, but it was made forgotten between me and you. But seek it in the last ten of Ramadan."
"2353","Abidah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: This land is sacred; Allah made it sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and it is sacred, Allah having made it sacred until the Day of Resurrection. Killing in it was not permitted for anyone before me, nor is it permitted for anyone after me until the Hour comes. And it was not permitted for me in it except for an hour of the day. It is sacred, Allah Almighty having made it sacred until the Hour comes. Its thorns are not cut, its herbage is not uprooted, its game is not disturbed, and its lost property is not picked up except by one who announces it. He said: So al-Abbas said, and he was of the people of the land and knew what they indispensably needed: Except al-idhkhir, O Messenger of Allah, for they indispensably need it, for graves and houses. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except al-idhkhir."
"2354","Abidah narrated to us, he said: Waqid Abu Abdullah al-Khayyat narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Clarified butter and dried yogurt and a lizard were gifted to the Messenger of Allah, upon him be prayer and peace; he ate the clarified butter and the dried yogurt, then said of the lizard: This is something I have never eaten; whoever wishes to eat it, let him eat it. He said: So it was eaten at his table."
"2355","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Hassan, narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram, on his head, for a headache he had, or something he had, at a water called Lahy Jamal."
"2356","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mukatab is compensated according to what he has paid as the blood money of a free man, and according to what remains enslaved as the blood money of a slave."
"2357","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Husayn ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the people gathered to wash the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was in the house none but his family, his uncle al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Ali ibn Abi Talib and al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas and Qutham ibn al-Abbas and Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Harithah and Salih his freedman, when they gathered to wash him, Aws ibn Khawli al-Ansari, then one of Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj, and he was a Badri, called to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from behind the door and said to him: O Ali, I adjure you by Allah and our share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So Ali said to him: Enter. So he entered and attended the washing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but did not handle any of his washing. He said: So he leaned him against his chest, with his shirt upon him, and al-Abbas and al-Fadl and Qutham would turn him with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Usamah ibn Zayd and Salih their freedman would pour the water, and Ali kept washing him. And nothing was seen of the Messenger of Allah of what is seen of the dead, while he said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, how sweet you are alive and dead. When they finished washing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was washed with water and lote, they dried him, then there was done with him what is done with the dead, then he was wrapped in three garments, two white garments and a Hibarah cloak. Then al-Abbas called two men and said: Let one of you go to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and Abu Ubaydah used to dig the grave trench for the people of Makkah, and let the other go to Abu Talhah ibn Sahl al-Ansari, and Abu Talhah used to dig the lahd for the people of Madinah. He said: Then al-Abbas said to them when he sent them: O Allah, choose for Your Messenger. He said: So they went; the companion of Abu Ubaydah did not find Abu Ubaydah, and the companion of Abu Talhah found Abu Talhah, so he brought him, and he dug the lahd for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2358","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Khusayf ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jazari narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abbas: O Abu al-Abbas, I wonder at the disagreement of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the ihram call of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he made it obligatory. He said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about that; it was only one Hajj of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from there they disagreed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out as a pilgrim, and when he prayed in his mosque at Dhu al-Hulayfah his two rakahs, he made it obligatory in his place, and called out Hajj when he finished his two rakahs, and peoples heard that from him and preserved it from him. Then he rode, and when his she-camel rose with him he called out, and peoples perceived that from him, and that is because the people only used to come in groups, so they heard him when his she-camel rose with him calling out, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only called out when his she-camel rose with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on, and when he ascended the height of al-Bayda he called out, and peoples perceived that from him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only called out when he ascended the height of al-Bayda. By Allah, he made it obligatory in his prayer place, and called out when his she-camel rose with him, and called out when he ascended the height of al-Bayda. So whoever takes the word of Abdullah ibn Abbas should call out in his prayer place when he finishes his two rakahs."
"2359","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: A man narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted in the Farewell Hajj one hundred camels; he slaughtered thirty of them with his hand, then commanded Ali, and he slaughtered what remained of them, and said: Divide their meat and their coverings and their skins among the people, and do not give a butcher anything from them. And take for us from every camel a portion of meat, then put it in a single pot until we eat of its meat and sip of its broth. So he did."
"2360","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Kurayb the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: I said to him: O Abu al-Abbas, what do you think of your saying: No man who did not drive the sacrificial animal with him performed Hajj then circumambulated the House but that he exits into Umrah, and no pilgrim who drove the sacrificial animal with him circumambulated it but that Umrah and Hajj are combined for him, while the people do not say this? He said: Woe to you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out, and those of his companions with him mentioned nothing but Hajj. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded whoever did not have the sacrificial animal with him to circumambulate the House and exit into Umrah. A man of them would say: O Messenger of Allah, it is only Hajj. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: It is not Hajj, but it is Umrah."
"2361","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not make Aishah perform Umrah on the night of al-Hasbah except to cut off the affair of the people of polytheism, for they used to say: When the wound heals and the trace fades and Safar enters, then Umrah has become lawful for whoever performs Umrah."
"2362","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gifted the camel of Abu Jahl which he had taken as spoil on the day of Badr, with a silver nose-ring on its head, in the year of al-Hudaybiyah among his sacrificial animals. And he said in another place: To enrage thereby the polytheists."
"2363","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Bushayr ibn Yasar, the freedman of Banu Harithah, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of the Conquest in Ramadan, and fasted, and the Muslims fasted with him, until when he was at al-Kadid he called for water in a cup while upon his mount, and drank with the people looking, informing them that he had broken fast. So the Muslims broke fast."
"2364","Yaqub narrated to me, my father narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The People of the Book used to let their hair hang down, and the polytheists used to part their heads. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to agree with the People of the Book in some of what he had not been commanded about. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let his forelock hang down, then parted afterwards."
"2365","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl ibn Abbas ibn Rabiah, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman is more entitled to her affair, and the orphan girl is consulted about herself, and her permission is her silence."
"2366","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter Zaynab to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi on the first marriage, and her Islam had been six years before his Islam, and he did not renew a testimony nor a dowry."
"2367","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Talhah ibn Nafi mentioned, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man married a woman of the Ansar of Balajlan and consummated with her and spent the night with her, then in the morning said: I did not find her a virgin. He said: So their affair was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the girl and asked her, and she said: Yes, I was a virgin. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them both and they invoked mutual curses, and he gave her the dowry."
"2368","Yaqub and Sad narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the stoning of the Jewish man and the Jewish woman at the door of his mosque. When the Jewish man felt the touch of the stones, he stood over his companion and bent over her, shielding her from the touch of the stones, until they were both killed. And it was of what Allah Almighty did for His Messenger in establishing adultery against them."
"2369","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: And Ibn Shihab narrated that Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did you not make use of its hide? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only eating it is forbidden."
"2370","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: The nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud informed me that Abdullah ibn Abbas informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Qaysar calling him to Islam, and sent his letter with Dihyah al-Kalbi, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to hand it to the chief of Busra so he would hand it to Qaysar. The chief of Busra handed it over. And Qaysar, when Allah Almighty had uncovered from him the troops of Persia, walked from Hims to Iliya upon carpets spread for him. Abdullah ibn Abbas said: When the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Qaysar, he said when he read it: Seek for me one of his people whom I may ask about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Abbas said: So Abu Sufyan ibn Harb informed me that he was in al-Sham among men of Quraysh who had come as traders, and that was during the truce between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the unbelievers of Quraysh. Abu Sufyan said: So the messenger of Qaysar came to me and took me and my companions until we arrived at Iliya, and we were admitted to him, and he was sitting in his royal assembly with the crown upon him and around him the great men of Rome. He said to his interpreter: Ask them which of them is nearest in kinship to this man who claims he is a prophet. Abu Sufyan said: I am the nearest of them to him in kinship. He said: What is your kinship to him? He said: I said: He is my cousin. Abu Sufyan said: And there was not in the party that day any man of Banu Abd Manaf besides me. He said: So Qaysar said: Bring him near to me. Then he commanded my companions and they were placed behind my back at my shoulder. Then he said to his interpreter: Say to his companions: I am asking this man about the man who claims he is a prophet; if he lies, then belie him. Abu Sufyan said: By Allah, were it not for shame that day that my companions would transmit lying from me, I would have lied about him when he asked me, but I was ashamed that lying be transmitted from me, so I told the truth about him. Then he said to his interpreter: Say to him: How is the lineage of this man among you? He said: I said: He is of lineage among us. He said: Did any of you ever say this saying before him? He said: I said: No. He said: Did you accuse him of lying before he said what he said? He said: I said: No. He said: Was any of his forefathers a king? He said: I said: No. He said: Do the nobles of the people follow him or their weak? He said: I said: Rather their weak. He said: Do they increase or decrease? He said: I said: Rather they increase. He said: Does anyone apostatize in anger at his religion after entering it? He said: I said: No. He said: Does he betray? He said: I said: No, and we are now in a truce with him, and we fear that. Abu Sufyan said: And no word enabled me to insert anything by which I disparaged him except it, for I feared lying would be transmitted from me. He said: Did you fight him, or did he fight you? He said: I said: Yes. He said: How was your war and his war? He said: I said: It was alternating fortunes; he prevails over us once, and we prevail over him another time. He said: What does he command you? He said: I said: He commands us to worship Allah alone and associate nothing with Him, and forbids us what our fathers used to worship, and commands us with prayer and truthfulness and chastity and fulfilling the covenant and rendering the trust. He said: So he said to his interpreter when I said that to him: Say to him: I asked you about his lineage among you, and you claimed he is of lineage among you, and thus are messengers sent among the lineage of their people. And I asked you whether any of you ever said this saying before him, and you claimed no; and I said: Had any of you said this saying before him, I would say: A man following a saying said before him. And I asked you whether you accused him of lying before he said what he said, and you claimed no; and I have known he would not abandon lying against people and lie against Allah Almighty. And I asked you whether any of his forefathers was a king, and you claimed no; and I said: Had any of his forefathers been a king, I would say: A man seeking the kingdom of his forefathers. And I asked you whether the nobles of the people follow him or their weak, and you claimed their weak followed him, and they are the followers of messengers. And I asked you whether they increase or decrease, and you claimed they increase, and thus is faith until it is complete. And I asked you whether anyone apostatizes in anger at his religion after entering it, and you claimed no, and thus is faith when its joy mixes with hearts, none hates it. And I asked you whether he betrays, and you claimed no, and thus are messengers. And I asked you whether you fought him and he fought you, and you claimed you did, and that your war and his war alternate, you prevail over him once and he prevails over you another, and thus are messengers tried, and theirs is the outcome. And I asked you what he commands you with, and you claimed he commands you to worship Allah Almighty alone, associating nothing with Him, and forbids you what your fathers used to worship, and commands you with truthfulness and prayer and chastity and fulfilling the covenant and rendering the trust. And this is the description of a prophet. I knew he would come forth, but I did not think he was from you. If what you said about him is true, he will soon own the place of these two feet of mine. By Allah, if I hoped to reach him I would undertake meeting him, and if I were with him I would wash his feet. Abu Sufyan said: Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and commanded it be read, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muhammad, the servant of Allah and His Messenger, to Hiraql, chief of Rome. Peace upon whoever follows guidance. As for after: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit and be safe, and submit and Allah will give you your reward twice. But if you turn away, upon you is the sin of the Arisiyyin, meaning the tillers. And: O People of the Book, come to a word equal between us and you, that we worship none but Allah and associate nothing with Him, and take not one another as lords besides Allah; but if they turn away, then say: Bear witness that we are Muslims. Abu Sufyan said: When he finished his speech, the voices of those around him of the great men of Rome rose and their clamor increased, and I do not know what they said, and we were commanded and taken out. Abu Sufyan said: When I went out with my companions and was alone with them, I said to them: The affair of Ibn Abi Kabshah has become great; this king of Banu al-Asfar fears him. Abu Sufyan said: By Allah, I remained humbled, certain his affair would prevail, until Allah put Islam into my heart, though unwilling."
"2371","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud informed me that Abdullah ibn Abbas informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote, and he mentioned it."
"2372","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, and he mentioned it."
"2373","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ubaydullah said: I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas about the dream of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he mentioned. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned to me, he said: While I was asleep I saw that two bracelets of gold were placed in my hands, and I was alarmed by them and disliked them, and I was permitted, so I blew them and they flew away. I interpreted them as two liars who would come forth. Ubaydullah said: One of them is al-Ansi, whom Fayruz killed in Yemen, and the other is Musaylimah."
"2374","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik informed me that Ibn Abbas informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came out from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during his illness in which he died, and the people said: O Abu Hasan, how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wake this morning? He said: He woke, praise be to Allah, recovered. Ibn Abbas said: So Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib took his hand and said: Do you not see? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will die of this illness; I know the faces of Banu Abd al-Muttalib at death. So go with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him about whom this authority is. If it is among us, we shall know that, and if it is in other than us, we shall speak to him and he will enjoin us. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, if we ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for it and he withholds it from us, the people will never give it to us ever. By Allah, I will never ask him."
"2375","Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari narrated to them both that they heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: I heard Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam recite, and he mentioned the hadith. Muhammad said: And Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud narrated to me that Ibn Abbas narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, recited to me upon one harf, and I kept asking him for more, and I did not cease seeking increase from him and he increased me, until it reached seven ahruf."
"2376","Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud informed me that Ibn Abbas said: I came, having nearly reached puberty, riding a she-ass, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing praying for the people, meaning until I passed in front of part of the first row. Then I dismounted from it and it grazed, and I lined up with the people behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2377","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata ibn Ayyash ibn Alqamah, the brother of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas at the house of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the morrow of Friday. He said: And Maymunah had bequeathed it to him, and when he prayed Friday it was spread for him in it, then he returned to it and sat in it for the people. He said: So a man asked him, while I listened, about ablution from what fire has touched of food. He said: So Ibn Abbas raised his hand to his eyes, and his sight had been taken away, and said: May these two eyes of mine see; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution for the Zuhr prayer in one of his chambers, then Bilal called to prayer, and he rose going out. When he stood at the door of the chamber, a gift of bread and meat met him, sent to him by one of his companions. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned with those with him, and it was placed for them in the chamber. He said: So he ate, and they ate with him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose with those with him to prayer, and neither he nor any of those with him touched water. He said: Then he prayed with them. And Ibn Abbas only understood of the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the last of it."
"2378","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated upon his camel, and whenever he came upon the Corner he gestured to it and said takbir."
"2379","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while I was circumcised."
"2380","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Nuwayfi narrated to me, from Kurayb the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Banu Sad ibn Bakr sent Dimam ibn Thalabah as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He arrived and made his camel kneel at the door of the mosque, then tied it, then entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his companions. Dimam was a hardy, hairy man with two braids. He came until he stood over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his companions and said: Which of you is Ibn Abd al-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am Ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Muhammad said: Yes. He said: Ibn Abd al-Muttalib, I am asking you and will be stern in questioning, so do not take it to heart. He said: I will not take it to heart; ask whatever occurs to you. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah send you to us as a messenger? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah command you to command us to worship Him alone, associating nothing with Him, and to cast off these rivals our fathers used to worship with Him? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah command you that we pray these five prayers? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: Then he kept mentioning the obligations of Islam, obligation by obligation, zakah and fasting and Hajj and all the laws of Islam, adjuring him at every obligation as he adjured him at the one before it, until when he finished he said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that our master Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and I shall perform these obligations and avoid what you forbade me, then neither add nor lessen. He said: Then he turned back to his camel. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he turned away: If the one with the two braids tells the truth, he will enter Paradise. He said: So he came to his camel and untied its hobble, then went out until he arrived to his people, and they gathered to him. The first thing he spoke was to say: Evil are al-Lat and al-Uzza. They said: Stop, O Dimam; fear leprosy and white leprosy; fear madness. He said: Woe to you, by Allah they neither harm nor benefit. Allah Almighty has sent a messenger and revealed to him a book by which He rescued you from what you were in. I bear witness there is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. I have come to you from him with what he commanded you and forbade you. He said: By Allah, that evening did not come while in his settlement there remained a man or woman but Muslim. Ibn Abbas says: We never heard of a delegate of a people better than Dimam ibn Thalabah."
"2381","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Nuwayfi, the freedman of Al al-Zubayr, narrated to me, and he mentioned it abridged."
"2382","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Dawud ibn al-Husayn, the freedman of Amr ibn Uthman, narrated to me, from Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The fear prayer was only like the prayer of your guards today behind your imams, except that it was in turns. A party stood, a company with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a party prostrated with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and those who were standing prostrated for themselves. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and they stood with him all together. Then he bowed, and they bowed with him all together. Then he prostrated, and those who had been standing the first time prostrated with him, and the others who had prostrated with him the first time stood. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, and those who prostrated with him at the end of their prayer, those who had been standing prostrated for themselves, then sat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined them with the salam."
"2383","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Tawus al-Yamani, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abbas: They claim the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash on Friday and wash your heads though you are not junub, and touch perfume. He said: So Ibn Abbas said: As for perfume, I do not know; as for washing, yes."
"2384","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Salamah ibn Kuhayl al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Nuwayfi, the freedman of Al al-Zubayr, both narrated to me, from Kurayb the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at night in a Hadrami cloak of his, wrapped in it, with nothing else upon him."
"2385","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas narrated to us, from Ikrimah the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a rainy day shielding himself from the mud when he prostrated with a cloak he placed before his hands toward the ground when he prostrated."
"2386","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Abbas ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas narrated to me, from some of his family, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in his two rakahs before Fajr, with the Opening of the Book and the two verses from the end of al-Baqarah in the first rakah, and in the other rakah with the Opening of the Quran and with the verse from Al Imran: Say: O People of the Book, come to a word equal between us and you, until he finished the verse."
"2387","Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, from Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Rukanah ibn Abd Yazid, the brother of al-Muttalib, divorced his wife three times in one sitting. He grieved for her with severe grief. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him: How did you divorce her? He said: I divorced her three times. He said: So he said: In one sitting? He said: Yes. He said: Then that is only one; return her if you wish. He said: So he returned her. And Ibn Abbas used to hold that divorce is only at every purity."
"2388","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Ismail ibn Umayyah ibn Amr ibn Said narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your brothers were struck at Uhud, Allah Almighty placed their souls in the bellies of green birds that come to the rivers of Paradise, eat of its fruits, and shelter to lamps of gold in the shade of the Throne. When they found the sweetness of their drink and their food and the goodness of their return, they said: Would that our brothers knew of what Allah did for us, lest they abstain from jihad and hold back from war. Allah Almighty said: I shall convey from you to them. So Allah Almighty revealed these verses upon His Messenger: And do not think those killed in the way of Allah dead; rather alive."
"2389","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2390","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Harith ibn Fudayl al-Ansari narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid al-Ansari, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are upon the bank of a river at the gate of Paradise, in a green dome; their provision comes out to them from Paradise morning and evening."
"2391","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Thawr ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with them to Baqi al-Gharqad, then directed them and said: Go in the name of Allah. O Allah, help them, meaning the party he directed to Kab ibn al-Ashraf."
"2392","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: So Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on his journey and left Abu Ruhm Kulthum ibn Husayn ibn Utbah ibn Khalaf al-Ghifari in charge of Madinah, and set out with ten days passed of Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted, and the people fasted with him, until when he was at al-Kadid, a water between Usfan and Amaj, he broke fast, then went on until he camped at Marr al-Zahran with ten thousand of the Muslims."
"2393","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Aban ibn Salih and Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah bint al-Harith during his journey while in ihram."
"2394","Husayn, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: A man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose mount broke his neck while in ihram. He said: Shroud him, and do not cover his head, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection saying the talbiyah, or calling out."
"2395","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, with its isnad, except that he said: And do not cover his face."
"2396","Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: No migration, he says, after the Conquest, but jihad and intention; and if you are called to march forth, then march forth."
"2397","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand upon my shoulder, or upon my shoulder-blade, Said doubted, then said: O Allah, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation."
"2398","He said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Stone has a tongue and two lips; it will testify for whoever touches it on the Day of Resurrection with truth."
"2399","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah fifteen years, eight years or seven seeing the light and hearing the voice, and eight or seven with revelation to him, and stayed in Madinah ten."
"2400","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning to a palm trunk. When the minbar was made, he moved to the minbar, and the trunk moaned until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and embraced it, and it calmed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection."
"2401","'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ammar, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of its meaning."
"2402","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there came to him in what the sleeper sees two angels, and one of them sat at his feet and the other at his head, and the one at his feet said to the one at his head, Strike a parable of this man and a parable of his ummah. He said, Indeed the parable of him and the parable of his ummah is like the parable of traveling people who came to the edge of a desert, and they had neither provision to cross the desert nor to return with, and while they were thus, a man in a Hibarah cloak came to them and said, What if I bring you to lush gardens and full cisterns, will you follow me. They said, Yes. He said, So he set out with them and brought them to lush gardens and full cisterns, and they ate and drank and grew fat. He said to them, Did I not meet you in that state, and you pledged to me that if I brought you to lush gardens and full cisterns you would follow me. They said, Yes. He said, Then ahead of you are gardens more lush than these and cisterns more full than these, so follow me. He said, And a party said, He has spoken the truth, by Allah, we will follow him, and a party said, We are content with this, we will stay upon it."
"2403","Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, he said, The water, the water of his washing (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they washed him after his death, used to collect in the eyelids of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and 'Ali used to sip it."
"2404","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, he said, Ibn 'Abbas, when he said the Talbiyah, would say, Here I am, O Allah, here I am, no partner have You, here I am, indeed praise and blessing belong to You and dominion, no partner have You. He said, And Ibn 'Abbas said, Stop at it, for it is the Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2405","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi who narrates the Tafsir, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind him, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits while he was bowed low in prostration with his hands spread apart."
"2406","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder of sheep, then prayed and did not renew ablution."
"2407","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me that Ibn 'Abbas narrated to him, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the shade of a room of his rooms, and with him were a group of Muslims, and the shade had almost shrunk away from them. He said, And he said, A man will come to you looking at you with the two eyes of a devil, and when he comes to you do not speak to him. He said, Then a blue-eyed man came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and spoke to him. He said, On what grounds do you revile me, you and so-and-so and so-and-so, a group whom he named by their names. He said, So the man went and called them, and they swore by Allah and made excuses to him. He said, So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down, They swear to him as they swear to you, and they reckon, the verse."
"2408","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of a room, and the shade had almost shrunk away from him, and he mentioned it."
"2409","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Qabus, that his father narrated to him, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, Two men whose need was one came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them spoke, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) noticed a bad smell from his mouth, and said to him, Will you not use the siwak. He said, Indeed I do, but I have not eaten food for three days. So he commanded a man to take him in and fulfilled his need."
"2410","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zabyan, that his father narrated to him, he said, We said to Ibn 'Abbas, What do you think about the saying of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, Allah has not made for a man two hearts in his breast, what did He mean by it. He said, The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day praying. He said, Then a passing thought crossed, and the hypocrites who prayed with him said, Do you not see that he has two hearts, a heart with you and a heart with them. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down, Allah has not made for a man two hearts in his breast."
"2411","Hasan, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a matter distressed him, would say, There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Mighty, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth and Lord of the Noble Throne, then he would supplicate."
"2412","Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to one of his daughters while she was in the market, and he took her and placed her in his lap until she died, and his eyes shed tears, and Umm Ayman wept. It was said to her, Do you weep in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said, Shall I not weep while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeps. He said, Indeed I did not weep, and this is mercy. Indeed the believer, his soul leaves from between his sides while he praises Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"2413","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, and 'Abd al-Samad, in meaning, said, Thabit narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, I stood to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I stood on his left, and he motioned with his hand from behind me until he took my upper arm or my hand until he set me on his right."
"2414","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Hasan ibn Thawban narrated to us, from 'Amir ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri, Hanash narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, This verse, Your wives are a tilth for you, was sent down concerning people among the Ansar who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Approach her in every manner if it is in the vulva."
"2415","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Qaza'ah, meaning Ibn Suwayd, narrated to us, 'Abdillah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I do not ask you for what I have brought you of proofs and guidance any reward, except that you love Allah and draw near to Him by obeying Him."
"2416","Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said, Ibn Bilal informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he performed ablution, and washed his face, then took a handful of water and rinsed his mouth with it and sniffed it out, then took a handful and did with it thus, meaning he added it to his other hand, and washed his face with it, then took a handful of water and washed his right hand with it, then took a handful of water and washed his left hand with it, then wiped his head, then took a handful of water then sprinkled it upon his right foot until he washed it, then took another handful and washed his left foot with it, then said, Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2417","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim informed me, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of this, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2418","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of hers, and said, Indeed this son of mine has madness that seizes him at our lunch and our dinner, and troubles us. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his chest and supplicated, and he vomited a vomit, meaning he coughed, and there came out of his belly the like of a black puppy."
"2419","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from 'Amr, meaning Ibn Abi 'Amr, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, and a man asked him about washing on Friday, is it obligatory. He said, No, and whoever wishes may wash. And I will tell you about the beginning of washing. The people were needy, and they used to wear wool, and they used to water the palms upon their backs, and the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was narrow with a low roof. So the people went in wool and sweated, and the minbar of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was short, it was only three steps. So the people sweated in wool, and their odors rose, the odors of wool, and some of them harmed others, until their odors reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon the minbar. So he said, O people, when you come to Friday, then wash, and let each of you touch of the best perfume he has if he has any."
"2420","Abu Sa'id narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Whoever has intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal."
"2421","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning advancing and delaying in stoning and slaughtering and shaving, No harm."
"2422","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said, Husayn ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Allah, grant Ibn 'Abbas wisdom and teach him interpretation."
"2423","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Rabi'ah ibn Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn 'Abdillah ibn Kinanah narrated to us, he said, I heard my grandfather Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn 'Abdillah narrating from his father, he said, al-Walid sent asking Ibn 'Abbas, How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in seeking rain. He said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out humble and lowly, and came to the prayer place, and prayed two rak'ahs as he prays in al-Fitr and al-Adha."
"2424","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed in poetry there is wisdom, and in eloquence there is magic."
"2425","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, There is no contagion and no omen and no Safar and no Hamah. And Simak mentioned that Safar is a beast that is in the belly of man. And a man said, O Messenger of Allah, a mangy camel is among a hundred camels and makes them mangy. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Then who infected the first."
"2426","'Abd al-Rahman and Abu Sa'id said, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman said, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a Khumrah."
"2427","Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from 'Arafah, and commanded them to be calm, and mounted Usamah ibn Zayd behind him, and said, O people, upon you is calmness and dignity, for righteousness is not in urging camels and horses. So I saw no camel lifting its leg running until it reached Muzdalifah. Then he mounted al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas behind him from Muzdalifah to Mina, while saying, O people, upon you is calmness and dignity, for righteousness is not in urging camels and horses. So I saw no camel lifting its leg running until it reached Mina."
"2428","Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah gave as gift a hundred sacrificial camels, among them a red camel belonging to Abu Jahl with a silver nose-ring in its nose."
"2429","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Whoever speaks about the Qur'an without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2430","Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said, Hammad narrated to us, he said, 'Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn 'Abbas, that a woman whose husband was absent came to a man to buy something from him, and he said, Enter the passageway until I give you. So she entered, and he kissed her and groped her. She said, Woe to you, indeed I am married. So he left her and regretted what he had done. Then he came to 'Umar and told him what he had done. He said, Woe to you, perhaps she is married. He said, Indeed she is married. He said, Go to Abu Bakr and ask him. So he came to Abu Bakr and told him. Abu Bakr said, Woe to you, perhaps she is married. He said, Indeed she is married. He said, Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and tell him. So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Perhaps she is married. He said, Indeed she is married. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent, and the Qur'an came down, And establish prayer at the ends of the day and in the watches of the night, to His saying, for those who remember. He said, So the man said, O Messenger of Allah, is it for me in particular or for people in general. He said, So 'Umar said, No, nor a comfort to your eye, rather it is for people in general. He said, So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said, 'Umar has spoken the truth, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2431","Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, Concerning the saying of the jinn, And that when the servant of Allah stood calling upon Him they almost became about him a compacted mass. He said, When they saw him praying with his companions, and they praying with his prayer and bowing with his bowing and prostrating with his prostration, they marveled at the obedience of his companions to him. So when they returned to their people they said, Indeed when the servant of Allah, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), stood calling upon Him they almost became about him a compacted mass."
"2432","Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out in his illness in which he died, binding his head with a rag, and sat upon the minbar, and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, Indeed there is none more beneficent to me in himself and his wealth than Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah. And had I taken from people a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but the brotherhood of Islam is better. Close off from me every small door in this mosque except the small door of Abu Bakr."
"2433","Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when Ma'iz ibn Malik came to him, said, Perhaps you kissed or touched or looked. He said, No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Did you penetrate her, without using a euphemism. He said, Yes. He said, So at that he ordered that he be stoned."
"2434","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying, I seek protection for you both in the perfect words of Allah from every devil and pest and from every envious eye. Then he would say, Thus my father Ibrahim, peace be upon him, used to seek protection for Isma'il and Ishaq, peace be upon them."
"2435","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, I said to him, Indeed we go raiding and are brought skins and waterskins. He said, I do not know what to say to you except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, Whatever skin is tanned has become pure."
"2436","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven and not to tuck hair nor garment."
"2437","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while he was in ihram."
"2438","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it. Ibn 'Abbas said, And I deem everything in the position of food."
"2439","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said, Eat in the bowl from its sides and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends in its middle."
"2440","Surayj narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, I think he raised it, he said, When he raised his head from bowing he would say, Allah hears whoever praises Him, O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heaven and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of a thing after."
"2441","Surayj narrated to us, 'Abbad, meaning Ibn al-'Awwam, narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to Maymunah bint al-Harith, and she gave her affair to al-'Abbas, so he married her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2442","Surayj narrated to us, 'Abbad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Muslims killed a man of the polytheists on the day of the Trench, and they sent a messenger to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offering to pay blood-money for his corpse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed it is filthy, filthy its blood-money, filthy its corpse. So he left him to them."
"2443","Surayj narrated to us, 'Abbad narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet wrote a document between the Muhajirin and the Ansar, that they share their blood-money liabilities and ransom their captive with kindness and reconciliation among the Muslims."
"2444","Surayj narrated to me, 'Abbad narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"2445","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'ma 'Ubaydillah ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his sword Dhu al-Faqar as an extra share on the day of Badr, and it is that about which he saw the vision on the day of Uhud. He said, I saw in my sword Dhu al-Faqar a notch, and I interpreted it as a loss among you, and I saw that I was riding a ram behind another, and I interpreted it as the ram of the squadron, and I saw that I was in strong armor, and I interpreted it as Madinah, and I saw cows being slaughtered, and cows, by Allah, are good, and cows, by Allah, are good. So it was what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said."
"2446","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night was to the measure that one in the room could hear him while he was in the house."
"2447","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Report is not like seeing. Indeed Allah the Mighty and Majestic told Musa what his people did with the calf, and he did not throw the tablets, but when he saw what they had done he threw the tablets and they broke."
"2448","Surayj narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said, I was with Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said, Which of you saw the star that fell last night. I said, I, then I said, But indeed I was not in prayer, but I was stung. He said, And what did you do. I said, I sought ruqyah. He said, And what carried you to that. I said, A hadith al-Sha'bi narrated to us from Buraydah al-Aslami, that he said, There is no ruqyah except for an eye or a sting. So Sa'id, meaning Ibn Jubayr, said, He has done well who stops at what he heard. Then he said, Ibn 'Abbas narrated to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, The nations were displayed to me, and I saw the prophet and with him the group, and the prophet and with him the man, and the prophet and with him no one, when there was raised to me a great multitude. I said, This is my ummah. It was said, This is Musa and his people, but look to the horizon. And there was a great multitude. Then it was said, Look to this other side. And there was a great multitude. It was said, This is your ummah, and with them seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning nor punishment. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose and entered, and the people discussed about that. They said, Who are these who will enter Paradise without reckoning nor punishment. Some said, Perhaps they are those who accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And some said, Perhaps they are those who were born in Islam and never associated anything with Allah ever. And they mentioned things. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them and said, What is this you were discussing about. So they told him of their saying. He said, They are those who do not cauterize and do not seek ruqyah and do not take omens and upon their Lord they rely. So 'Ukkashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi stood and said, Am I among them, O Messenger of Allah. He said, You are among them. Then another stood and said, Am I among them, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Ukkashah has beaten you to it."
"2449","Shuja' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, the like of it."
"2450","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fasted a complete month ever except Ramadan. And when he fasted, he would fast until one saying would say, By Allah, he will not break. And when he broke, he would break until one saying would say, By Allah, he will not fast."
"2451","Surayj narrated to us, 'Abdillah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from 'Ata, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traversed the valleys and came with sacrificial animals, and he had to circumambulate the House and run between al-Safa and al-Marwah before standing at 'Arafah. As for you, O people of Makkah, delay your circumambulation until you return."
"2452","Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, When wine was forbidden they said, O Messenger of Allah, our companions who died while drinking it. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down, There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted."
"2453","Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said, It was narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbas that he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The drunkard, if he dies, meets Allah like a worshipper of idols."
"2454","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn 'Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed the auspiciousness of horses is in their white foreheads and legs."
"2455","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Jabr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, Allah took the covenant from the back of Adam at Na'man, meaning 'Arafah, and brought forth from his loins every offspring He created, and scattered them before Him like dust, then spoke to them directly. He said, Am I not your Lord. They said, Yes, we bear witness, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, Indeed we were of this unaware, or you say, Our fathers associated before, and we were offspring after them, so will You destroy us for what the falsifiers did."
"2456","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday, Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and Has there come upon man a time of the age."
"2457","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"2458","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a man who approaches his wife while she is menstruating, he said, He gives half a dinar in charity."
"2459","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us ahead, or sent Umm Salamah ahead, and I was with them, from Muzdalifah to the Jamarah of al-'Aqabah, and commanded us to stone it when the sun rises."
"2460","Husayn narrated to us, Dawud, meaning al-'Attar, narrated to us, from 'Amr, he said, 'Ata narrated to me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with the heavy baggage and the weak of his family on the night of Muzdalifah, so we prayed dawn at Mina and stoned the Jamarah."
"2461","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ata ibn 'Alqamah al-Qurashi, he said, We entered the house of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found in it 'Abdillah ibn 'Abbas. So we mentioned ablution from what fire has touched. 'Abdillah said, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating of what fire had touched, then praying and not performing ablution. One of us said to him, Did you see him, O Ibn 'Abbas. He said, So he pointed with his hand to his eyes and said, My eyes saw."
"2462","Husayn ibn Muhammad and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, A man of Banu Sulaym passed by a group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while driving his sheep, and greeted them. They said, He greeted you only to seek protection from you. So they set upon him and killed him and took his sheep, and brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down, O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of Allah, verify, and do not say to whoever offers you peace, You are not a believer, to the end of the verse."
"2463","Husayn and Abu Nu'aym said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning His saying the Mighty and Majestic, You are the best nation brought forth for mankind, enjoining right and forbidding wrong. He said, They are those who emigrated with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah. Abu Nu'aym said, With the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2464","Husayn and Abu Nu'aym said, Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', he said, One who heard Ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not alight between 'Arafat and Muzdalifah except to pass water."
"2465","Husayn narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said, 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said, I heard Jabir ibn Zayd, he said, I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed eight together and seven together."
"2466","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave among his sacrificial camels a camel that belonged to Abu Jahl with a silver nose-ring in its nose."
"2467","He said, Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked up a bone with meat and ate from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"2468","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, When Hilal ibn Umayyah accused his wife, it was said to him, By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will flog you eighty lashes. He said, Allah is more just than that He strike me eighty strokes, while He knows that I saw until I was certain and heard until I was certain. No, by Allah, he will never strike me. He said, So the verse of mutual cursing came down."
"2469","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the daughter of Khidham came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that her father married her while she was unwilling, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice."
"2470","Husayn and Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Malik said, 'Ubaydillah, meaning Ibn 'Amr, narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Ibn Jubayr, Ahmad said, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, There will be a people at the end of time who dye with this black, Husayn said, like the crops of pigeons, they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"2471","He said, Husayn narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said, 'Abdillah ibn 'Abbas said, A group of Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Abu al-Qasim, tell us of traits we ask you about, none knows them but a prophet. And among what they asked him was, What food did Isra'il forbid upon himself before the Torah was sent down. He said, So I adjure you by Allah who sent down the Torah upon Musa, do you know that Isra'il, Ya'qub, peace be upon him, fell gravely ill, and his sickness lasted long, so he vowed a vow to Allah, that if Allah healed him of his sickness he would forbid the most beloved drink to him and the most beloved food to him. And the most beloved food to him was camel meat, and the most beloved drink to him was their milk. They said, O Allah, yes."
"2472","al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"2473","al-Fadl narrated to us, he said, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed in poetry there is wisdom, and indeed in speech there is magic."
"2474","al-Fadl narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, he said, Ibn 'Abbas passed by people who had set up a dove shooting at it. He said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking a living soul as a target."
"2475","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a daughter of his dying, and embraced her and placed her between his breasts, and she died in his hands. And Umm Ayman cried out. It was said, Do you weep in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said, Do I not see you weeping, O Messenger of Allah. He said, I do not weep, it is only mercy. Indeed the believer is in every good in every state, indeed his soul leaves from between his sides while he praises Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"2476","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Badhimah, Qays ibn Habtar narrated to me, he said, I asked Ibn 'Abbas about white jars and green jars and red jars. He said, Indeed the first who asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays. They said, Indeed we get sediment, so in which vessels. He said, Do not drink in gourds and varnished vessels and hollowed stumps and green jars, and drink in waterskins. Then he said, Indeed Allah has forbidden upon me, or has forbidden, wine and gambling and the drum, and every intoxicant is forbidden. Sufyan said, I said to 'Ali ibn Badhimah, What is the drum. He said, The tabl."
"2477","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from a man, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, The evil eye is true, it brings down the mountain-climber."
"2478","'Abdillah ibn al-Walid al-'Adani narrated to us, he said, Sufyan narrated to us, from Duwayd, from Isma'il ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of it."
"2479","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abdillah ibn 'Uthman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The best of your kohl is ithmid at sleep, it grows hair and clears sight. And the best of your garments is white, so wear it and shroud your dead in it."
"2480","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, al-'Ala ibn Salih narrated to us, 'Adi ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking anything in which there is a soul as a target."
"2481","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, 'Ubaydillah ibn 'Abdillah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said, Nafi' ibn Jubayr informed me, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said, The unmarried woman has more right to her affair than her guardian, and the virgin is asked concerning herself, and her silence is her consent."
"2482","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The jinn used to hear the revelation, and hear a word and add to it ten, so what they heard was true and what they added was false. And the stars were not shot with before that. But when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, none of them came to his seat but was shot with a flame burning whatever it struck. So they complained of that to Iblis. He said, This is only from a matter that has occurred. So he spread his troops, and there they were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying between the two mountains of Nakhlah. So they came to him and told him. He said, This is the event that occurred on earth."
"2483","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, 'Abdillah ibn al-Walid al-'Ijli narrated to us, and he had a presence we saw him with Hasan, from Bukayr ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Abu al-Qasim, indeed we ask you of five things, and if you tell us of them we will know you are a prophet and follow you. So he took upon them what Isra'il took upon his sons when they said, Allah is guardian over what we say. He said, Bring them. They said, Tell us of the sign of the prophet. He said, His eyes sleep and his heart does not sleep. They said, Tell us how the woman feminizes and how she masculinizes. He said, The two waters meet, and if the water of the man overcomes the water of the woman it masculinizes, and if the water of the woman overcomes it feminizes. They said, Tell us what Isra'il forbade upon himself. He said, He used to complain of sciatica, and found nothing suiting him except the milk of such and such, 'Abdillah ibn Ahmad said, My father said, some of them said, meaning camels, so he forbade their meat. They said, You have spoken the truth. They said, Tell us what this thunder is. He said, An angel among the angels of Allah the Mighty and Majestic entrusted with clouds, in his hand, or in his hand is a firebrand with which he drives the clouds, guiding them where Allah commands. They said, Then what is this sound that is heard. He said, His voice. They said, You have spoken the truth, only one remains, and it is that for which we pledge you if you tell us of it, for there is no prophet but has an angel coming to him with news, so tell us who is your companion. He said, Jibril, peace be upon him. They said, Jibril, he who descends with war and fighting and punishment, our enemy. Had you said Mika'il who descends with mercy and vegetation and rain, it would have been. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down, Whoever is an enemy to Jibril, to the end of the verse."
"2484","al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from 'Ilba ibn Ahmar, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the sacrifice came, so we slaughtered a cow for seven and a camel for ten."
"2485","al-Hasan ibn Yahya and al-Talaqani said, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abdillah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray turning right and left, and not twisting his neck behind his back. al-Talaqani said, Thawr narrated to me, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the like of it."
"2486","Waki' narrated to us, 'Abdillah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from a man of the companions of 'Ikrimah, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glance in his prayer without twisting his neck."
"2487","Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Ja'd Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Raja, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Whoever sees of his ruler a thing he dislikes, let him be patient, for whoever splits from the community a span and dies, his death is jahili."
"2488","Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Muslim al-'Abdi narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Mutawakkil narrated to us that Ibn 'Abbas narrated that he spent a night with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night and went out and looked at the sky, then recited this verse that is in Al 'Imran, Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day, until he reached, Glory be to You, so shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Then he returned to the house and used the siwak and performed ablution, then stood and prayed, then lay down, then returned also and looked at the sky, then recited this verse, then returned and used the siwak and performed ablution, then stood and prayed, then lay down, then returned also and looked at the sky, then recited this verse, then returned and used the siwak and performed ablution, then stood and prayed."
"2489","Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said, Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hashim, from Yahya ibn 'Abbad, or from Abu Hashim, from Hajjaj, Mansur doubted, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said, Allah hears whoever praises Him, would say, O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of a thing after. He said, And Mansur said, And 'Awn narrated to me from his brother 'Ubaydillah with this."
"2490","'Abdillah ibn Bakr and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked concerning the daughter of Hamzah to marry her. He said, Indeed she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and what is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by suckling."
"2491","'Abdillah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said, Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn 'Abbas, that 'Ali said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the daughter of Hamzah, and mentioned of her beauty. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed she is the daughter of my brother through suckling. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Do you not know that Allah the Mighty and Majestic has forbidden by suckling what He has forbidden by lineage."
"2492","'Abdillah ibn Bakr and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he saw no harm in a man marrying while in ihram, and would say, Indeed the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah bint al-Harith at a water called Sarif while in ihram. And when the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed his pilgrimage, he came until when he was at that water he consummated with her."
"2493","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man with his thigh exposed. He said, Cover your thigh, for the thigh of a man is of his nakedness."
"2494","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, He said, Which of the two readings was later, the reading of 'Abdillah or the reading of Zayd. He said, We said, The reading of Zayd. He said, No, except that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to review the Qur'an with Jabra'il every year once. And when it was the year in which he died, he reviewed it with him twice. And the last reading was the reading of 'Abdillah."
"2495","Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi 'Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, concerning His saying, Alif Lam Mim, the Romans have been defeated. He said, They were defeated and they will defeat. He said, The polytheists loved that Persia prevail over Rome because they are people of idols, and the Muslims loved that Rome prevail over Persia because they are people of the Book. So they mentioned it to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, But indeed they will defeat. He said, So Abu Bakr mentioned it to them. They said, Make between us and you a term, and if we prevail it is for us such and such, and if you prevail it is for you such and such. So he made a term of five years, and they did not prevail. So Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said, Why did you not make it to less than, he thought he said, ten. He said, Sa'id ibn Jubayr said, Bid' is what is less than ten. Then Rome prevailed after. He said, So that is His saying, Alif Lam Mim, the Romans have been defeated, to His saying, And that day the believers will rejoice. He said, They rejoice in the victory of Allah."
"2496","Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said, Za'idah narrated to us, 'Abdillah ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, he said, 'Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me that Dhakwan, chamberlain of 'A'ishah, narrated to him that 'Abdillah ibn 'Abbas came seeking permission to see 'A'ishah. So I came, and at her head was her nephew 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman. I said, This is Ibn 'Abbas seeking permission. So her nephew 'Abdillah leaned over her and said, This is 'Abdillah ibn 'Abbas seeking permission, and she is dying. She said, Leave me from Ibn 'Abbas. He said, O mother, indeed Ibn 'Abbas is of your righteous sons, to greet you and bid you farewell. She said, Give him permission if you wish. He said, So I let him in. When he sat he said, Rejoice. She said, Also. He said, There is nothing between you and meeting Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the beloved ones except that the soul leaves the body. You were the most beloved wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved only what was good. And your necklace fell on the night of al-Abwa, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed until morning in the dwelling, and the people woke with no water with them. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down, Then seek clean earth, and that was in your cause, and what Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down for this ummah of concession. And Allah sent down your innocence from above seven heavens, brought by the Trustworthy Spirit, so there is no mosque of the mosques of Allah in which Allah is mentioned but it is recited in it night and day. She said, Leave me from you, O Ibn 'Abbas, by Him in whose hand is my soul, I wish I were forgotten dust."
"2497","Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from a man, he said, Ibn 'Abbas said to her, You were only named Mother of the Believers to be happy, and indeed it is your name before you were born."
"2498","Mu'awiyah narrated to me, he said, Za'idah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qays ibn Sa'd, 'Ata narrated to me that Ibn 'Abbas narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, would say, O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of a thing after."
"2499","Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi 'Amrah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds and green jars and varnished vessels and hollowed stumps, and mixing ripe dates and fresh yellow dates."
"2500","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydillah ibn 'Abdillah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, The conquest was on thirteen nights past of Ramadan."
"2501","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Mujahid who said: We were with Ibn Abbas and they mentioned the Dajjal, and they said: Written between his eyes is Kaf Fa Ra. He said: What are you saying. He said: They say: Written between his eyes is Kaf Fa Ra. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: I did not hear him say that, but he said: As for Ibrahim, peace be upon him, then look at your companion, and as for Musa, peace be upon him, he is a brown-skinned curly-haired man upon a red camel haltered with a fiber rope, as though I am looking at him when he descends into the valley reciting the Talbiyah."
"2502","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us from Mujahid who said: They mentioned him meaning the Dajjal, and he said: Written between his eyes is Kaf Fa Ra. Then Ibn Abbas said: I did not hear him say that, but he said: As for Ibrahim, peace be upon him, then look at your companion. Yazid said meaning himself, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And as for Musa he is a brown-skinned curly-haired tall man upon a red camel haltered with a fiber rope, as though I am looking at him when he descends into the valley reciting the Talbiyah. My father said: Hushaym said: Al-khulbah is fiber."
"2503","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Muhammad that Ibn Abbas said, Ibn Awn said: I think he raised it, he said: He ordered a crier who called on a rainy day: Pray in your dwellings."
"2504","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim meaning Ibn Nafi narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Ata from Ibn Abbas that a sheep belonging to one of the houses of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why did you not make use of its skin."
"2505","Ibn Abi Bukayr, he is Yahya, narrated to us, Ibrahim meaning Ibn Nafi narrated to us from Wahb ibn Minas al-Adani from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he intended to prostrate after the rakah would say: O Allah our Lord to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of things after."
"2506","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Khalid ibn Abi Imran from Hanash al-Sanani from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was born on Monday, and was commissioned as a prophet on Monday, and died on Monday, and left emigrating from Makkah to Madinah on Monday, and arrived in Madinah on Monday, and raised the Black Stone on Monday."
"2507","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from al-Amash from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Arafat standing while he had mounted al-Fadl behind him, then a Bedouin came and stood nearby with a slave girl behind him, and al-Fadl began looking at her, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, noticed him and began turning his face away. He said: Then he said: O people, righteousness is not by urging horses or camels, so calmness is upon you. He said: Then he moved on. He said: I did not see it raising its foreleg running until it reached Jam. He said: When he stood at Jam he mounted Usamah behind him, then he said: O people, righteousness is not by urging horses and camels, so calmness is upon you. He said: Then he moved on, and I did not see it raising its foreleg running until it reached Mina. Then there came to us the weak dark ones of Banu Hashim upon their donkeys, and he began striking our thighs and saying: O my sons, move on and do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises."
"2508","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr narrated to him from Kurayb the freedman of Ibn Abbas from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered the House found therein a picture of Ibrahim and a picture of Maryam, so he said: As for them they have heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture. This is Ibrahim depicted, why does he seek division by arrows."
"2509","Harun narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, Abu Sakhr narrated to me from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir from Kurayb the freedman of Ibn Abbas from Abd Allah ibn Abbas that a son of his died at Qudayd or at Usfan, so he said: O Kurayb, see how many people have gathered for him. He said: So I went out and there were people gathered for him, so I informed him. He said: He says: Are they forty. He said: Yes. He said: Bring him out, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no Muslim who dies and forty men who associate nothing with Allah stand over his funeral except that Allah accepts their intercession for him."
"2510","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad meaning al-Khattabi narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us from Abd al-Karim from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that a man went out and two men followed him with a man behind them saying: Return. He said: So they returned. He said: Then he said to him: These two are devils, and I kept with them until I turned them back. When you come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, convey to him greetings of peace and inform him that we are engaged in collecting our charities, and had it been permissible for him we would have sent it to him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at that forbade seclusion."
"2511","Abu Qatan narrated to us from al-Masudi who said: We did not meet anyone more upright in the doctrine of the Shiah than Adi ibn Thabit."
"2512","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad meaning al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah meaning Ibn Amr narrated to us from Abd al-Karim from Qays ibn Habtar from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The price of a dog is evil. He said: If he comes to you seeking the price of the dog then fill his palms with dust."
"2513","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Abu Hassan who said: A man from Balhujaym said: O Abu al-Abbas, what is this fatwa that has spread among the people that whoever circumambulates the House has exited ihram. Then he said: It is the Sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, even if you dislike."
"2514","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to us, Ibn Abbas said: A group of Jews came to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day and said: O Abu al-Qasim, inform us about matters we ask you about which none knows except a prophet. He said: Ask me about whatever you wish, but grant me the covenant of Allah and what Yaqub, peace be upon him, took upon his sons, that if I inform you of something and you recognize it, you will follow me in Islam. They said: That is yours. He said: Then ask me about whatever you wish. They said: Inform us about four matters we ask you about: Inform us what food Israil forbade upon himself before the Torah was revealed, and inform us how the water of the woman and the water of the man are, how the male comes from them, and inform us how this unlettered Prophet is in sleep, and who is his ally among the angels. He said: Upon you is the covenant of Allah and His pact, that if I inform you, you will follow me. He said: So they gave him whatever covenant and pact he wished. He said: I adjure you by the One Who revealed the Torah to Musa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do you know that Israil, Yaqub, peace be upon him, fell severely ill and his sickness lasted long, so he vowed to Allah a vow that if Allah Exalted healed him from his sickness he would forbid the most beloved drink to him and the most beloved food to him, and the most beloved food to him was camel meat and the most beloved drink to him was their milk. They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. I adjure you by Allah besides Whom there is no god, Who revealed the Torah to Musa, do you know that the water of the man is white and thick and the water of the woman is yellow and thin, so whichever prevails the child and resemblance belong to it by Allah's permission: If the water of the man prevails over the water of the woman it is male by Allah's permission, and if the water of the woman prevails over the water of the man it is female by Allah's permission. They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. I adjure you by the One Who revealed the Torah to Musa, do you know that this unlettered Prophet, his eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. They said: And you now, inform us who is your ally among the angels, then we will join you or part from you. He said: My ally is Jibril, peace be upon him, and Allah has never sent a prophet except that he is his ally. They said: Then we part from you. Had your ally been other than him among the angels we would have followed you and believed you. He said: What prevents you from believing him. They said: He is our enemy. He said: At that Allah Mighty and Majestic said: Say whoever is an enemy to Jibril for he brought it down upon your heart by Allah's permission, up to His saying Mighty and Majestic: They cast the Book of Allah behind their backs as though they do not know. At that they incurred anger upon anger."
"2515","Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr narrated to us from Ibn Abbas with similar meaning."
"2516","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from a man from Saeed ibn Jubayr who said: I came upon Ibn Abbas while he was eating pomegranate at Arafah, and he reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, broke his fast at Arafah. Umm al-Fadl sent him milk and he drank."
"2517","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, broke his fast at Arafah. He said: Umm al-Fadl sent him milk and he drank it."
"2518","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah informed us from Musa ibn Salamah who said: I performed Hajj, I and Sinan ibn Salamah, and Sinan had a sacrificial camel which became exhausted, and he was perplexed by its affair. I said: If I reach Makkah I will surely investigate about this. He said: When we reached Makkah I said: Come with us to Ibn Abbas. So we entered upon him while with him was a slave girl. I had two needs and my companion had a need. He said: Shall I be alone with you. I said: No. I said: I had a sacrificial camel which became exhausted upon us, so I said: If I reach Makkah I will surely investigate about this. Then Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent sacrificial camels with so-and-so and instructed him concerning them. When he turned back he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I do with what becomes exhausted of them. He said: Slaughter it and dye its sandal in its blood and strike it upon its side, and neither you nor anyone of your companions shall eat from it. He said: I said to him: I join these expeditions and gain spoils and emancipate on behalf of my mother, will it suffice for her that I emancipate. Then Ibn Abbas said: The wife of Salman ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani ordered that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, be asked about her mother who died without performing Hajj, will it suffice for her to perform Hajj on her behalf. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Tell me, if her mother had a debt and she paid it on her behalf, would it suffice for her mother. He said: Yes. He said: Then let her perform Hajj on behalf of her mother. And he asked him about seawater, and he said: Seawater is pure."
"2519","Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Jad Abu Uthman narrated to us from Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what he related from his Lord, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your Lord Blessed and Exalted is Merciful. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, it is written for him as a good deed, and if he does it, it is written for him as ten up to seven hundred up to many multiples. And whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is written for him as a good deed, and if he does it, it is written for him as one, or Allah erases it. And none perishes upon Allah Exalted except one doomed."
"2520","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Seek it in the last ten of Ramadan, in a ninth remaining, or a seventh remaining, or a fifth remaining."
"2521","Affan narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrate in Sad."
"2522","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Walah who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: We raid the people of the Maghreb and most of their waterskins, and perhaps Hammad said: and most of their waterskins are dead animals. Then he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Its tanning is its purification."
"2523","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed in Makkah fifteen years: seven years seeing the light and hearing the voice, and eight years being revealed to, and stayed in Madinah ten years."
"2524","Affan narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Qatadah from Yahya ibn Yamur from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate meat from a shoulder then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"2525","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Jabir from Ammar from Saeed ibn Jubayr who said: Abd Allah narrated to me, Affan did not attribute him more than Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not resemble me. And Affan once said: Does not resemble me."
"2526","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd reporting that he heard Abd Allah ibn Abbas that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, preaching at Arafat: Whoever does not find two sandals let him wear two khuffs, and whoever does not find an izar let him wear trousers."
"2527","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Tawus reporting from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones and not to gather hair nor garment. And he said another time: Your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2528","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hassan reporting from Abd Allah ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zhuhr at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then his sacrificial camel was brought and he marked the right side of its hump then wiped the blood from it then garlanded it with two sandals, then his mount was brought, and when he sat upon it and it stood straight with him at al-Bayda he entered ihram for Hajj."
"2529","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Saeed ibn al-Musayyab reporting that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"2530","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: A hindquarter of a donkey, or he said: A leg of a donkey, was gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in ihram, so he returned it."
"2531","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith informed us from Abu al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a matter distressed him would say: There is no god but Allah the Mighty the Forbearing, there is no god but Allah Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth Lord of the Mighty Throne, there is no god but Allah Lord of the Noble Throne, there is no god but Allah Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth Lord of the Noble Throne."
"2532","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Saeed ibn Jubayr reporting from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not take anything containing a soul as a target. Shubah said: I said to him: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"2533","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Saeed ibn Jubayr reporting from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out at Fitr and did not pray before it nor after it, then he came to the women with Bilal, and began saying: Give charity. So the woman began casting her earring and her necklace."
"2534","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam informed me, he said: Saeed ibn Jubayr led us in Maghrib at Jam as three rakahs with an iqamah. He said: Then he gave salam then prayed Isha as two rakahs, then he mentioned that Abd Allah ibn Umar did that, and mentioned that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did that."
"2535","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Saeed ibn Jubayr reporting from Ibn Abbas who said: Sab ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a leg of a donkey while he was in ihram, so he returned it while it was dripping blood."
"2536","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while he was fasting."
"2537","Bahz narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi from the cousin of your Prophet meaning Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate with these supplications at distress: There is no god but Allah the Mighty the Forbearing, there is no god but Allah Lord of the Mighty Throne, there is no god but Allah Lord of the heavens and the earth Lord of the Noble Throne."
"2538","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Walah who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: We raid this Maghreb and most of their waterskins are hides of dead animals. He said: Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Its tanning is its purification."
"2539","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Abu Hassan that a man said to Abd Allah ibn Abbas: This which you say has spread among the people. Hammam said meaning: Everyone who circumambulates the House has exited ihram. Then he said: It is the Sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, even if you dislike. Hammam said meaning: Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him."
"2540","Affan narrated to us, Hajib ibn Umar Abu Khushaynah the brother of Isa al-Nahwi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn al-Araj narrated to us, he said: I sat with Ibn Abbas while he was pillowing his cloak at the well of Zamzam, and I sat with him, and he was an excellent companion. So I asked him about Ashura. Then he said: About which of its states do you ask. I said: About its fast. He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram then count, and when you wake on its ninth then fast that day. I said: Did Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fast it thus. He said: Yes."
"2541","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us that Tawus said: One who knows it better than them narrated to me meaning Abd Allah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For a man to grant his brother his land is better for him than to take upon it a known rent."
"2542","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the husband of Barirah was a black slave named Mughith. He said: I used to see him following her in the streets of Madinah squeezing his eyes upon her. He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave four judgments concerning her: Her masters stipulated the wala, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged the wala belongs to whoever emancipates. And he gave her the choice, so she chose herself, and he ordered her to observe the waiting period. He said: And charity was given to her, so she gifted some of it to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"2543","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Lahiq ibn Humayd and Ikrimah who said: Umar said: Who knows when Laylat al-Qadr is. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is in the ten, in seven passing or seven remaining."
"2544","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-Amash from Amr ibn Murrah from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ascended al-Safa one day and said: O morning calamity, O morning calamity. He said: Quraysh gathered to him and said to him: What is wrong with you. Then he said: Tell me, if I informed you that the enemy will attack you in the morning or in the evening, would you believe me. Then they said: Yes. He said: Then he said: I am a warner to you before severe punishment. He said: Then Abu Lahab said: Is it for this you gathered us, perdition to you. He said: Then Allah Mighty and Majestic revealed: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab and perish, to the end of the Surah."
"2545","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Wahb ibn Kaysan from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata from Abd Allah ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating a shoulder of sheep then praying without rinsing and without touching water."
"2546","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Nadrah who said: Ibn Abbas addressed us upon the minbar of Basrah and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There was no prophet except that he had a supplication he hastened in this world, and I have hidden my supplication as intercession for my ummah. And I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection without boast, and I am the first whom the earth splits upon without boast, and in my hand is the banner of praise without boast. Adam and those below him are under my banner without boast. And the Day of Resurrection becomes long upon the people, so some of them say to others: Come with us to Adam the father of mankind, let him intercede for us to our Lord Mighty and Majestic, let Him judge between us. So they come to Adam, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and say: O Adam, you whom Allah created with His hand and settled you in His Garden and made His angels prostrate to you, intercede for us to our Lord, let Him judge between us. Then he says: I am not there for you. I was expelled from Paradise due to my error, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But come to Nuh the head of the prophets. So they come to Nuh and say: O Nuh, intercede for us to our Lord, let Him judge between us. Then he says: I am not there for you. I invoked a supplication that drowned the people of the earth, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But come to Ibrahim the intimate friend of Allah. So they come to Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and say: O Ibrahim, intercede for us to our Lord, let Him judge between us. Then he says: I am not there for you. I uttered in Islam three lies, and by Allah he attempted with them only on behalf of the religion of Allah: His saying: I am ill, and his saying: Rather the greatest of them did this, so ask them if they speak, and his saying to his wife when he came upon the king: She is my sister. And today nothing concerns me except myself. But come to Musa, peace be upon him, whom Allah chose with His message and His speech. So they come to him and say: O Musa, you whom Allah chose with His message and spoke to you, intercede for us to your Lord, let Him judge between us. Then he says: I am not there for you. I killed a soul without a soul, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But come to Isa the spirit of Allah and His word. So they come to Isa and say: O Isa, intercede for us to your Lord, let Him judge between us. Then he says: I am not there for you. I was taken as a god besides Allah, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But have you considered, were goods in a sealed vessel, could what is inside it be reached until the seal is broken. He said: Then they say: No. He said: Then he says: Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is the seal of the prophets, and he has come today, and he has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So they come to me and say: O Muhammad, intercede for us to your Lord, let Him judge between us. So I say: I am for it, until Allah Mighty and Majestic permits whomever He wills and is pleased. When Allah Blessed and Exalted intends to separate between His creation, a caller calls: Where is Ahmad and his ummah. So we are the last the first. We are the last of the nations and the first to be reckoned. So the nations make way for us from our path, and we proceed bright in limbs from the trace of purification. So the nations say: This nation almost all became prophets. So we come to the gate of Paradise, and I take the ring of the gate and knock. It is said: Who are you. So I say: I am Muhammad. So it is opened for me. So I come to my Lord Mighty and Majestic upon His Kursi or His bed, Hammad doubted, and I fall to Him prostrating. So I praise Him with praises with which none before me praised Him and with which none after me will praise Him. It is said: O Muhammad, raise your head, and ask you will be given, and speak you will be heard, and intercede you will be granted intercession. So I raise my head and say: O Lord, my ummah, my ummah. Then He says: Bring out whoever has in his heart the weight of such and such, Hammad did not retain it. Then I return and prostrate and say what I said. It is said: Raise your head, and speak you will be heard, and ask you will be given, and intercede you will be granted intercession. So I say: O Lord, my ummah, my ummah. Then He says: Bring out whoever has in his heart the weight of such and such less than the first. Then I return and prostrate and say similar to that. It is said to me: Raise your head, and speak you will be heard, and ask you will be given, and intercede you will be granted intercession. So I say: O Lord, my ummah, my ummah. Then He said: Bring out whoever has in his heart the weight of such and such less than that."
"2547","Affan narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Simak informed us from Ikrimah who said: Ibn Abbas said: I was approached while I was sleeping in Ramadan and it was said to me: Tonight is Laylat al-Qadr. He said: So I stood while I was drowsy and clung to some of the ropes of the tent of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was praying. So I looked at that night. He said: It was the night of twenty-three."
"2548","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Kathir from Abu al-Minhal from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived while they were paying in advance, so he said: Whoever pays in advance let him not pay except in a known measure and a known weight."
"2549","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out of the lavatory and food was brought to him. It was said to him: Will you not perform ablution. Then he said: I was only commanded with ablution when I stand for prayer."
"2550","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hanzalah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: I said to Ikrimah: I recite in Maghrib prayer: Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the dawn, and: Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and people criticize me for that. Then he said: What is wrong with that. Recite them, for they are from the Quran. Then he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and prayed two rakahs in which he recited only the Mother of the Book."
"2551","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought people of these heretics with books, so he ordered a fire which was kindled, then he burned them and their books. Ikrimah said: That reached Ibn Abbas, so he said: Had I been I would not have burned them due to the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but I would have killed them due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever changes his religion kill him. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not punish with the punishment of Allah Mighty and Majestic."
"2552","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us from Ayyub from Ikrimah that Ali seized people who apostatized from Islam and burned them with fire. That reached Ibn Abbas, so he said: Had I been I would not have burned them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not punish anyone with the punishment of Allah Mighty and Majestic. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever changes his religion kill him. What Ibn Abbas said reached Ali, so he said: Woe to the son of the mother of Ibn Abbas."
"2553","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, he is Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ammar informed us from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what the sleeper sees at midday while he was standing disheveled dusty with a bottle in his hand containing blood. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you O Messenger of Allah, what is this. He said: This is the blood of Husayn and his companions. I have kept collecting it since today. So we counted that day and found he was killed on that day."
"2554","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Sulayman al-Shaybani from al-Shabi from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over a funeral after it was buried. And Waki said: Sufyan narrated to us similar to it."
"2555","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Kurayb the freedman of Ibn Abbas from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one of them when he comes to his wife says: In the name of Allah, O Allah keep Satan from me and keep Satan from what You provide us, then a child is born between them, Satan will never harm him ever."
"2556","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Layth from Tawus from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Teach and ease and do not complicate. And when you are angry then be silent. And when you are angry then be silent. And when you are angry then be silent."
"2557","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, combined Zhuhr and Asr in Madinah without travel nor fear. He said: I said: O Abu al-Abbas, why did he do that. He said: He intended not to burden anyone of his ummah."
"2558","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Amr ibn Dinar from Saeed ibn al-Huwayrith from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to relieve himself and fulfilled his need, then food was brought near to him. They said: Shall we bring you ablution water. Then he said: Why should I perform ablution. Shall I pray to perform ablution, or did I pray to perform ablution."
"2559","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas who said: I slept with my maternal aunt Maymunah bint al-Harith. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rose at night and relieved himself, then came and washed his face and his hands, then slept. Then he rose at night and came to the waterskin and loosened its tie and performed ablution between two ablutions, not excessive yet thorough. Then he stood praying. And I stretched myself disliking that he see me, I was watching him meaning I observe him. Then I stood and did as he did. So I stood at his left, and he took what is next to my ear until he turned me so I was at his right while he was praying. His prayer reached thirteen rakahs including the two rakahs of Fajr. Then he reclined and slept until he snored. Then Bilal came and informed him of prayer. So he stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
"2560","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Abd Allah ibn Uthman from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married while he was in ihram, and was cupped while he was in ihram."
"2561","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from al-Ajlah from Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Ibn Abbas that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what Allah wills and you will. Then he said: Have you made me an equal to Allah. Rather what Allah alone wills."
"2562","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, Uthman al-Jazari informed me that he heard Miqsam the freedman of Ibn Abbas reporting from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the House and supplicated in its corners, then went out and prayed two rakahs."
"2563","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, Abd al-Aziz meaning Ibn Rufay narrated to us, he said: One who heard Ibn Abbas informed me, he says: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not descend between Arafat and Jam except to urinate."
"2564","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us from Ayyub from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"2565","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us from Ayyub from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymunah at Sarif while he was in ihram."
"2566","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri informed us from Simak ibn Harb from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that a wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bathed from janabah, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to perform ablution from her leftover. She said: I washed from it. Then he said: Water is not made impure by anything."
"2567","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah and watched how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prays. He stood and urinated then washed his face and his hands then slept. Then he stood and went to the waterskin and loosened its tie, then poured into the basin or the bowl and bent his hand over it, then performed a good ablution between two ablutions. Then he stood praying. So I came and stood at his left, and he took me and placed me at his right. The prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached thirteen rakahs. He said: Then he slept until he snored, and we used to know him when he slept by his snoring. Then he went out to prayer and prayed, and began saying in his prayer or in his prostration: O Allah place in my heart light, and in my hearing light, and in my sight light, and at my right light, and at my left light, and before me light, and behind me light, and above me light, and below me light, and make me light. Shubah said: Or he said: Make for me light. He said: And Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas that he slept lying."
"2568","Rawh narrated to us, Saeed and Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say at distress: There is no god but Allah the Mighty the Forbearing, there is no god but Allah Lord of the Mighty Throne, there is no god but Allah Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth Lord of the Noble Throne."
"2569","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Umar ibn Harmalah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: My maternal aunt Umm Hufayd gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ghee and milk and lizards. As for the lizards, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spat toward them. Khalid ibn al-Walid said to him: You found it disgusting O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes, or: Indeed. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took the milk and drank from it, then he said to Ibn Abbas while he was at his right: Indeed the drink is yours, but will you permit that I give your uncle to drink. Ibn Abbas said: I said: No, by Allah, I will not prefer anyone over your leftover. He said: So I took it and drank then gave him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know no drink that suffices instead of food except milk. Whoever drinks it among you let him say: O Allah bless us in it and increase us from it. And whoever eats food let him say: O Allah bless us in it and feed us better than it."
"2570","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Saeed ibn al-Huwayrith narrated to us from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to relieve himself, then returned and a bone with meat was brought, and he did not perform ablution and ate from it. And Amr added upon me in this hadith from Saeed ibn al-Huwayrith who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you did not perform ablution. He said: I did not intend prayer to perform ablution."
"2571","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found these hadiths in the book of my father in his handwriting: Saeed ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Rashdin ibn Kurayb narrated to us from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he drank would breathe twice in the drink. And my father wrote after this hadith: I do not think Abd Allah heard this hadith."
"2572","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi al-Asari narrated to me, he said: Jabalah ibn Atiyah narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Abbas who said: I stayed as a guest with Maymunah the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who is my maternal aunt, on a night when she does not pray. She took a cloak and folded it and cast a cushion upon it, then threw another cloak over it, then entered it. And she spread for me a mat beside her, and I pillowed with her upon her pillow. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came after he had prayed the last Isha. So he took a rag and wrapped his waist with it and cast his garment and entered with her in her quilt. And he slept until when it was the end of the night he rose to a hanging waterskin and shook it. I intended to stand to pour upon him, but I disliked that he see that I was awake. He said: So he performed ablution, then came to the bed and took his two garments and cast the rag. Then he came to the mosque and stood therein praying. And I stood to the waterskin and performed ablution, then I came to the mosque and stood at his left. So he took me and placed me at his right. So he prayed and I prayed with him thirteen rakahs. Then he sat and I sat beside him. So he placed his elbow beside him and inclined his cheek to my cheek until I heard the breath of the sleeper. While I was thus Bilal came and said: Prayer O Messenger of Allah. So he went to the mosque and I followed him. So he stood praying the two rakahs of Fajr, and Bilal began the iqamah."
"2573","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Tamimi from Ibn Abbas, and he mentioned something, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used the siwak much. He said: Until we thought, or we saw, that revelation would descend upon him about it."
"2574","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed then preached, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, at Eid without adhan nor iqamah. My father said: Abd Allah heard it."
"2575","Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: I found this hadith in the book of my father: Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Safar from Saeed ibn Shufay from Ibn Abbas that they began asking him about prayer in travel, so Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he left his family would not exceed two rakahs until he returned."
"2576","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two qiblas are not valid in one city, nor is jizyah upon Muslims."
"2577","Jarir narrated to us, he also raised it, he said: Two qiblas are not valid in a land, and there is no jizyah upon a Muslim."
"2578","al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Rashdin from his father from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to breathe twice in the vessel."
"2579","al-Hakam narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us from Khusayf from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited the Talbiyah after the prayer."
"2580","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw my Lord Blessed and Exalted. And I heard this hadith from my father, he dictated it to me in another place."
"2581","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married while he was in ihram."
"2582","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he prayed seven together and eight together."
"2583","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Zayd reporting from Ibn Abbas that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, preaching at Arafat, and he said: Whoever does not find an izar let him wear trousers, and whoever does not find two sandals let him wear two khuffs."
"2584","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus reporting from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2585","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus reporting from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling food until he takes full possession of it, or it is taken possession of. And Ibn Abbas said: I consider all sales in its position."
"2586","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit who said: I heard Saeed ibn Jubayr reporting from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Do not take anything containing a soul as a target."
"2587","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah and Ibn Ata that they heard Ata reporting from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"2588","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2589","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while in ihram fasting."
"2590","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus reporting from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2591","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us from Qatadah and Ayyub from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that a man was thrown from his mount and died while he was in ihram, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that they wash him with water and lote leaves, and shroud him in his two garments, and not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah. And Ayyub said: With matted hair."
"2592","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Saeed narrated to us from Yala ibn Hakim from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that he saw no harm in a man marrying while he is in ihram, and he says: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymunah bint al-Harith at a water called Sarif while he was in ihram. When the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, completed his Hajj he came until he was at that water and consummated with her."
"2593","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ayyub from Ata that he testified concerning Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas testified concerning the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he prayed on a day of Eid then preached then came to the women and ordered them with charity, so they began casting."
"2594","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while fasting."
"2595","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us from Shubah from al-Hakam from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning one who comes to his wife while she is menstruating: He gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"2596","Hushaym narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones and not to gather hair nor garment."
"2597","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: If one of you, or: If one of them, when he comes to his wife says: O Allah keep Satan from me and keep Satan from what You provide me, then there is a child between them except Satan will not dominate him, or: Satan will not harm him."
"2598","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah from Tawus and Ata and Mujahid from Rafi ibn Khadij who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us and forbade us a matter that was beneficial to us, and the command of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is better for us than what he forbade us. He said: Whoever has land let him cultivate it, or let him leave it, or let him grant it. He said: So I mentioned that to Tawus, and he considered Ibn Abbas among their most knowledgeable. He said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only said: For one to grant his brother his land is better for him. Shubah said: Abd al-Malik used to combine these: Tawus and Ata and Mujahid, and the one he reported from was Mujahid. Shubah said: As though he is the master of the hadith."
"2599","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Tawus, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about this verse: Say I do not ask you for reward except love for kinship. He said: Saeed ibn Jubayr said: The kinship of the family of Muhammad. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: You hastened. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, there was no clan of Quraysh except that he had kinship among them. Then he said: Except that you maintain what is between me and you of kinship."
"2600","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bishr reporting that he heard Saeed ibn Jubayr reporting that he heard Ibn Abbas reporting that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in ihram and fell from his she-camel which killed him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that he be washed with water and lote leaves and shrouded in two garments, and said: Do not touch him with perfume outside his head. Shubah said: Then he narrated it to me after that and said: Outside his head or his face, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with matted hair."
"2601","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when I was ten years old and I was circumcised and I had recited al-Muhkam of the Quran He said So I said to Abu Bishr What is al-Muhkam He said Al-Mufassal"
"2602","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying so I stood on his left and he took me and placed me on his right"
"2603","He said Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to me Shu'bah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhadah from Abu Salih from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the women who visit graves and those who take mosques and lamps over them"
"2604","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Salih freedman of al-Taw'amah he said I heard Ibn Abbas saying A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about something concerning prayer so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him Run water between the fingers of your hands and your feet meaning the completion of ablution And among what he said to him was When you bow place your palms upon your knees until you are at rest and al-Hashimi once said until you both rest and when you prostrate press your forehead firmly upon the ground until you feel the bulk of the ground"
"2605","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us he said Abdullah informed us and Attab said Abdullah narrated to us he said Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri he said Ubaydullah narrated to me from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to let his hair hang down and the polytheists used to part their heads and the People of the Book used to let their hair hang down and he used to love agreeing with the People of the Book in what he had not been commanded concerning with anything then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parted his head"
"2606","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us Abdullah narrated to us he said Husayn ibn Abdullah informed us from Ikrimah that a man asked Ibn Abbas about the nabidh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he said He used to drink in the daytime what was made in the night and drink in the night what was made in the daytime"
"2607","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us he said Abdullah informed us he said Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas informed us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh in al-naqir and al-dubba and al-muzaffat and he said Do not drink except in a skin with a tie So they made camel hides then made for them necks from sheep hides and that reached him so he said Do not drink except in what its top is tied shut"
"2608","He said Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to me Abdullah informed us and Attab said Abdullah narrated to us Asim informed us from al-Sha'bi that Ibn Abbas narrated to him he said I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Zamzam to drink so he drank while standing"
"2609","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to me Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us from his father from Ubaydullah from Ibn Abbas that he said Allah Blessed and Exalted did not aid in a place as He aided on the day of Uhud He said So we denied that So Ibn Abbas said Between me and whoever denies that is the Book of Allah Blessed and Exalted Allah Almighty says concerning the day of Uhud And Allah fulfilled His promise to you when you slew them by His leave Ibn Abbas says al-hass is killing until when you failed to His saying And He pardoned you and Allah is bountiful to the believers And He only meant by this the archers and that is that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stationed them in a place then said Guard our backs if you see us killed do not aid us and if you see us plunder do not share with us So when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) plundered and they overran the camp of the polytheists the archers all poured and entered the camp looting and the ranks of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had met so they are thus and he interlaced between the fingers of his hands and they mingled So when the archers left that gap they were in the horsemen entered from that place upon the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so they struck one another and mingled and many Muslims were killed And there was for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions the first of the day until seven or nine of the standard-bearers of the polytheists were killed and the Muslims wheeled a wheeling toward the mountain and they did not reach where people say the cave they were only under al-Mihras And Satan cried Muhammad is killed so there was no doubt in it that it was true So we remained thus not doubting he was killed until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose between al-Sadayn we knew him by his leaning when he walked He said So we rejoiced until as if what befell us did not befall us He said So he ascended toward us saying Allah's anger intensified upon a people who bloodied the face of His Messenger He said And he says another time O Allah they have no right to overcome us until he ended to us so he stayed an hour and lo Abu Sufyan crying at the foot of the mountain Exalt Hubal twice meaning his god Where is the son of Abu Kabshah where is the son of Abu Quhafah where is the son of al-Khattab So Umar said O Messenger of Allah shall I not answer him He said Yes So when he said Exalt Hubal Umar said Allah is higher and greater He said So Abu Sufyan said O son of al-Khattab it has gladdened its eye so turn away from it So he said Where is the son of Abu Kabshah where is the son of Abu Quhafah where is the son of al-Khattab So Umar said This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this is Abu Bakr and here I am Umar He said So Abu Sufyan said A day for the day of Badr days alternate and war is sundry He said So Umar said Not equal our slain in Paradise and your slain in Fire He said You claim that then we failed and lost Then Abu Sufyan said You will find among your slain mutilation and that was not by the view of our chiefs He said Then the zeal of ignorance overtook him He said So he said It was that and we did not dislike it"
"2610","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us he said Abdullah meaning al-Umari informed us from Muhammad ibn Uqbah from his brother Ibrahim ibn Uqbah from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas that a woman brought out a boy of hers and said O Messenger of Allah is there Hajj for this one So he said Yes and for you is reward"
"2611","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ibn Abbas and Aishah they both said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Mina by night"
"2612","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Aishah and Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the tawaf of the Day of Sacrifice until night"
"2613","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from Abu Yahya from Ibn Abbas that two men disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the claimant for proof and he had no proof so he made the defendant swear and he swore by Allah besides whom there is no god so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said You have sworn but Allah has forgiven you for your sincere saying There is no god but Allah"
"2614","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us Abdullah informed us Ibn Lahiah informed us from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah from Hanash from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out and urinate then wipe with dust so I would say O Messenger of Allah water is near from you so he would say And what makes me know perhaps I will not reach it"
"2615","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us he said Abdullah informed us he said al-Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas informed us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Do not fast the day of Friday alone"
"2616","Attab narrated to us Abdullah narrated to us he said Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri he said Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah narrated to me from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most generous of people and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril met him and Jibril used to meet him in every night of Ramadan and review the Quran with him He said So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more generous with good than the sent wind"
"2617","Attab narrated to us Abdullah narrated to us he said Mamar informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that al-Aslami came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed adultery so he said Perhaps you kissed or touched or looked"
"2618","Attab narrated to us Abdullah narrated to us he said Mamar informed us from Amr ibn Abdullah from Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said Do not eat al-sharitah for it is the slaughter of Satan"
"2619","Attab narrated to us Abdullah narrated to us he said Shubah informed us from al-Hakam from Maymun ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas that he forbade every fanged beast from predators and taloned bird He said al-Hakam raised it Shubah said And I dislike narrating its raising He said And Ghaylan and al-Hajjaj narrated to me from Maymun ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas he did not raise it"
"2620","Attab narrated to us he said Abdullah informed us Sufyan informed us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abu Qatadah while he was with a man he had killed so he said Leave him and his spoils"
"2621","Attab narrated to us he said Abu Hamzah informed us from Yazid al-Nahwi from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made equal between teeth and fingers in blood-money"
"2622","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Bukayr ibn Abdullah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab he said I heard Ibn Abbas saying I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying The likeness of one who gives charity then returns in his charity is like one who vomits then eats his vomit"
"2623","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Harrani narrated to us he said Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us he said I heard my father narrating from Abu al-Jawza from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Atonement for sin is remorse And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said If you did not sin Allah Almighty would bring a people who sin so that He forgives them"
"2624","Ali ibn al-Hasan meaning Ibn Shaqiq narrated to us he said Abu Hamzah informed us he said Yazid al-Nahwi narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Teeth are equal and fingers are equal"
"2625","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik and Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad said Ubaydullah meaning Ibn Amr narrated to us from Abd al-Karim from Qays ibn Habtar from Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said Allah has forbidden upon you wine and gambling and al-kubah and he said Every intoxicant is forbidden"
"2626","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us Ubaydullah narrated to us from Abd al-Karim from Qays ibn Habtar that Ibn Abbas said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of wine and the dowry of the prostitute and the price of the dog and he said When its owner comes seeking its price fill his palms with dust"
"2627","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us he said Ibn Lahiah narrated to us from Ibn Hubayrah that Maymun al-Makki informed him that he saw Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr praying with them gesturing with his palms when he stands and when he bows and when he prostrates and when he rises for standing so he stands and gestures with his hands He said So I went to Ibn Abbas and said I saw Ibn al-Zubayr praying a prayer I never saw anyone pray and I described to him this gesturing so he said If you wish to look at the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) follow the prayer of Ibn al-Zubayr"
"2628","Dawud ibn Mihran narrated to us Dawud meaning al-Attar narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid from Ibn Abbas he said A man said How much suffices me for ablution He said A mudd He said How much suffices me for washing He said A sa So the man said It does not suffice me He said No mother for you it sufficed one better than you the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"2629","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out covering himself with a garment so he said O people people increase and the Ansar decrease so whoever of you is put in charge of a matter in which he benefits someone let him accept from their good-doer and overlook their wrongdoer"
"2630","Affan narrated to us Shubah narrated to us he said al-Hakam ibn Utaybah informed me he said I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah al-Laythi gave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram at Qudayd the hind part of an ass so he returned it while it dripped blood"
"2631","Affan narrated to us he said Shubah from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it"
"2632","Affan narrated to us Shubah narrated to us he said Qatadah informed me he said I heard Musa ibn Salamah he said I asked Ibn Abbas he said I said I am in Makkah so how do I pray He said Two rakahs the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"2633","Bahz and Affan said Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah Affan said Qatadah narrated to us from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was offered the daughter of Hamzah so he said She is the daughter of my brother through nursing and what is forbidden by kinship is forbidden by nursing Affan said And she is not lawful to me"
"2634","Affan narrated to us Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I saw my Lord Blessed and Exalted"
"2635","Affan narrated to us Abd al-Wahid narrated to us al-Hajjaj narrated to us al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to us from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamarat when the sun declined"
"2636","Affan narrated to us Hammad informed us he said Thabit informed us from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The lightest of the people of Fire in punishment is Abu Talib wearing two sandals of fire from which his brain boils"
"2637","He said Affan narrated to us Hammam narrated to us he said Qatadah informed us from Musa ibn Salamah that he asked Ibn Abbas about prayer at al-Batha when he does not catch prayer with the imam He said Two rakahs the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"2638","Affan narrated to us Hammam narrated to us Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered then shaved"
"2639","Affan narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us Ayyub narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions came and the fever of Yathrib had weakened them He said So the polytheists said There comes to you a people whom fever has weakened He said So Allah informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that so he commanded his companions to trot and the polytheists sat at the side of al-Hijr looking at them so they trotted and walked between the two corners He said So the polytheists said These are those whom you claim fever weakened these are stronger than such and such they mentioned their saying Ibn Abbas said Nothing prevented him from commanding them to trot all the circuits except mercy for them And I heard Hammad narrating it from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas or from Abdullah from Sa'id ibn Jubayr no doubt in it from him"
"2640","Affan narrated to us Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us Yunus narrated to us from Ammar freedman of Banu Hashim he said I asked Ibn Abbas How old was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day he died He said You are not one I would think in his people would be unaware of that He said I said I asked and was disagreed with so I wished to know your saying in it He said Do you count I said Yes He said Hold forty he was sent at it and fifteen he stayed in Makkah safe and fearing and ten as emigrant in Madinah"
"2641","Affan narrated to us Wuhayb narrated to us Ayyub narrated to us from a man he said I heard Ibn Abbas saying The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions came on the morning of the fourth calling talbiyah for Hajj so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to make it Umrah except one who had the sacrificial animal with him He said So shirts were worn and incense burners spread scent and women were married"
"2642","Affan narrated to us Sulayman ibn Kathir Abu Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us he said I heard Ibn Shihab narrating from Abu Sinan from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said O people Hajj has been prescribed upon you He said So al-Aqra ibn Habis stood and said Every year O Messenger of Allah So he said If I said it it would become obligatory and if it became obligatory you would not act by it and you would not be able to act by it Hajj is once so whoever adds it is voluntary"
"2643","Affan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah will surely raise the Stone on the Day of Resurrection having two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks bearing witness by it for whoever touched it in truth"
"2644","Affan narrated to us Abd al-Warith narrated to us Ayyub narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr from his father from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and saw the Jews fasting the day of Ashura so he said What is this day which you fast They said This is a righteous day this is a day in which Allah saved the Children of Israel from their enemy He said So Musa fasted it He said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I am more deserving of Musa than you He said So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted it and commanded fasting it"
"2645","Affan narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from memory from Ayyub from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade habal al-habalah"
"2646","Affan narrated to us Hammam narrated to us Qatadah narrated to us from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said One who returns in his gift is like one who returns in his vomit Qatadah said And I do not know vomit except as forbidden"
"2647","Affan narrated to us Wuhayb narrated to us Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us from his father he said We used to say when we were boys One who returns in his gift is like a dog that vomits then returns in its vomit and we did not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a parable in that until Ibn Abbas narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said One who returns in his gift is like a dog that vomits then returns in its vomit"
"2648","Affan narrated to us Wuhayb narrated to us Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked in the Farewell Hajj so he said O Messenger of Allah I shaved before I slaughtered He said So he gestured with his hand and said No harm And a man said O Messenger of Allah I slaughtered before I stoned He said So he gestured with his hand and said No harm He said So he was not asked that day about anything of advancing and delaying except he gestured with his hand and said No harm"
"2649","Affan narrated to us Hammam narrated to us Abu Jamrah informed us he said I used to push people away from Ibn Abbas so I was held back days so he said What held you back I said Fever He said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Fever is from the heat of Hell so cool it with Zamzam water"
"2650","Affan narrated to us Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-dubba and al-hantam and al-muzaffat"
"2651","Affan narrated to us Abu Awanah narrated to us he said Abu Hamzah informed us he said I heard Ibn Abbas saying I was a boy running with boys He said So I turned and lo the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was behind me coming so I said The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come only to me He said So I ran until I hid behind a house door He said So I did not feel until he took me He said So he took by my nape and pushed me a push He said Go call Muawiyah for me and he was his scribe He said So I ran and said Answer the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for he has a need"
"2652","Affan narrated to us Abu Awanah narrated to us from Mansur from Mujahid from Tawus from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Madinah to Makkah so he fasted until he reached Usfan then he called for water and raised it to his hand to show people so he broke fast until he came to Makkah and that was in Ramadan And Ibn Abbas used to say The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted and broke fast so whoever wishes fasts and whoever wishes breaks fast"
"2653","Affan narrated to us Shubah narrated to us he said Amr informed me he said I heard Yahya ibn al-Jazzar from Ibn Abbas that a kid wanted to pass before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying so he kept warding it off"
"2654","Affan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Yusuf ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said There is none from the children of Adam except he has erred or intended a fault except Yahya ibn Zakariyya And it is not fitting for anyone to say I am better than Yunus ibn Matta"
"2655","Affan narrated to us Hammad informed us Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Yusuf ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and his rider behind him was Usamah so we gave him to drink from this nabidh meaning the nabidh of the watering place so he drank from it and said You did well thus do"
"2656","Affan narrated to us Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah he said I prayed behind an elder in Makkah so he said takbir in noon prayer twenty-two takbirs so I came to Ibn Abbas and said I prayed behind a foolish elder so he said takbir in noon prayer twenty-two takbirs He said May your mother lose you that is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"2657","Affan narrated to us Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us from his father from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Give the fixed shares to their people so what remains is for the nearest male kin"
"2658","Abdullah narrated to us and with this isnad thus my father said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones the forehead then he pointed with his hand to his nose and the two hands and the two knees and the ends of the two feet and not to tuck garments nor hair"
"2659","Abdullah said and with this isnad he said thus my father said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cupped and gave the cupper his wage and used snuff"
"2660","Affan narrated to us Aban al-Attar narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The mukatab is paid for what is freed of him by the reckoning of a free man and what remains enslaved of him by the reckoning of a slave"
"2661","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us from Muhammad meaning Ibn Ishaq from Husayn from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said There were in Madinah two men digging graves Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah digging for the people of Makkah and Abu Talhah digging for the Ansar and making a lahd for them He said So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died al-Abbas sent two men to them and said O Allah choose for Thy Prophet So they found Abu Talhah and did not find Abu Ubaydah so he dug for him and made a lahd"
"2662","Hasan narrated to us Abu Waki narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Tamimi from Ibn Abbas he said I stood behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so I saw the whiteness of his armpits while he was prostrating"
"2663","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us Sharik narrated to us from Simak from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said Upon every Muslim is a Hajj and if I said every year it would be"
"2664","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us Abd al-Wahid meaning Ibn Ziyad narrated to us Layth narrated to us from Tawus from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoyed tamattu until he died and Abu Bakr until he died and Umar until he died and Uthman may Allah be pleased with them until he died and the first who forbade it was Muawiyah Ibn Abbas said So I wondered at him and he had narrated to me that he trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a notched blade"
"2665","Yunus and Hujayn narrated to me they said Layth ibn Sad narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Tawus from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us the Quran so he used to say Greetings blessings prayers good words to Allah Peace upon you Hujayn said Peace upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah"
"2666","Yunus narrated to us Layth narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cupped while in ihram"
"2667","Yunus narrated to us al-Bara meaning Ibn Abdullah al-Ghanawi narrated to us from Abu Nadrah he said Ibn Abbas was upon the pulpit of the people of Basrah so I heard him saying The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge at the end of his prayer from four saying I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave and I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of Fire and I seek refuge in Allah from trials what is apparent of them and what is hidden and I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the one-eyed liar"
"2668","Yunus narrated to us Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us from Ilba from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew in the earth four lines he said Do you know what this is So they said Allah and His Messenger know best So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid and Fatimah bint Muhammad and Asiyah bint Muzahim wife of Pharaoh and Maryam daughter of Imran may Allah be pleased with them all"
"2669","Yunus narrated to us Layth narrated to us from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj from Hanash al-Sanani from Abdullah ibn Abbas that he narrated to him that he rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him O boy I teach you words Guard Allah He guards you guard Allah you find Him before you and when you ask ask Allah and when you seek help seek help in Allah and know that the nation if they gathered to benefit you would not benefit you except with something Allah has written for you and if they gathered to harm you would not harm you except with something Allah has written against you the pens are lifted and the pages are dried"
"2670","Abu Sa'id narrated to us Wuhayb narrated to us Ibn Tawus narrated to us from his father from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cupped and gave the cupper his wage and used snuff"
"2671","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to me he said my father narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin and from al-mujaththamah and from the milk of al-jallalah"
"2672","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj he said Ata informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said When one of you eats food let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked Abu al-Zubayr said I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying that I heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and let him not lift the dish until he licks it or has it licked for the last of the food has blessing in it"
"2673","Hasan meaning Ibn Musa narrated to us Ibn Lahiah narrated to us Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the eclipse so I did not hear from him in it a letter of the Quran"
"2674","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us Abdullah informed us he said Ibn Lahiah informed us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the prayer of the lunar eclipse so I did not hear from him in it a single letter"
"2675","Hasan narrated to us Abu Awanah al-Waddah informed us from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Fear narrating from me except what you know for whoever lies upon me deliberately let him take his seat in Fire"
"2676","Hasan narrated to us Shayban narrated to us from Layth from Tawus from Ibn Abbas that he said When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was attended he said Bring me a shoulder blade I write for you in it a writing after which no two men among you disagree after me He said So the people advanced in their clamor so the woman said Woe to you the covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"2677","Hasan narrated to us Ibn Lahiah narrated to us Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us from Hanash ibn Abdullah that Ibn Abbas said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said In the urine of camels and their milk is healing for those whose stomachs are sick"
"2678","Surayj narrated to us Hushaym narrated to us Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us from Barakah ibn al-Uryan al-Mujashii he said I heard Ibn Abbas narrating he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah cursed the Jews fats were forbidden upon them so they sold them and ate their prices and Allah Almighty when He forbids eating a thing forbids its price"
"2679","Hasan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar that Ibn Abbas said I was with my father at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with him was a man confiding with him so he was as if turning away from my father so we went out from him so my father said to me O my son did you not see my cousin as if turning away from me So I said O father there was with him a man confiding with him He said So we returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so my father said O Messenger of Allah I said to Abdullah such and such so he informed me that there was with you a man confiding with you so was there with you anyone So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said And did you see him O Abdullah He said I said Yes He said So that was Jibril and he is who busied me from you"
"2680","Hasan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah fifteen years eight or seven years seeing the light and hearing the voice and eight or seven being revealed to and stayed in Madinah ten"
"2681","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Duwayd Ismail ibn Thawban narrated to me from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The eye is truth the eye is truth it brings down al-haliq"
"2682","Abdullah narrated to me my father narrated to me Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us my father narrated to us he said I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The best of companions are four and the best of detachments four hundred and the best of armies four thousand and twelve thousand are not defeated from fewness"
"2683","Yunus narrated to us Abd al-Wahid narrated to us Yahya ibn Abdullah narrated to us he said Salim ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us he said A man came to Ibn Abbas and said O Ibn Abbas what think you of a man who killed a believer He said So Ibn Abbas said His recompense is Hell abiding in it to the end of the verse He said So he said O Ibn Abbas what think you if he repented and believed and did righteous He said May his mother lose him and whence repentance for him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The slain comes on the Day of Resurrection hanging his head by his right or he said by his left holding his companion with his other hand his jugulars spurting blood before the Throne of the Merciful so he says Lord ask this one for what he killed me"
"2684","Yunus narrated to us Abd al-Wahid narrated to us Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us he said Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrated to us he said A man invited us and brought a tray upon it thirteen lizards He said And that was supper so eater and leaver So in the morning we went to Ibn Abbas and asked him and his companions spoke much in that until some of them said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I do not eat it nor forbid it He said So Ibn Abbas said Evil what you said the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only sent making lawful and making unlawful Then he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Maymunah and with him al-Fadl ibn Abbas and Khalid ibn al-Walid and a woman so a tray was brought upon it bread and lizard meat He said So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to take Maymunah said to him It is O Messenger of Allah lizard meat so he withheld his hand and said It is meat I never ate but eat He said So al-Fadl ibn Abbas and Khalid ibn al-Walid and the woman ate He said And Maymunah said I do not eat from food from which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not eat"
"2685","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us Jarir ibn Hazim informed us from Qays ibn Sad from Yazid ibn Hurmuz that Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about the share of kinsmen for whom it is and about the orphan when his orphanhood ends and about the woman and the slave attending spoils and about killing children of polytheists So Ibn Abbas said Were it not that I turn him back from something he falls in I would not answer him And he wrote to him You wrote to me asking about the share of kinsmen for whom it is and we used to see it for the kin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so our people denied that to us And about the orphan when his orphanhood ends he said When he dreams or good is perceived from him And about the woman and the slave attending spoils so they have nothing but they are given a small gift and given And about killing children of polytheists the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not kill them and you do not kill them except you know of them what al-Khidr knew of the boy when he killed him"
"2686","Yunus narrated to us Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us Ayyub narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions came to Makkah and the fever of Yathrib had weakened them so the polytheists said There has come to you a people whom the fever of Yathrib weakened and they met evil from it so the polytheists sat from the side that follows al-Hijr so Allah informed His Prophet of what they said so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to trot the three circuits so the polytheists see their strength He said So they trotted three circuits and he commanded them to walk between the two corners where the polytheists did not see them And Ibn Abbas said Nothing prevented the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from commanding them to trot all the circuits except mercy for them So the polytheists said These whom you claimed fever weakened these are stronger than such and such"
"2687","Yunus narrated to us Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn Abbas that a Bedouin gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift so he rewarded him for it He said Are you pleased He said No He said So he increased him He said Are you pleased He said No He said So he increased him He said Are you pleased He said Yes He said So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I was about to not accept a gift except from a Qurashi or an Ansari or a Thaqafi"
"2688","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions performed Umrah from Jiranah so they trotted around the House three and walked four"
"2689","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Yusuf ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said There is none among people except he has erred or intended a fault except Yahya ibn Zakariyya"
"2690","Hasan and Affan the meaning said Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thabit al-Bunani from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said The lightest of the people of Fire in punishment is Abu Talib in his feet two sandals of fire from which his brain boils"
"2691","Shadhan narrated to us Israil informed us from Simak from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas he said When wine was forbidden people said O Messenger of Allah our companions who died while drinking it So was sent down There is no sin upon those who believed and did righteous in what they tasted He said And when the qiblah was changed people said O Messenger of Allah our companions who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis So was sent down And Allah would not waste your faith"
"2692","Hasan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Nadrah he said Ibn Abbas addressed us upon this pulpit the pulpit of Basrah he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said There was no prophet except he had a supplication he hastened in the world and I hid my supplication as intercession for my nation and I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection no boast and I am the first from whom the earth splits no boast and in my hand is the banner of praise no boast Adam and who is below him under my banner He said And the Day of Resurrection lengthens upon people until some say to some Come with us to Adam father of mankind so he intercedes for us to his Lord let Him judge between us so they come to Adam peace upon him so they say O Adam you whom Allah created with His hand and settled you in His garden and made His angels prostrate to you intercede for us to your Lord let Him judge between us so he says I am not there for you I was expelled from Paradise by my fault and nothing concerns me today except myself but come to Nuh head of prophets so they come to Nuh so they say O Nuh intercede for us to your Lord let Him judge between us so he says I am not there for you I prayed a prayer that drowned the people of earth and nothing concerns me today except myself but come to Ibrahim friend of Allah peace upon him He said So they come to Ibrahim so they say O Ibrahim intercede for us to your Lord let Him judge between us so he says I am not there for you I lied in Islam three lies and nothing concerns me today except myself So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said He only sought by them to defend the religion of Allah his saying I am sick and his saying Rather the eldest of them did this and his saying to his wife She is my sister but come to Musa peace upon him whom Allah chose with His message and His speech so they come to Musa so they say O Musa you whom Allah chose with His message and spoke to you intercede for us to your Lord let Him judge between us so he says I am not there for you I killed a soul without a soul and nothing concerns me today except myself but come to Isa spirit of Allah and His word so they come to Isa so they say O Isa you are the spirit of Allah and His word intercede for us to your Lord let Him judge between us so he says I am not there for you I was taken as god besides Allah and nothing concerns me today except myself Then he said Have you seen if goods were in a vessel sealed upon would what is in the vessel be reached until the seal is broken So they say No So he says Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the seal of prophets he has come today and he has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said So they come to me so they say O Muhammad intercede for us to your Lord let Him judge between us so I say Yes I am for it until Allah permits whom He wills and pleases So when Allah Almighty wills to separate between His creation a caller calls Where is Ahmad and his nation So we are the last the first so we are the last of nations and the first to be reckoned so nations are cleared from our path so we pass radiant white from the trace of ablution and nations say This nation was about to be all prophets He said Then I come to the gate of Paradise so I take the ring of the gate of Paradise so I knock the gate so it is said Who are you So I say Muhammad so it is opened for me so I see my Lord Almighty upon His chair or His couch so I fall to Him prostrating and I praise Him with praises none before me praised Him with nor after me praises Him with so it is said Raise your head and speak you are heard and ask you are given and intercede you are granted intercession He said So I raise my head so I say O Lord my nation my nation So it is said to me Bring out from Fire whoever was in his heart the weight of such and such so I bring them out Then I return so I fall prostrating and I praise Him with praises none before me praised Him with nor after me praises Him with so it is said to me Raise your head and speak you are heard and ask you are given and intercede you are granted intercession So I raise my head so I say O Lord my nation my nation So it is said Bring out from Fire whoever was in his heart the weight of such and such so I bring them out He said And he said in the third likewise also"
"2693","Hasan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thabit al-Bunani from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it that he said in the first Whoever was in his heart the weight of a barley grain of faith and the second a wheat grain and the third an atom"
"2694","Hasan narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Yusuf ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Jibril peace upon him said to me Prayer has been made beloved to you so take from it what you wish"
"2695","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us Sharik narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from Abu Yahya al-Araj from Ibn Abbas he said Two men disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so the oath fell upon one of them so he swore by Allah besides whom there is no god he has nothing with him He said So Jibril descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said He lies he has with him his right so he commanded him to give him his right and atonement for his oath is his knowing that there is no god but Allah or his testifying"
"2696","Hasan narrated to us Shayban narrated to us from Yahya he said and Abu Salamah informed me from Aishah and Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah ten years with the Quran descending upon him and in Madinah ten"
"2697","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us Israil narrated to us from Uthman meaning Ibn al-Mughirah from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I saw Isa son of Maryam and Musa and Ibrahim As for Isa red curly broad-chested And as for Musa he is corpulent They said to him And Ibrahim He said Look to your companion meaning himself"
"2698","Hasan narrated to us Zuhayr narrated to us he said Qabus ibn Abi Zabyan narrated to us that his father narrated to him from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said Zuhayr no doubt in it he said Good guidance and good demeanor and moderation are a part of twenty-five parts of prophethood"
"2699","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us Zuhayr and Jafar meaning al-Ahmar narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Good demeanor so he mentioned like it"
"2700","Aswad narrated to us Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us from al-Amash from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Mina five prayers"
"2701","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu al-Muhayyah Yahya ibn Yala al-Taymi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr on the day of Tarwiyah at Mina and prayed the dawn prayer on the day of Arafah there."
"2702","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Jad Abu Uthman, he said: I heard Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrating from Ibn Abbas, reporting it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever sees something he dislikes from his commander, let him be patient, for there is no one who parts from the community by a span and then dies except that he dies a death of ignorance."
"2703","Hasan narrated to us, Yaqub, meaning al-Qummi, narrated to us, from Jafar, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: And what has ruined you. He said: I turned my saddle last night. He said: Then he gave him no reply. He said: Then Allah revealed to His Messenger this verse: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish. Come from the front and from behind, and avoid the anus and menstruation."
"2704","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to one of his daughters while she was in the throes of death, so he bent over her and did not raise his head until she had passed away. He said: Then he raised his head and said: Praise be to Allah. The believer is in good: his soul is taken from between his sides while he is praising Allah, Exalted and Majestic."
"2705","Aswad ibn Amir and Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a group of the Ansar who had set up a pigeon as a target and were shooting at it, so he said: Do not take anything that has a soul as a target."
"2706","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted me behind him, with Qutham in front of him."
"2707","Surayj and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Abu Asim al-Ghanawi, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ran briskly around the House and that it is a sunnah. He said: They told the truth and they lied. I said: How did they tell the truth and how did they lie. He said: They told the truth: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ran briskly around the House, and they lied: it is not a sunnah. Quraysh said at the time of Hudaybiyah: Leave Muhammad and his companions until they die the death of the naghaf, then when they made peace with him that they would come the next year and stay in Makkah three days, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came while the polytheists were on the side of Quayqian, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: Run briskly around the House three times, and it is not a sunnah. I said: And your people claim that he circumambulated between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel and that it is a sunnah. He said: They told the truth and they lied. I said: How did they tell the truth and lie. He said: They told the truth: he did circumambulate between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel, and they lied: it is not a sunnah. The people would not be pushed away from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor turned away from him, so he circumambulated on a camel so that they could hear his words and their hands could not reach him. I said: And your people claim that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastened between al-Safa and al-Marwah and that it is a sunnah. He said: They told the truth. When Ibrahim was commanded with the rites, Satan confronted him at the place of hastening, so he raced him and Ibrahim outran him. Then Jibril took him to the Aqabah pillar, and a devil confronted him, Yunus said: Satan, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he went away. Then he confronted him at the middle pillar and he pelted him with seven pebbles. He said: He laid him on his forehead, Yunus said: And there he laid him on his forehead, and Ismail wore a white shirt, and he said: O my father, I have no garment to be shrouded in but it, so take it off so that you may shroud me in it, so he set about removing it, then he was called from behind him: O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision. Ibrahim turned and there was a white horned ram with large eyes. Ibn Abbas said: We have seen ourselves selling this kind of ram. He said: Then Jibril took him to the farthest pillar, and Satan confronted him and he pelted him with seven pebbles until he went away. Then Jibril took him to Mina. He said: This is Mina, Yunus said: This is the camping place of the people. Then he brought him to Jam, and said: This is the Sacred Landmark. Then he took him to Arafah. Ibn Abbas said: Do you know why Arafah was named Arafah. I said: No. He said: Jibril said to Ibrahim: Have you recognized, Yunus said: Have you recognized. He said: Yes. Ibn Abbas said: So from there it was named Arafah. Then he said: Do you know how the talbiyah came about. I said: And how was it. He said: When Ibrahim was commanded to proclaim the pilgrimage among the people, the mountains lowered their heads for him and the towns were raised for him, so he proclaimed the pilgrimage among the people."
"2708","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl, then he mentioned it, except that he said: Their hands could not reach him, and he said: And there Ibrahim laid Ismail on his forehead."
"2709","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach them this supplication as he used to teach them a surah of the Quran, to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death."
"2710","He said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood for prayer in the depth of the night would say: O Allah, to You is praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. You are the Truth, Your word is truth, Your promise is truth, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, Hell is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, by You I dispute, and to You I refer judgment, so forgive me what I have done before and what I have done after, what I have concealed and what I have declared. You are the One besides whom there is no god."
"2711","Ishaq, meaning Ibn Isa, narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The sun eclipsed, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with the people with him. He stood a long standing, he said: about the length of Surah al-Baqarah, then he bowed a long bowing, then he rose and stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he prostrated. Then he stood and stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing. Abdullah said: My father said, and in what I read to Abd al-Rahman, he said: Then he stood a long standing, he said: shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he prostrated, then he finished. Then he returned to the hadith of Ishaq: Then he finished while the sun had become clear, and he said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see that, remember Allah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you reach for something in your place, then we saw you hold back. He said: I saw Paradise and took a bunch of grapes from it, and had I taken it you would have eaten from it as long as the world remained. And I saw Hell, and I never saw a sight like today at all, and I saw that most of its people were women. They said: Why, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Because of their ingratitude. It was said: Do they disbelieve in Allah. He said: They are ungrateful to the husband and ungrateful for kindness. If you do good to one of them for a lifetime, then she sees something from you, she says: I never saw any good from you at all."
"2712","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him that Marwan said: Go, O Rafi, to his gatekeeper, to Ibn Abbas, and say: If every man among us who rejoices in what he has been given and loves to be praised for what he did not do is to be punished, we will all be punished. Ibn Abbas said: What have you to do with this. This was only revealed concerning the People of the Book. Then Ibn Abbas recited: And when Allah took the covenant of those who were given the Book: You shall make it clear to the people, this verse. And Ibn Abbas recited: Do not think that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they did not do. And Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked them about something, and they concealed it from him and told him something else, then they left having shown him that they had told him what he asked them about, and sought praise from him for that, and rejoiced in what they had done of concealing from him what he had asked them about."
"2713","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The first to deny was Adam, he said it three times. When Allah created him, He wiped his back and brought forth his offspring and presented them to him, and he saw among them a man shining. He said: O Lord, who is this. He said: Your son Dawud. He said: How long is his life. He said: Sixty. He said: O Lord, add to his life. He said: No, unless you add to him from your own life. So he added forty years from his life. Allah wrote a document against him and had the angels witness it. When He wanted to take his soul, he said: Forty years of my term remain. It was said to him: You gave them to your son Dawud. He said: Then he denied. He said: So Allah, Exalted and Majestic, produced the document and established the proof against him, so he completed for Dawud, peace be upon him, one hundred years, and completed for Adam, peace be upon him, his life of a thousand years."
"2714","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr, meaning al-Nahshali, narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray eight rakahs at night and pray witr with three, and pray two rakahs, then when he grew old he settled on nine and six and three."
"2715","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, he said: One who heard Ibn Abbas informed me, he says: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Beware of the three cursed places. It was said: What are the cursed places, O Messenger of Allah. He said: That one of you sits in a shade that is used for shade, or on a road, or in a pool of water."
"2716","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Layth informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while he was fasting."
"2717","Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated to me that Ibn Abbas narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, taught me to recite in one mode, so I kept asking him for more and he kept giving me more until it reached seven modes."
"2718","Yunus narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of companions are four, the best of detachments are four hundred, and the best of armies are four thousand. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A people will not be overcome from small numbers if they reach twelve thousand."
"2719","Zakariya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man left Khaybar, and two men followed him, with another behind them saying: Go back, go back, until he turned them back. Then he caught up with the first one and said: These two are two devils, and I kept at them until I turned them back. When you come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, convey greetings to him and inform him that we are here gathering our charities, and had they been lawful for him we would have sent them to him. He said: When the man reached Madinah, he informed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and at that point the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade seclusion."
"2720","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"2721","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Muhammad of the family of Amr ibn Uthman, from Fatimah bint Husayn, she said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to stare persistently at lepers."
"2722","Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to me, from Jabalah ibn Atiyah, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the house of one of his wives, he laid his head down and slept, and laughed in his sleep. When he awoke, one of his wives said to him: You laughed in your sleep; what made you laugh. He said: I am amazed at people of my community who will ride this sea facing the terror of the enemy, striving in the path of Allah, and he mentioned much good about them."
"2723","Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to go out on a journey, he would say: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel and grief at the return. O Allah, fold up the land for us and make travel easy for us."
"2724","Affan and Abu Said al-Mana narrated to us, they said: Thabit narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned toward Uhud and said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it would not please me that Uhud be turned into gold for the family of Muhammad to spend in the path of Allah, then I die on the day I die leaving of it two dinars, except two dinars I prepare for a debt, if there is one. Then he died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, neither slave nor servant, and he left his armor pawned with a Jew for thirty sa of barley."
"2725","Husayn ibn Muhammad and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"2726","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"2727","Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Habibah informed me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill the doer and the one to whom it is done in the act of the people of Lut, and the animal, and the one who has intercourse with an animal, and whoever has intercourse with a close unmarriageable kinswoman, kill him."
"2728","Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Habibah informed me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dispatched his armies, he would say: Go out in the name of Allah, fighting in the path of Allah those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not betray, do not steal from the spoils, do not mutilate, do not kill children, nor the dwellers of cloisters."
"2729","Abu al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Habibah informed me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach us against fever and pains: In the name of Allah, the Great. I seek refuge in Allah the Almighty from the evil of a spurting vein and from the evil of the heat of Hell."
"2730","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a bowl of tharid, so he said: Eat from around it and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends in its middle."
"2731","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked on the day of Sacrifice about a man who shaved before stoning, or sacrificed or slaughtered, and the like of this in doing things early or late, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No harm, no harm."
"2732","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whomever you find doing the act of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done."
"2733","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said concerning one who comes to an animal: Kill the doer and the one to whom it is done."
"2734","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man of the Ansar insulted a father of al-Abbas from the time of ignorance, so al-Abbas slapped him. His people came and said: By Allah, we will surely slap him as he slapped him, and they put on weapons. That reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he ascended the minbar and said: O people, which people of the earth are most honored with Allah. They said: You. He said: Al-Abbas is from me and I am from him, so do not revile our dead lest you harm our living. The people came and said: O Messenger of Allah, we seek refuge in Allah from your anger."
"2735","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman, from Mujahid, that the people were circumambulating the House while Ibn Abbas sat with a staff with him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims. Had a drop of zaqqum dripped, it would have embittered the life of the people of the earth, so how about those who have no food but zaqqum."
"2736","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no one among people but has erred or intended a sin, except Yahya ibn Zakariya."
"2737","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fasted a complete month except Ramadan, and when he fasted he would fast until one would say: By Allah, he will not break his fast, and he would break his fast until when he broke it one would say: By Allah, he will not fast."
"2738","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to trim his mustache, and your father Ibrahim before him used to trim his mustache."
"2739","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not boast of your fathers who died in ignorance, for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, what the dung beetle rolls with its nose is better than your fathers who died in ignorance."
"2740","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three."
"2741","Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year. He said: Rather one pilgrimage is upon every person, and had I said yes, every year, it would have been every year."
"2742","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been given five that no prophet before me was given, and I do not say it out of pride. I was sent to all people, the red and the black, and I was aided with terror over a month journey, and spoils were made lawful for me though they were not lawful for anyone before me, and the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification, and I was given intercession, so I deferred it for my community, and it is for whoever does not associate anything with Allah."
"2743","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at Uhud and said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it would not please me that Uhud be gold for the family of Muhammad to spend in the path of Allah, then I die on the day I die with two dinars of it with me, unless I prepare them for a debt. He said: Then he died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, neither slave nor servant, and he left his armor pawned with a Jew for thirty sa of barley."
"2744","Abd al-Samad and Abu Said and Affan narrated to us, they said: Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was on a mat that had marked his side, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, if only you would take a bedding softer than this. He said: What have I to do with the world. My example and the example of the world are only like a rider who traveled on a hot summer day and shaded himself under a tree for an hour of the day, then departed and left it."
"2745","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fought an enemy and did not finish with them until he delayed Asr past its time, and when he saw that he said: O Allah, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire and fill their graves with fire, and the like of that."
"2746","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Thabit narrated to us, from Hilal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against them for a consecutive month in Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr, at the end of every prayer, when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, in the last rakah, supplicating against them, against a clan of Banu Sulaym, against Ril and Dhakwan and Usayyah, with those behind him saying amen. He had sent to them calling them to Islam, and they killed them. Affan said in his hadith, he said: And Ikrimah said: This was the beginning of qunut."
"2747","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, al-Hakam and Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade every predator with fangs and every bird with talons."
"2748","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Buraydah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yamar narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, by You I dispute. I seek refuge in Your might, there is no god but You, from leading me astray. You are the Living who does not die, while jinn and men die."
"2749","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amr ibn Said, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Dimad al-Azdi came to Makkah and saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with boys following him, and said: O Muhammad, I treat madness. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Praise be to Allah. We seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead, and whomever He misleads, none can guide. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He said: Then he said: Repeat these words to me. He said: Then he said: I have heard poetry and divination and soothsaying, and I never heard the like of these words. They have reached the depth of the sea. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. So he became Muslim, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him when he became Muslim: Upon you and upon your people. He said: Then he said: Yes, upon me and upon my people. He said: Then a detachment of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by his people after that, and some of them took something from them, a waterskin or otherwise, and they said: This is from the people of Dimad; return it. He said: So they returned it."
"2750","Abu Jafar al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Husayn ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith came with Umm Habibah bint Abbas and placed her in the lap of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she urinated. Umm al-Fadl snatched her away, then struck between her shoulders, then pulled her away. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give me a cup of water, so he poured it over the place of her urine, then he said: Follow up water in the path of urine."
"2751","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Ziyad informed me that Qazaah, a freedman of Abd al-Qays, informed him that he heard Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: Ibn Abbas said: I prayed beside the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with Aishah behind us praying with us, and I beside the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying with him."
"2752","Aswad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of gharar. Ayyub said: And Yahya explained the sale of gharar. He said: Among gharar is the diver strike, and among the sale of gharar is the runaway slave, and the sale of the stray camel, and among the sale of gharar is what is in the bellies of livestock, and among the sale of gharar is the dust of mines, and among the sale of gharar is what is in the udders of livestock, except by measure."
"2753","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating with his arms spread wide until I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"2754","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The talbiyah of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am, You have no partner, here I am. Praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion, You have no partner."
"2755","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought cheese on a campaign, so he said: Where was this made. They said: In Persia, and we think dead meat is put in it. He said: Pierce it with the knife, mention the name of Allah, and eat. Sharik mentioned it another time and added to it: So they began striking it with sticks."
"2756","Aswad narrated to us, al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in an upper chamber of his, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon you, may Umar enter."
"2757","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When you differ about the road, leave seven cubits, then build. And whoever is asked by his neighbor to rest a beam on his wall, let him allow him."
"2758","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, conquered Makkah and stayed in it seventeen days praying two rakahs."
"2759","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whose slave girl bears him a child, she is freed after his death, or he said: after him."
"2760","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment wrapped around himself, guarding with its excess against the cold of the ground and its heat."
"2761","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and spoke clear speech, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom."
"2762","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The chiefs of Quraysh gathered in the Hijr and pledged by al-Lat and al-Uzza and Manat the third, the other, and Nailah and Isaf that if they saw Muhammad they would rise against him as one man and not leave him until they killed him. His daughter Fatimah, may Allah Exalted be pleased with her, came weeping until she entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: These chiefs of Quraysh have pledged against you; if they see you they will rise against you and kill you, and there is not a man among them but knows his share of your blood. He said: O my daughter, show me ablution water. So he performed ablution, then entered the mosque upon them. When they saw him they said: Here he is, and lowered their gazes, and their chins fell to their chests, and they were transfixed in their seats, and did not raise their gaze to him, and not a man among them rose toward him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came forward until he stood over their heads, then took a handful of dust and said: Disfigured be the faces. Then he pelted them with it, and no man among them was struck by a pebble of that gravel but was killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever."
"2763","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Yazid, that Qays ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to him that Hanash narrated to him that Ibn Abbas narrated to him, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to me: O boy, I will tell you a teaching: Guard Allah and He will guard you. Guard Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pens have been lifted and the books have dried. Had the community come to benefit you with something Allah, Exalted and Majestic, did not write for you, they could not, and had they wished to harm you with something Allah did not write for you, they could not."
"2764","Yahya ibn Ishaq and Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, Yahya said: from al-Araj, and Musa did not say: from al-Araj, from Hanash, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would go out and pass urine, then wipe himself with dust. I would say: O Messenger of Allah, water is near you. He said: I do not know; perhaps I will not reach it."
"2765","Yahya said another time: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he went out and passed urine, then performed dry ablution. It was said to him: Water is near us."
"2766","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah informed us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed five prayers at Mina."
"2767","Aswad narrated to us, Huraym narrated to us, from Layth, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was optimistic and did not take bad omens, and the good name pleased him."
"2768","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that he saw Abdullah ibn al-Harith praying with his head tied up from behind, so he stood behind him and began undoing it, and the other accepted it from him. Then he turned to Ibn Abbas and said: What is with you and my head. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The likeness of this is only like the likeness of one who prays while bound."
"2769","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to me, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Avoid drinking in the hantam, the dubba, and the muzaffat, and drink in the waterskin."
"2770","Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Muslims loved that the Romans defeat Persia because they were People of the Book, and the polytheists loved that Persia defeat the Romans because they were people of idols. The Muslims mentioned that to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: They will indeed be defeated. Abu Bakr mentioned that to them, and they said: Set a term between us and you: if they prevail, you shall have so and so, and if we prevail, we shall have so and so. So he set between them a term of five years, but they did not prevail. Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Why did you not make it, I think he said: less than ten. He said: And Said said: Bid means less than ten. He said: The Romans prevailed after that, and that is His Exalted saying: Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated in the nearest land, and after their defeat they will prevail within a few years. He said: The Romans were defeated afterward, then prevailed afterward. He said: To Allah belongs the command before and after, and on that day the believers will rejoice in the victory of Allah. He said: The believers rejoice in the victory of Allah."
"2771","Husayn narrated to us, Duwayd narrated to us, from Salm ibn Bashir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two believers will meet at the gate of Paradise, a rich believer and a poor believer who were in the world. The poor one will be admitted to Paradise, and the rich one will be detained as long as Allah wills him to be detained, then admitted to Paradise. The poor one will meet him and say: O my brother, what detained you. By Allah, you were detained so long that I feared for you. He will say: O my brother, I was detained after you in a dreadful, hateful detention, and I did not reach you until sweat poured from me such that had a thousand camels come to it, all of them eating salty feed, they would have drunk their fill from it."
"2772","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Amrah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the dubba, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat, and mixing unripe dates with ripe dates. He said: I said: O Ibn Abbas, what about a man who puts his drink in a green jar like a bottle and drinks it overnight. He said: Will you not stop what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade you."
"2773","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Ata, narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came while he had been ill, and circumambulated the House on a camel with a staff with him; whenever he passed a corner he touched it with it. When he finished his circumambulation he made it kneel and prayed two rakahs."
"2774","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let no man touch another man directly, nor a woman another woman."
"2775","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, those who died while drinking wine. Then was revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, to the end of the verse."
"2776","Khalaf narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the qiblah was changed, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis. So Allah revealed: And Allah would never waste your faith."
"2777","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"2778","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid informed us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones: the forehead, and he pointed with his hand to his nose, and the two hands, and the two knees, and the ends of the toes, and not to tuck up clothes nor hair."
"2779","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Bara ibn Abdullah al-Ghanawi of themselves narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating, he said: Ibn Abbas was upon this minbar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek refuge at the end of every prayer from four, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from trials, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the one-eyed liar."
"2780","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever is killed defending against his wrong, he is a martyr."
"2781","Musa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent his letter to Khosrau with a man and ordered him to hand it to the chief of Bahrain. The chief of Bahrain handed it to Khosrau, and when he read it he tore it. He said: I thought Ibn al-Musayyab said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against them that they be torn to utter pieces."
"2782","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I considered the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and saw him spreading his arms wide, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"2783","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Zakariya, narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Uthman, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended at Marr al-Zahran during his umrah, it reached the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Quraysh were saying: They will not rise from emaciation. His companions said: If we slaughtered from our riding animals and ate of their meat and sipped of their broth, we would arrive tomorrow when we enter upon the people with vigor. He said: Do not do it, but gather for me from your provisions. So they gathered for him, and spread the leather mats, and they ate until they turned away full, and each one of them filled his bag. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came forward until he entered the mosque, while Quraysh sat toward the Hijr. He draped his cloak over one shoulder, then said: Let the people see no weakness in you. So he touched the Corner, then entered, until when he was hidden by the Yemeni Corner he walked to the Black Corner. Quraysh said: They are not content with walking; they are leaping like gazelles. He did that for three circuits, and it became a sunnah. Abu al-Tufayl said: And Ibn Abbas informed me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did that in the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"2784","Surayj narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There was a beautiful woman praying behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Some of the people would advance to the first row so as not to see her, and some would hang back until in the last row, then when he bowed he would look from under his armpit. So Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed concerning her: We know those who advance among you, and We know those who lag."
"2785","Surayj narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Hilal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a Jewish woman gave the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a poisoned sheep. He sent to her and said: What made you do what you did. She said: I wished, or I intended: if you are a prophet, Allah will inform you of it, and if you are not a prophet, I will relieve the people of you. He said: And whenever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, felt anything of that, he was cupped. He said: He traveled once, and when he entered ihram he felt something of that, so he was cupped."
"2786","Husayn narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, its highlands and its lowlands, and where cultivation is suitable in Quds, and did not give him the right of a Muslim. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote for him: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani: he gave him the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, its highlands and its lowlands, and where cultivation is suitable in Quds, and did not give him the right of a Muslim."
"2787","Husayn narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Zayd, freedman of Banu al-Dil ibn Bakr ibn Kinanah, narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"2788","Surayj and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions performed umrah from Jiranah, and they ran briskly around the House three times and walked four times."
"2789","Surayj narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ata al-Attar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He should give a dinar in charity, and if he does not find, then half a dinar."
"2790","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Harmalah, informed me, from Kurayb, that Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith sent him to Muawiyah in Sham. He said: I reached Sham and fulfilled her need, and Ramadan began while I was in Sham. We saw the crescent on Friday night, then I reached Madinah at the end of the month. Abdullah ibn Abbas asked me, then mentioned the crescent, and said: When did you see it. I said: We saw it on Friday night. He said: Did you see it yourself. I said: Yes, and the people saw it and fasted, and Muawiyah fasted. He said: But we saw it on Saturday night, so we will keep fasting until we complete thirty or see it. I said: Will you not suffice with the sighting of Muawiyah and his fasting. He said: No, thus the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded."
"2791","Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind informed me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whomever Allah wants good for, He gives him understanding in the religion."
"2792","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, he said: Thawr narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would glance in his prayer right and left without turning his neck."
"2793","Surayj and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions performed umrah from Jiranah, and they draped their cloaks under their armpits. Yunus narrated to us: They placed their cloaks, Yunus said: and cast them over their left shoulders."
"2794","Surayj and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Quraysh said: Muhammad and his companions have been weakened by the fever of Yathrib. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came for his year in which he performed umrah, he said to his companions: Run briskly around the House three times so that the polytheists see your strength. When they ran, Quraysh said: They have not been weakened."
"2795","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril took Ibrahim to the Aqabah pillar, and Satan confronted him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles and he sank down. Then he came to the middle pillar, and Satan confronted him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles and he sank down. Then he came to the farthest pillar, and Satan confronted him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles and he sank down. When Ibrahim wanted to slaughter his son Ishaq, he said to his father: O my father, tie me fast so I do not shake and my blood splashes on you when you slaughter me. So he tied him, and when he took the blade and wanted to slaughter him, he was called from behind him: O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision."
"2796","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Black Stone is from Paradise, and it was whiter than snow until the sins of the people of idolatry blackened it."
"2797","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Stone will surely be raised on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes by which it sees, and a tongue by which it speaks, and it will testify for whoever touched it in truth."
"2798","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, then he mentioned it, except that he said: The Corner will be raised."
"2799","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I have been commanded with the siwak until I thought a Quran or revelation would descend upon me about it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is the speaker of this."
"2800","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, the prostration, and: Has there come upon man a period of time."
"2801","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Shubah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, that Ibn Abbas, when he washed from janabah, would pour with his right hand onto his left and wash it seven times before putting it into the vessel, then he once forgot how many times he poured onto his hand, so he asked me how many times I poured, and I said I do not know, so he said May you have no mother, why do you not know, then he performed wudu as for prayer, then he poured water over his head and his body, he said This is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to purify himself, meaning wash."
"2802","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said When Allah Almighty revealed: And warn your closest kin, he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to al-Safa and climbed it, then called out: O morning cry, so the people gathered to him, some coming to him and some sending his messenger, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, O Banu Fihr, O Banu Luayy, if I told you that horses at the foot of this mountain intended to raid you, would you believe me, they said Yes, he said: Then I am a warner to you before a severe punishment, then Abu Lahab said: Perdition to you all day, did you call us only for this, then Allah Almighty revealed: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab and perish he."
"2803","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas informed me, claiming that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep on the day of sacrifice among his companions and said: Slaughter them for your umrah, for they will suffice you, then Sad ibn Abi Waqqas got a billy goat."
"2804","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Furafisah, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is Abdullah ibn Yazid, and I had seen him on a road and he greeted me when I was a boy, he raised it to Ibn Abbas, or he attributed it to Ibn Abbas, he said: And Hammam ibn Yahya Abu Abdullah the Basran narrated to me, attributing it to Ibn Abbas, and Abdullah ibn Luhayah and Nafi ibn Yazid the two Egyptians narrated to me, from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ibn Abbas, and I do not remember the hadith of some of them from others, that he said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O boy, or O young boy, shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you, so I said Yes, then he said: Guard Allah and He will guard you, guard Allah and you will find Him before you, know Him in ease and He will know you in hardship, and when you ask then ask Allah, and when you seek help then seek help from Allah, the pen has dried with what is to be, so if all creation together intended to benefit you with something Allah did not write for you, they could not do it, and if they intended to harm you with something Allah did not write against you, they could not do it, and know that in patience over what you dislike there is much good, and that victory comes with patience, and that relief comes with distress, and that with hardship comes ease."
"2805","Al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I came, I and a boy from the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, on a donkey, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, he said: So we let it loose grazing in front of us, and it did not interrupt, he said: And two slave girls from the Banu Abd al-Muttalib came racing, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them, and it did not interrupt, and a kid fell, and it did not interrupt."
"2806","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman from among the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from janabah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to bathe from her leftover water, so she said I washed from it, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is not made impure by anything."
"2807","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is not made impure by anything, Abdullah said: My father said in his hadith."
"2808","Waki narrated it to us in al-Musannaf, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Ikrimah, then afterwards he made it from Ibn Abbas."
"2809","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: An umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"2810","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: And Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2811","Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yahya meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said O Abu al-Abbas, I am a man who makes these pictures and fashions these images, so give me a ruling about them, he said Come near me, so he came near him until he placed his hand on his head, he said: I inform you of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every image-maker is in the Fire, for every image he made a soul will be made for him to torment him in Hell, so if you must do it then make trees and what has no soul."
"2812","Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Zafaraniy narrated to us, he said Jafar narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, he said: Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about five matters, then Ibn Abbas said: People claim that Ibn Abbas corresponds with the Haruriyyah, and were it not that I fear concealing my knowledge I would not have written to him, Najdah wrote to him: As for what follows, inform me: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raid with women with him, and did he strike a share for them, and did he kill children, and when does the orphanhood of the orphan end, and inform me about the fifth, to whom does it belong, so Ibn Abbas wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raid with women with him, and they would treat the sick, and he would not strike a share for them, but he would give them gifts from the spoils, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not kill children, and do not kill children unless you know what al-Khidr knew about the boy he killed, so you kill the disbeliever and spare the believer, and you wrote asking me about the orphanhood of the orphan, when it ends, and by my life, a man grows his beard while he is weak in taking care of himself, so when he can take for himself soundly as people take, orphanhood has gone, and as for the fifth, we used to consider it ours, but our people denied it to us."
"2813","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman, from Malik, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makkiy, from Tawus, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to prayer in the middle of the night, would say: O Allah, to You is praise, You are the light of the heavens and the earth and those in them, and to You is praise, You are the sustainer of the heavens and the earth and those in them, and to You is praise, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and those in them, and to You is praise, You are the Truth, and Your word is truth, and Your promise is truth, and meeting You is true, and Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the Hour is true, O Allah, to You I submit, and in You I believe, and upon You I rely, and to You I turn, and by You I dispute, and to You I bring judgment, so forgive me what I have done before and after, and what I concealed and what I declared, You are my God, there is no god but You."
"2814","Abdullah narrated to us, and my father narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zaidah, and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah."
"2815","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among poetry there is wisdom, and among eloquence there is magic."
"2816","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Aishah and Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the tawaf on the day of sacrifice until the night."
"2817","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Amr meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah curses whoever slaughters for other than Allah, Allah curses whoever changes the boundaries of the land, and Allah curses whoever misleads the blind from the path, and Allah curses whoever reviles his father, and Allah curses whoever takes other than his masters as allies, and Allah curses whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, and Allah curses whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, and Allah curses whoever does the deed of the people of Lut."
"2818","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Israil, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into food and drink."
"2819","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No man who believes in Allah and His Messenger hates the Ansar, or: Except that Allah and His Messenger hate him."
"2820","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, the meaning, they said: Awf narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night and I woke in Makkah, I was distressed by my matter and I knew that the people would disbelieve me, so he sat apart grieving, he said: Then the enemy of Allah Abu Jahl passed by and came until he sat to him and said to him mockingly: Was there anything, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Yes, he said What is it, he said I was taken by night tonight, he said To where, he said To Bayt al-Maqdis, he said Then you woke among us, he said Yes, he said: He did not show that he disbelieved him, fearing he would deny the account if he called his people to it, he said: What if I call your people, will you tell them what you told me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Yes, so he said: Come O company of Banu Kab ibn Luayy, he said: So the gatherings rushed to him and they came until they sat to them, he said: Tell your people what you told me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night tonight, they said To where, I said To Bayt al-Maqdis, they said Then you woke among us, he said Yes, he said: Some clapping and some placing his hand on his head in wonder at the lie, as he claimed, they said: Can you describe the mosque to us, and among the people were those who had traveled to that land and seen the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I went on describing, and I kept describing until some of the description became confused to me, he said: So the mosque was brought while I was looking until it was placed before the house of Iqal or Uqayl, and I described it while looking at it, he said: And there was with this a description I did not remember, he said: So the people said: As for the description, by Allah he has got it right."
"2821","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Pharaoh said: I believe that there is no god but the one in whom the Children of Israil believe, he said: Jibril said to me: O Muhammad, if you had seen me when I took mud from the sea and stuffed it into his mouth, fearing that mercy would reach him."
"2822","Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night in which I was taken by night, a pleasant scent came over me, so I said O Jibril, what is this pleasant scent, so he said This is the scent of the hairdresser of the daughter of Pharaoh and her children, he said: I said What is her story, he said: While she was combing the daughter of Pharaoh one day, the comb fell from her hands, so she said In the name of Allah, so the daughter of Pharaoh said to her: My father, she said No, but my Lord and the Lord of your father is Allah, she said Shall I tell him of that, she said Yes, so she told him, so he called her and said O so-and-so, do you have a lord other than me, she said Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah, so he ordered a cow of copper to be heated, then ordered her and her children to be thrown into it, she said to him I have a need to you, he said What is your need, she said I would like you to gather my bones and the bones of my child in one cloth and bury us, he said That is your right upon us, he said: So he ordered her children and they were thrown before her one by one until that reached a nursing infant of hers, and it was as if she hesitated because of him, he said O mother, plunge in, for the punishment of this world is easier than the punishment of the Hereafter, so she plunged in, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Four infants spoke: Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, and the companion of Jurayj, and the witness of Yusuf, and the son of the hairdresser of the daughter of Pharaoh."
"2823","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was taken by night, a pleasant scent passed by him, then he mentioned the like of it."
"2824","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was taken by night, a pleasant scent passed by him, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Who is your Lord, she said My Lord and your Lord is He who is in the heaven, and he did not mention the saying of Ibn Abbas: Four spoke."
"2825","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2826","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Jad Abu Uthman narrated to us, Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to me, narrating it from Ibn Abbas, narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Any man who dislikes something from his commander, let him be patient, for there is no one among the people who leaves the authority a handspan and dies except that he dies a death of ignorance."
"2827","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Jad Abu Uthman informed us, Abu Raja narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever sees something from his commander that he dislikes, then he mentioned the like of it."
"2828","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Jad Abu Uthman informed us, he said Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating it from his Lord Almighty, he said: Allah wrote good deeds and bad deeds, so whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, Allah writes for him with Him a complete good deed, and if he does it, Allah writes it for him ten to seven hundred to many multiples, or to what Allah wills to multiply, and whoever intends a bad deed and does not do it, Allah writes it for him with Him a complete good deed, and if he does it, Allah writes it as one bad deed."
"2829","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman the freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj walking, he said: Allah has no need of the hardship of your sister, let her go out riding and let her expiate for her oath."
"2830","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said Qatadah informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House seven times and ran seven times, and he only ran because he liked to show the people his strength."
"2831","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: He disliked unripe dates alone, and he would say The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the delegation of Abd al-Qays from muzaza, so I fear that unripe dates may be that."
"2832","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and saw the Jews fasting the day of Ashura, so he said to them What is this day that you fast, they said This is a righteous day, this is a day in which Allah saved the Children of Israil from their enemy, so Musa, peace be upon him, fasted it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said I have more right to Musa than you, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted it and ordered its fast."
"2833","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked on the day of sacrifice, it was said O Messenger of Allah, a man slaughtered before stoning, or shaved before slaughtering, so he said No harm, he said: He was not asked that day about anything except that he closed with his hands as if throwing with them and saying No harm, no harm."
"2834","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, and in it were six pillars, so he stood at each pillar and supplicated, and did not pray in it."
"2835","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, the meaning, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to perform Hajj walking, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said Allah Almighty has no need of the vow of your sister, let her ride and let her offer a camel."
"2836","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated running, and he only circumambulated to show the polytheists his strength, and Affan said: And for this the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to show the people his strength."
"2837","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about witr, so he said I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A rakah at the end of the night, and I asked Ibn Umar, so he said I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A rakah at the end of the night."
"2838","Rawh narrated to us, Habib ibn Shihab al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I came to Ibn Abbas, I and a companion of mine, and we met Abu Hurayrah at the door of Ibn Abbas, so he said Who are you, so we told him, so he said Go to people with dates and water, every valley flows according to its measure, he said: We said May your good be abundant, ask permission for us to see Ibn Abbas, he said: So he asked permission for us, and we heard Ibn Abbas narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon on the day of Tabuk and said: There is no one among people like a man who takes the bridle of his horse and strives in the way of Allah and avoids the evils of people, and like a man in the desert with his sheep who honors his guest and fulfills his due, he said: I said Did he say it, he said He said it, he said: I said Did he say it, he said He said it, he said: I said Did he say it, he said He said it, so I magnified Allah and praised Allah and thanked."
"2839","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them this supplication as he taught them the surah from the Quran, saying: Say O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and the trial of death."
"2840","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said Ata al-Khurasani said, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came to him and said I owe a camel, and I am wealthy enough for it, but I cannot find one to buy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to buy seven sheep and slaughter them."
"2841","Rawh narrated to us, Abu Malik Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Mughith, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns knowledge from the stars learns a branch of magic, the more he adds the more, and the more he adds the more."
"2842","Rawh narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of Muzdalifah, young boys of the Banu Abd al-Muttalib on our donkeys, so he began to pat our thighs with his hand and say: O my sons, do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises, so Ibn Abbas said: I do not think anyone stones the jamrah until the sun rises."
"2843","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ghanawi, from Abu al-Tufayl, thus Rawh said Asim, and people say Abu Asim, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel, and that that is sunnah, so he said They told the truth and they lied, I said What is they told the truth and they lied, he said: He did circumambulate between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel, but that is not sunnah, the people would not turn away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor be pushed away, so he circumambulated on a camel so they could hear and see his place, and their hands could not reach him."
"2844","Yazid narrated to me, he said Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the one who comes to his wife while she is menstruating to give a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"2845","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said Ibn Jurayj informed us, Umar ibn Ata informed me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: There is no sarurah in Islam."
"2846","Abu Kamil and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, he said Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, Hasan said: From Ammar, Hammad said: And I think it is from Ibn Abbas, and Hasan did not doubt in it, he said: Ibn Abbas said, my father said: And Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, mursal, with no Ibn Abbas in it, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadijah, then Affan mentioned the hadith, and Abu Kamil and Hasan said in their hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Khadijah: I see a light and hear a voice, and I fear there is madness in me, she said Allah would not do that to you, O son of Abdullah, then she came to Waraqah ibn Nawfal and mentioned that to him, so he said If he is truthful then this is a namus like the namus of Musa, so if he is sent and I am alive, I will support him and aid him and believe in him."
"2847","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah fifteen years, seven years seeing the light and illumination and hearing the voice, and eight years being revealed to, and he stayed in Madinah ten years."
"2848","Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, the meaning, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him was a man conversing with him, Affan said: While he was as if turning away from al-Abbas, so we went out from him, so he said Did you not see my cousin as if turning away from me, so I said He had a man with him conversing with him, Affan said: So he said Was there anyone with him, I said Yes, he said: So he returned to him and said O Messenger of Allah, was there anyone with you, for Abdullah told me that you had a man conversing with you, he said Did you see him, O Abdullah, he said Yes, he said That was Jibril, and he is the one who kept me from you."
"2849","Affan narrated to us: He was with you a man conversing with you."
"2850","Abdullah narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2851","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, in what Hammad thinks, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah, and her father desired to marry her off, so she prepared food and drink, then she called her father and a group of Quraysh, so they ate and drank until they became drunk, then Khadijah said to her father: Muhammad ibn Abdullah proposes to me, so marry me to him, so he married her to him, then she perfumed him and dressed him in a robe, and thus they used to do with fathers, then when his drunkenness wore off he looked and found himself perfumed and wearing a robe, so he said What is my affair, what is this, she said You married me to Muhammad ibn Abdullah, he said I marry the orphan of Abu Talib, no, by my life, so Khadijah said Are you not ashamed, you want to disgrace yourself before Quraysh, telling people you were drunk, and she kept at him until he agreed."
"2852","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed us, from Ibn Abbas, in what he thinks, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid, then he mentioned its meaning."
"2853","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said Ata al-Khurasani said, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came to him and said I owe a camel, and I am wealthy enough for it, but I cannot find one to buy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to buy seven sheep and slaughter them."
"2854","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said Shubah informed me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, mentioning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned the Dajjal, he said He is one-eyed, fair, as if his head is a viper, the most resembling of your men to him is Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan, so if the perishing perish, then your Lord Almighty is not one-eyed."
"2855","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Tawus saying: We said to Ibn Abbas about squatting on the feet, so he said It is the sunnah, he said: So we said We consider it roughness to the foot, so Ibn Abbas said It is the sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2856","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: I did not know the Messenger of Allah seeking a day, seeking its virtue over others, except this day, the day of Ashura, or the month of Ramadan."
"2857","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas kneeling on the front of his feet, so I said This, people claim it is roughness, he said It is the sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2858","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade a garment of pure silk."
"2859","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said Khusayf informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr and Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade a garment of pure silk."
"2860","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril recited to me upon one harf, so I asked him to add, and I kept asking for more and he added to me, until it reached seven ahruf, al-Zuhri said: These ahruf are in one matter, and they do not differ about lawful or unlawful."
"2861","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among poetry there is wisdom, and among eloquence there is magic."
"2862","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Divide wealth among those entitled to fixed shares according to the Book of Allah Blessed and Exalted, then what the fixed shares leave is for the nearest male."
"2863","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in two white cloaks and a red cloak."
"2864","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: For one of you to lend his brother his land is better for him than to take for it such and such for a known thing, he said: Ibn Abbas said: And it is haql, and in the tongue of the Ansar it is muhaqalah."
"2865","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tamattu, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman likewise, and the first who forbade it was Muawiyah."
"2866","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us its meaning with its isnad."
"2867","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No harm and no reciprocated harm, and a man may place wood on the wall of his neighbor, and the thoroughfare is seven cubits."
"2868","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed us, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: If you can, let none of you go out on the day of Fitr until he eats, then do so, he said: I have not left eating before going out since I heard that from Ibn Abbas, so I eat from the edge of dried meat a morsel, or drink milk or water, I said How is this interpreted, he said: He heard it, I think, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They would not go out until the forenoon extended, so they would say We eat lest we hasten from our prayer."
"2869","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri informed us, from Ismail, my father said: He is Abu Israil al-Mulaiy, from Fudayl meaning Ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten to Hajj, meaning the obligatory, for none of you knows what will happen to him."
"2870","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions when they intended to enter Makkah in their umrah after al-Hudaybiyah: Your people tomorrow will see you, so let them see you strong, so when they entered the mosque they touched the corner, then they ran, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with them, until when they reached the Yemeni corner they walked to the Black Corner, and he did that three times, then he walked the four."
"2871","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Israil informed us, and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged a fifth in rikaz."
"2872","My father said: Aswad narrated it to us, Israil narrated to us, he said: And he judged, and Abu Nuaym said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged a fifth in rikaz."
"2873","Abd al-Razzaq and Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not touch a man, nor a woman a woman."
"2874","And Aswad did not raise it, and he narrated it to us from Hasan, from Simak, from Ikrimah, mursal."
"2875","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished from Badr: You have the caravan, there is nothing beyond it, he said: Then al-Abbas called to him while he was a prisoner in bonds: It is not right, he said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him Why, he said Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"2876","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Maiz, so he confessed before him twice, so he said Take him away, then he said Return him, so he confessed twice, until he confessed four times, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Take him away and stone him."
"2877","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Divorce in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and two years of the caliphate of Umar ibn al-Khattab, the divorce of three was one, then Umar said People have hastened in a matter in which they had deliberation, so if we enforce it upon them, so he enforced it upon them."
"2878","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Harim, from Sadaqah al-Dimashqi, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas asking him about fasting, so he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Among the best fasting is the fasting of my brother Dawud, he used to fast a day and break a day."
"2879","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tamattu, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and the first who forbade it was Muawiyah."
"2880","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his brother, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to perform wudu from a waterskin, so it was said to him It is carrion, so he said Its tanning removes its filth, or its impurity, or its uncleanness."
"2881","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, he said Said ibn Jubayr informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand between my shoulders, or he said On my shoulder, and said O Allah, make him understand the religion and teach him interpretation."
"2882","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed one hundred camels in Hajj, he sacrificed sixty of them with his hand, and ordered the rest and they were sacrificed, and he took from each camel a piece, and they were gathered in a pot, and he ate from it and sipped its broth, and he sacrificed seventy on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, among them the camel of Abu Jahl, and when it was barred from the House it moaned as it moans for its young."
"2883","Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar meaning Ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drove one hundred camels, then he mentioned the like of it."
"2884","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Ibn Idris, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the year of the conquest, ten days past Ramadan, then when he camped at Marr al-Zahran he broke his fast."
"2885","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah in the year of the conquest seventeen days praying two rakahs, Abu al-Nadr said: Shortening, praying two rakahs."
"2886","Abdullah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz from the trustworthy narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, and Nasr ibn Ali narrated to me, he said: My father informed me, from Sharik, from Ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2887","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman the freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to him, that he said: Let her ride and let her expiate her oath."
"2888","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sayf ibn Sulayman al-Makkiy informed us, Qays ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by a witness and an oath."
"2889","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Qariz ibn Shaybah, from Abu Ghatfan, he said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and found him performing wudu, so he rinsed his mouth then sniffed water, then he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twice twice, or two fully, or three."
"2890","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to me, Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was in ihram."
"2891","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ulwan, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Fifty prayers were imposed upon your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he asked his Lord Almighty, and He made them five."
"2892","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Usm, from Ibn Abbas, saying: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with fifty prayers, so he asked his Lord Almighty, and He made them five prayers."
"2893","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Usm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah Almighty imposed upon His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayer as fifty prayers, so he asked his Lord, and He made them five prayers."
"2894","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us the surah from the Quran."
"2895","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded with the siwak until I feared revelation would come to me about it."
"2896","Yahya ibn Adam and Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A righteous dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"2897","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Kamil ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas, or from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said between the two prostrations in the night prayer: My Lord, forgive me and have mercy on me and raise me and provide for me and guide me, then he prostrated."
"2898","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: This land is sacred, Allah made it sacred, killing was not permitted in it for anyone before me, and it was permitted for me for an hour, so it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Resurrection, its game is not to be disturbed, nor its thorns cut, nor its lost property picked up except by one who announces it, nor its herbage cut, so al-Abbas said O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir, for it is for their houses and their smiths, so he said Except idhkhir, and there is no hijrah, but jihad and intention, and when you are called to march then march."
"2899","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Malik ibn Khayr al-Ziyadiy informed me, that Malik ibn Sad al-Tujibiy narrated to him, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Jibril came to me and said O Muhammad, Allah Almighty has cursed wine, and its presser, and the one for whom it is pressed, and its drinker, and its carrier, and the one to whom it is carried, and its seller, and its buyer, and its pourer, and the one for whom it is poured."
"2900","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Luhayah ibn Uqbah al-Hadrami Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah al-Sabaiy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Walah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Saba, what is it, a man or a woman or a land, so he said Rather it is a man who had ten children, six of them settled in Yemen and four of them in Syria, as for the Yemenis, they are Madhhij and Kindah and al-Azd and al-Ashariyyun and Anmar and Himyar, all Arabs, and as for the Syrians, they are Lakhm and Judham and Amilah and Ghassan."
"2901","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, then two slave girls came and stood in front of him near his head, so he moved them aside and gestured with his hands to his right and to his left."
"2902","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas: The name of Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed her name and named her Juwayriyah."
"2903","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ilba, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines on the ground and said: Do you know what this is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh."
"2904","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Shubah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, or Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, that Abd Allah ibn Abbas passed by Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Rabiah while he was praying with his head braided and tied from behind, so he stood over him and kept undoing the knots of his head, and Abd Allah ibn al-Harith yielded to him until he finished undoing it, then he sat. When Ibn al-Harith finished his prayer he came to him and said: Why did you do to my head what you did just now. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of one who prays with his head tied from behind is like the likeness of one who prays bound."
"2905","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Bukayr, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of one who prays with his head gathered up is like the likeness of one who prays while he is tied up."
"2906","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped three times on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders, and he gave the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."
"2907","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three: with Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and Say O disbelievers, and Say He is Allah the One."
"2908","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday Alif Lam Mim the Revelation of the Prostration and Has there come upon man."
"2909","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating, having spread his arms wide, until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"2910","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I observed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him prostrating with his arms spread wide, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"2911","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every alliance that existed in the pre-Islamic period, Islam only increased it in strength or firmness."
"2912","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Any slave woman who bears a child to her master is freed after his death, or he said: after him, and perhaps he said both together."
"2913","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he commanded Ali, so he prepared washing water for him, then gave him a garment and said: Screen me and turn your back to me."
"2914","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you differ about the road, make it seven cubits, and whoever is asked by his neighbor to place a support upon his wall, let him do so."
"2915","Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed whoever changes the boundary marks of the earth, Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah, Allah has cursed whoever curses his parents, Allah has cursed whoever takes others than his patrons as patrons, Allah has cursed whoever misleads a blind man from the path, Allah has cursed whoever has intercourse with an animal, Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, three times."
"2916","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, who said: Amr ibn Abi Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accursed is whoever reviles his father, accursed is whoever reviles his mother, accursed is whoever slaughters for other than Allah, accursed is whoever changes the boundary marks of the earth, accursed is whoever misleads a blind man from the road, accursed is whoever has intercourse with an animal, accursed is whoever does the deed of the people of Lut. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it repeatedly, three times concerning sodomy."
"2917","Abu Said narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed whoever changes the boundary marks of the earth, Allah has cursed whoever takes others than his patrons as patrons, Allah has cursed whoever misleads a blind man from the road, Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah, Allah has cursed whoever has intercourse with an animal, Allah has cursed whoever disobeys his parents, Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut. He said it three times."
"2918","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to pray the two rakahs of the forenoon though you were not commanded with them, and I was commanded with the sacrifice though it was not prescribed as obligatory."
"2919","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Sacrificial slaughter was prescribed for me though it was not prescribed for you, and I was commanded with the two rakahs of the forenoon though you were not commanded with them."
"2920","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Razin, from Abu Yahya, the freedman of Ibn Aqil al-Ansari, who said: Ibn Abbas said: I have been taught a verse of the Quran about which no man has ever asked me, and I do not know whether people know it and so have not asked about it, or have not noticed it so as to ask about it. Then he began narrating to us, and when he stood up we blamed one another for not having asked him about it, so I said: I will take care of it when he comes tomorrow. When he came the next day I said: O Ibn Abbas, yesterday you mentioned that there is a verse of the Quran about which no man has ever asked you, and you do not know whether people know it and so have not asked about it, or have not noticed it. Tell me about it and about those you recited before it. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: O assembly of Quraysh, there is no one worshipped besides Allah in whom there is any good. Quraysh knew that the Christians worship Isa son of Maryam, and what do you say about Muhammad. They said: O Muhammad, do you not claim that Isa was a prophet and a righteous servant among the servants of Allah. If you are truthful, then their gods are as you say. He said: Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And when the son of Maryam is cited as an example, your people turn away from it. He said: I said: What is yasiddun. He said: They raise a clamor. And indeed he is knowledge of the Hour. He said: It is the emergence of Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, before the Day of Resurrection."
"2921","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated to us, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the courtyard of his house in Makkah, Uthman ibn Mazun passed by him and grinned toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you not sit. He said: Yes indeed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat facing him, and while he was speaking to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze toward the sky and looked for a while at the sky, then began lowering his gaze until he placed it on his right on the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from his companion Uthman toward where he had placed his gaze, and began nodding his head as though trying to understand what was being said to him, while Ibn Mazun looked on. When he had finished his need and understood what was being said to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze toward the sky as he had the first time, and he followed him with his gaze until he disappeared into the sky. Then he turned to Uthman with his first sitting posture. He said: O Muhammad, in all the time I sat with you and came to you, I never saw you do as you did this morning. He said: And what did you see me do. He said: I saw you fix your gaze toward the sky, then place it where you placed it on your right, then turn toward it and leave me, and begin nodding your head as though trying to understand something being said to you. He said: And did you notice that. Uthman said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A messenger of Allah came to me just now while you were sitting. He said: A messenger of Allah. He said: Yes. He said: And what did he say to you. He said: Indeed Allah commands justice and excellence and giving to near relatives, and forbids shameful deeds and wrongdoing and transgression. He admonishes you that you may remember. Uthman said: That was when faith settled in my heart and I loved Muhammad."
"2922","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to us, Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a sanctuary, and my sanctuary is Madinah. O Allah, I make it sacred by Your sanctity, that no innovator be sheltered in it, its grass not be cut, its thorns not be lopped, and its lost property not be taken except by one who announces it."
"2923","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to us, Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man who claims affiliation to other than his father, or takes as patrons other than his patrons who freed him, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people until the Day of Resurrection. Neither compensation nor recompense will be accepted from him."
"2924","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Shahr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prohibited from categories of women except believing emigrant women. He said: Women are not lawful for you after this, nor that you exchange them for other wives, even though their beauty pleases you, except what your right hand possesses. And Allah the Mighty and Majestic permitted your believing slave girls, and a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet, and He forbade every woman of a religion other than Islam. He said: And whoever disbelieves in faith, his deed is lost and he is among the losers in the Hereafter. And He said: O Prophet, We have made lawful for you your wives to whom you have given their dowries and what your right hand possesses, up to His saying: exclusively for you apart from the believers. And He forbade other than that among the categories of women."
"2925","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed marriage to a woman of his people called Sawdah, who had children; she had five or six boys by a husband of hers who had died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What prevents you from me. She said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, nothing prevents me from you except that you are the dearest of creation to me, but I honor you too much for these boys to clamor around your head morning and evening. He said: Has anything other than that prevented you from me. She said: No, by Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: May Allah have mercy on you. The best women who have ridden the backs of camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, the most affectionate toward a child in his childhood and the most careful with a husband regarding his property."
"2926","And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in a sitting place of his, then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placing his palms upon the knees of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what Islam is. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is to submit your face to Allah, and to bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He said: If I do that, am I a Muslim. He said: When you do that, you have submitted. He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what faith is. He said: Faith is to believe in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, the prophets, and to believe in death and in life after death, and to believe in Paradise and Hell, the Reckoning and the Balance, and to believe in the decree, all of it, its good and its evil. He said: If I do that, I have believed. He said: When you do that, you have believed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me what excellence is. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Excellence is to act for Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me when the Hour is. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah. They are among five matters of the unseen which none knows but He: Indeed Allah has knowledge of the Hour, sends down the rain, knows what is in the wombs, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware. But if you wish, I will tell you of signs of it short of that. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, tell me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the slave woman give birth to her mistress or her master, and you see the herders of sheep competing in tall buildings, and you see the barefoot, hungry, dependent poor become the leaders of people, that is among the signs of the Hour and its portents. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and who are the herders of sheep and the barefoot hungry dependent. He said: The Arabs."
"2927","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take good omens and not take bad omens, and every good name pleased him."
"2928","Hashim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: You are the best nation brought forth for people. He said: Those who emigrated with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah."
"2929","Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Khalid, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhuayb, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came or went out to them while they were sitting and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people in station. He said: We said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the bridle of a horse in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the one next to him. We said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving alms, and keeping apart from the evils of people. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the worst of people in station. He said: We said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The one who is asked by Allah and does not give thereby."
"2930","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhuayb, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he went out to them while they were sitting and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people in station. Then he mentioned it."
"2931","Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the woman and the slave from the spoils from what the army obtained."
"2932","Husayn narrated it to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the slave and the woman from the spoils."
"2933","Yazid narrated it to us, he said: from one who heard Ibn Abbas, and he said: less than what the army receives."
"2934","Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Shubah, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah visited Ibn Abbas to console him for an illness, while he wore a cloak of brocade, so I said: O Abu Abbas, what is this garment. He said: And what is it. He said: This is brocade. He said: By Allah, I did not know of it, and I do not think the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this when he forbade it except for arrogance and pride, and we, praise be to Allah, are not like that. He said: Then what are these images in the stove. He said: Do you not see that we have burned them with fire. When al-Miswar left, he said: Remove this garment from me and cut off the heads of these statues. They said: O Abu Abbas, had you taken them to the market they would have fetched more with the head. He said: No. So he ordered their heads to be cut off."
"2935","Hashim, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Shubah, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: Your freedman, when he prostrates, places his forehead, his forearms, and his chest on the ground. Ibn Abbas said to him: What makes you do what you do. He said: Humility. He said: This is the crouching of the dog. I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"2936","And Husayn narrated it to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, and he mentioned the like of it."
"2937","He said: Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Shubah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send him with his family to Mina on the day of sacrifice to stone the pillar at dawn."
"2938","He said: Husayn narrated it to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Shubah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with his family to Mina on the day of sacrifice, and they stoned the pillar at dawn."
"2939","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has intercourse with his slave woman and she bears him a child, she is freed after his death."
"2940","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray wrapped in a garment, guarding with its excess against the heat and cold of the ground."
"2941","Husayn ibn Ali, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A slave girl would bring the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a shoulder from the pot, he would eat from it, then go out to prayer and pray without performing ablution and without touching water."
"2942","Husayn, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the mat."
"2943","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah al-Haruri, when he left the turmoil of Ibn al-Zubayr, sent to Ibn Abbas asking him about the share of the near relatives, for whom he deemed it. He said: It is for us, the near kin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it for them. Umar had offered us something from it which we deemed less than our right, so we returned it to him and refused to accept it. What he offered them was to help their marrying ones, pay for their debtors, and give to their poor, and he refused to give them more than that."
"2944","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to let his hair hang down, while the polytheists parted their heads, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved to agree with the People of the Book in what had not been revealed to him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parted his head."
"2945","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one among people but he has erred or intended an error, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya."
"2946","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas and Dawud ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas informed me, one of them adding to the other, that a man called out to Ibn Abbas while people were around him and said: Is it a sunnah you seek with this date-drink, or is it lighter for you than milk and honey. Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Abbas and said: Give us to drink. He said: This date-drink is a drink that has been stirred and mixed. Shall we not give you milk or honey to drink. He said: Give us to drink from what you give people to drink. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with his companions of the Emigrants and Helpers, was brought two waterskins containing date-drink. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, he hastened before quenching his thirst, then raised his head and said: You have done well. Do so like this. Ibn Abbas said: The pleasure of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with that is dearer to me than that its valleys flow with milk and honey."
"2947","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you."
"2948","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Umar informed me that Ata informed him that Abd Allah ibn Abbas invited al-Fadl to food on the day of Arafah, but he said: I am fasting. Abd Allah said: Do not fast, for milk was brought near to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he drank from it on this day, and people follow your example."
"2949","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fasted a complete month except Ramadan. When he fasted he would fast until one would say: By Allah, he will never break his fast, and when he broke his fast he would break it until one would say: By Allah, he will never fast."
"2950","Struck through. Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: It was in the book of my father, from Abd al-Samad, from his father, from al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Dhakwan, from Habib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade walking in a single leather sock or a single sandal. And in the hadith there is much other speech besides this, but he did not narrate it to us. It was struck through in his book, so I thought he abandoned his hadith because he narrated from Amr ibn Khalid, who narrates from Zayd ibn Ali, and Amr ibn Khalid is worth nothing."
"2951","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying down animals as targets, and the milk of the dung-eating animal, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"2952","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Jafar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me and commanded me to proclaim the talbiyah aloud."
"2953","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Khusayf informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr, and from Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade garments of pure silk. As for a garment whose warp is silk but is not pure silk, we see no harm in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade drinking from silver vessels."
"2954","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Husayn say: I was with Said ibn Jubayr when he said: From Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. I said: Who are they. He said: They are those who do not seek ruqyah, do not take bad omens, do not divine by birds, and rely upon their Lord."
"2955","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ziyad informed me that Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, informed him that he heard Ibn Abbas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The womb is a branch attached to the waist of the Most Merciful. He joins whoever joins it and cuts whoever cuts it."
"2956","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Dawud, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs: the umrah of Hudaybiyah, the umrah of fulfillment, the third from al-Jiranah, and the fourth which was with his Hajj."
"2957","Abu al-Nadr and Husayn said: Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath, Said ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at one who drags his garment."
"2958","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Yahya al-Araj, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Two men disputed, and the oath fell upon one of them, so he swore by Allah besides whom there is no god that he owed him nothing. Then Jibril descended and said: Command him to give him his right, for the right is due upon him though he is lying, and the expiation of his oath is his acknowledgment of Allah that there is no god but He, or his testimony that there is no god but He."
"2959","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, Ilba ibn Ahmar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines, then said: Do you know why I drew these lines. They said: No. He said: The best women of Paradise are four: Maryam bint Imran, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, and Asiyah daughter of Muzahim."
"2960","Uthman ibn Umar said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said ibn Khalid, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to them while they were sitting in a gathering of theirs and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people. They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the head of his horse in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed. Shall I inform you of the one next to him. He said: We said: Yes. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving alms, and keeping apart from the evils of people. Shall I inform you of the worst of people in station. They said: Yes. He said: The one who is asked by Allah and does not give thereby."
"2961","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Iyas informed me, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Umm Hufayd, the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas, gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried yogurt, and lizards as a gift. He ate of the clarified butter and the dried yogurt and left the lizards out of distaste. He said: And it was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and had it been unlawful it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2962","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and wore it, then said: This has distracted me from you since today, a glance to it and a glance to you. Then he threw it away."
"2963","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Barakah Abu al-Walid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews. Fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and consumed their price. When Allah forbids a people a thing, He forbids them its price."
"2964","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its thorny trees are not to be cut, its game is not to be startled, its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it, and its grass is not to be cut. Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir. He said: Except idhkhir. Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix a penalty for wine. Ibn Abbas said: A man drank and became intoxicated, then was met swaying in a mountain pass, so he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he came near the house of Abbas, he slipped away and entered upon Abbas, clinging to him from behind. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he laughed and said: He has done it. Then he did not order them anything concerning him."
"2965","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the qiblah was changed: What of those who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis. Then Allah the Blessed and Exalted revealed: And Allah would never waste your faith."
"2966","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Idris ibn Sinan al-Yamani, from his father Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Jibril to see him in his form, so he said: Call upon your Lord. He said: So he called upon his Lord. He said: Then a darkness appeared to him from the east. He said: It kept rising and spreading. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he fell unconscious, so he came to him, revived him, and wiped the spittle from his cheeks."
"2967","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought people of the Zutt worshipping an idol, so he burned them. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"2968","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sayf ibn Sulayman al-Makki informed me, from Qays ibn Sad al-Makki, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath and a witness. Zayd ibn al-Hubab said: I asked Malik ibn Anas about the oath with the witness, whether it is allowed in divorce and emancipation. He said: No. This is only in buying, selling, and the like."
"2969","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Sayf ibn Sulayman, from Qays ibn Sad, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with the oath along with the witness. Amr said: That is only in property."
"2970","Al-Zubayri Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Upon every Muslim is a Hajj, and had I said every year it would have been so."
"2971","Al-Zubayri and Aswad, the meaning, said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought from a caravan that arrived and profited in ounces, which he distributed among the widows of Abd al-Muttalib, then said: I will not make a purchase for which I do not have the price."
"2972","And Waki also narrated it to us, giving its chain."
"2973","Al-Zubayri and Aswad ibn Amir said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A woman embraced Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then married. Her first husband came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam and she knew of my Islam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her from her latter husband and returned her to her first husband."
"2974","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Israil narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, or from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, or from one of them from the other, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends Hajj, let him hasten, for a stray mount may be lost, a sick person may fall ill, and a need may arise."
"2975","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of narrating from me except what you know, for whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire, and whoever lies about the Quran without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2976","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ata, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two leather socks. Ask these who claim that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped before the revelation of al-Maidah or after al-Maidah. By Allah, he did not wipe after al-Maidah. To wipe on the back of a passerby in the desert is dearer to me than to wipe over them."
"2977","Waki, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: Ibn Abbas said to Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: O Urayyah, ask your mother: Did your father not come with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and release from ihram."
"2978","Waki, from Israil, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The devils had seats in the heaven, and they would listen to the revelation, and the stars did not move, and the devils were not pelted. He said: When they heard the revelation, they descended to the earth and added nine to the word. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, whenever a devil sat in his seat, a meteor came to him and never missed him until it burned him. He said: They complained of that to Iblis, who said: This is only because of an event that has occurred. He said: So he dispersed his troops. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing praying between the two mountains of Nakhlah. He said: They returned to Iblis and informed him. He said: This is what has occurred."
"2979","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ibn Walah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man set out while wine was lawful and gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine as a gift. He came leading it on a camel until he found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting and said: What is this with you. He said: A waterskin of wine I have gifted to you. He said: Do you not know that Allah the Blessed and Exalted has forbidden it. He said: No. He said: Allah has forbidden it. Then the man turned to the camel driver and spoke something between him and him. He said: What did you say to him. He said: I ordered him to sell it. He said: The One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it. He said: Then he ordered the mouths of the waterskin to be opened, so they were opened and it poured out onto the dust. I looked at it in the plain with nothing in it."
"2980","Hashim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given him. He was cupped on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders. A slave of Banu Bayadah used to cup him, from whom a mudd and a half was taken each day, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interceded for him with his owners, and it was made a mudd."
"2981","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram."
"2982","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ibn Ata, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"2983","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was granted victory by the easterly wind, and Ad were destroyed by the westerly wind."
"2984","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Tawus narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven. Shubah said: He narrated it to me another time, he said: I was commanded to prostrate and not to gather hair or garment."
"2985","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women who visit graves and those who take mosques and lamps over them."
"2986","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen rakahs at night."
"2987","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man of Banu Sulaym who had sheep of his. He greeted them, but they said: He only greeted you to shield himself from you. So they set upon him, killed him, and took his sheep, then brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Allah the Blessed and Exalted revealed: And do not say to one who offers you peace, You are not a believer, seeking the goods of worldly life, to the end of the verse."
"2988","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: You are the best nation brought forth for people. He said: The companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who emigrated with him to Madinah."
"2989","Husayn ibn Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A Jew passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting and said: What do you say, O Abu al-Qasim, on the day Allah the Blessed and Exalted places the heaven on this, pointing with the forefinger, and the earth on this, and the water on this, and the mountains on this, and the rest of creation on this, each time pointing with his finger. He said: Then Allah the Blessed and Exalted revealed: And they did not esteem Allah His true estimation, to the end of the verse."
"2990","Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one day with no water in the camp. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no water in the camp. He said: Do you have anything. He said: Yes. He said: Bring it to me. So he brought him a vessel containing a little water. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his fingers over the mouth of the vessel and opened his fingers. He said: Springs burst forth from between his fingers. And he commanded Bilal and said: Announce among the people the blessed ablution."
"2991","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When death approached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Come, I will write for you a document after which you will never go astray. In the house were men, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is overcome by pain, and you have the Quran. The Book of Allah suffices us. He said: The people of the house differed and disputed. Some said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will write for you, or he said: Bring near, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will write for you. And some said what Umar said. When they increased in noise and dispute and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was distressed, he said: Stand up from me. Ibn Abbas used to say: The calamity, all the calamity, is what came between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his writing that document for them, because of their dispute and noise."
"2992","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while in Makkah toward Bayt al-Maqdis with the Kabah before him, and after emigrating to Madinah for sixteen months, then he was turned toward the Kabah."
"2993","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Umar came and said: Peace be upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon you, may Umar enter."
"2994","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attach the prescribed shares to their rightful recipients. What remains is for the nearest male."
"2995","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in the year of the conquest in Ramadan and fasted until he reached Usfan, then called for a vessel and drank by day for people to see, then broke his fast until he entered Makkah. He conquered Makkah in Ramadan. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted while traveling and broke his fast, so whoever wishes fasts and whoever wishes breaks his fast."
"2996","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Miqsam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: Upon him is half a dinar."
"2997","He said: And Sharik said, from Ibn Abbas."
"2998","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Hajj every year, so he said: Upon every Muslim is a Hajj, and had I said every year it would have been so."
"2999","Yahya ibn Adam, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Kab, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali came out from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during his illness, so they said: How is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) this morning, O Abu Hasan. He said: He is recovered, praise be to Allah. Abbas said: Do you not see, I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will die of this illness, and I recognize death in the faces of Banu Abd al-Muttalib. Come with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and let us speak to him. If authority is among us, he will clarify it, and if it is in others, we will speak to him and he will counsel for us. Ali said: If he says authority is in others, people will never give it to us. By Allah, I will never speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this."
"3000","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Maiz when he said: I committed adultery: Perhaps you touched, or kissed, or looked at her, as though fearing he did not know what adultery is."
"3001","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to review the Quran with Jibril every year once, and in the year in which he died he reviewed it with him twice, and the recitation of Abdullah was the last recitation."
"3002","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: When 'And do not approach the orphan's wealth except in the best manner' was revealed, they isolated the wealth of the orphans until food spoiled and meat rotted, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then 'And if you mix with them then they are your brothers, and Allah knows the corrupter from the reformer' was revealed. He said: So they mixed with them."
"3003","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished Badr: Go after the caravan, there is nothing besides it. Al-Abbas called out to him: It is not right for you; Allah promised you one of the two parties and He has given you what He promised you."
"3004","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every beast of prey with fangs."
"3005","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us on the night of sacrifice while darkness of night was upon us, and he began tapping our thighs saying: My sons, pour forth and do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises."
"3006","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night eight rak'ahs, pray witr with three, and pray the two rak'ahs of fajr."
"3007","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Abu Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas who said: The name of Juwayriyah bint al-Harith was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed her name and called her Juwayriyah."
"3008","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent the weak of his family ahead from Muzdalifah by night, and he kept instructing them not to stone Jamrat al-Aqabah until the sun rises."
"3009","Asbat narrated to us, Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Shaybani, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm who said: I came to Ibn Abbas and said: So-and-so married, and he brought us food and we ate, then he brought us thirteen lizards, some eating and some refraining. One of those with Ibn Abbas said: I will not eat it, nor forbid it, nor command it, nor prohibit it. Ibn Abbas said: Evil is what you say; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only sent making lawful and making unlawful. It was brought near to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he extended his hand to eat from it, so Maymunah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is lizard meat. So he withdrew his hand and said: This is meat I have never eaten at all; so eat. So al-Fadl ibn Abbas and Khalid ibn al-Walid and a woman with them ate, and Maymunah said: I will not eat from what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not eat from."
"3010","Asbat narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying 'Then when the trumpet is blown,' he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I be at ease when the companion of the horn has taken the horn and bent his forehead, listening for when he will be commanded to blow. The companions of Muhammad said: What should we say? He said: Say: Allah suffices us and He is the best guardian; upon Allah we rely."
"3011","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about fasting Rajab, what do you think of it? He said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast until we would say he will not break fast, and break fast until we would say he will not fast."
"3012","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to review the Quran with Jibril every Ramadan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning of the night in which he reviewed what he reviewed more generous than the sent wind; he was not asked for anything but he gave it, until the month after which he died, in which he reviewed twice."
"3013","Abdullah ibn al-Walid and Mu'ammal narrated to us, with the same meaning, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: That the Muslims captured a man from the chiefs of the polytheists and killed him, and they asked to buy his corpse."
"3014","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution for prayer, and one of his wives said to him: Sit, for the pot has cooked. So she handed him a shoulder and he ate, then wiped his hand, prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"3015","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that vomits then returns to it."
"3016","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Umar, meaning Ibn Farrukh, narrated to us, Habib, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, narrated to us, from Ikrimah who said: I saw a man enter the mosque and stand and pray; whenever he raised his head he said Allahu Akbar, and whenever he lowered his head he said Allahu Akbar, and whenever he rose from the two rak'ahs he said Allahu Akbar. I disapproved of that, so I came to Ibn Abbas and told him of that, and he said: May you lose your mother, is that not the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3017","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Nuh ibn Ja'wanah al-Sulami, a Khurasani, narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque saying with his hand like this - Abu Abd al-Rahman gestured with his hand toward the ground: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits for him, Allah will protect him from the scorch of Hell. Indeed the work of Paradise is rugged on a hill - three times. Indeed the work of Hell is easy on a plain. And the fortunate is he who is shielded from trials. And there is no draught more beloved to me than a draught of anger that a servant swallows; no servant swallows it for Allah but Allah fills his inside with faith."
"3018","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: To whom did this sheep belong? They said: To Maymunah. He said: Why did you not benefit from its hide."
"3019","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I and al-Fadl passed on a donkey while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with the people in an open land, so we dismounted and joined him, and he said nothing to us about that."
"3020","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave him his wage."
"3021","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent dinner to Abu Taybah and he cupped him, and he gave him his wage. Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Jam' [Muzdalifah], and when everything brightened before the sun rose, he poured forth."
"3022","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hashim narrated to us, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah who said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari say: We sighted the crescent of Ramadan while at Dhat Irq. We sent a man to Ibn Abbas to ask him - Hashim said: So he asked him - and Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has extended its sighting - Hashim said: for its sighting - so if it is obscured for you, complete the number."
"3023","Hashim narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, I heard Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, so I placed ablution water for him. When he came out he said: Who placed this. Ibn Abbas said [it was he]. He said: O Allah, make him learned in the religion."
"3024","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every beast of prey with fangs and every bird with talons."
"3025","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Guard against narrating from me except what you know. He said: And whoever lies about the Quran without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"3026","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began speaking eloquent speech, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed among eloquence is magic, and indeed among poetry is wisdom."
"3027","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A sheep belonging to Sawdah bint Zam'ah died, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died, meaning the sheep. He said: Why did you not take its skin. She said: Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Allah Almighty only said: 'Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it except carrion, or spilled blood, or swine flesh.' You do not eat it; if you tan it you can benefit from it. So she sent for it, skinned its hide, tanned it, and made from it a waterskin until it wore out with her."
"3028","Aswad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, and he mentioned it."
"3029","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ma'iz ibn Malik: Is what reached me about you true, that you lay with the slave girl of Banu so-and-so. He said: So he testified four testimonies. He said: So he stoned him."
"3030","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married my aunt Maymunah al-Hilaliyyah while he was in ihram."
"3031","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That they went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in ihram, and a man among them was thrown by his camel and died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote, shroud him in two garments, do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with his hair matted."
"3032","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no omen, no contagion, no hamah, and no Safar. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we take the mangy sheep and throw it among the flock and they become mangy. He said: Then who infected the first."
"3033","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the house of Maymunah, and I placed ablution water for him at night. He said: Maymunah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah ibn Abbas placed this for you. So he said: O Allah, make him learned in the religion and teach him interpretation."
"3034","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind who said: So-and-so narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he walked, walked compactly, without laziness in it."
"3035","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists. He said: Allah knows best what they would have done when He created them."
"3036","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white of your garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them. And among the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears sight and grows hair."
"3037","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before sacrificing. He said: No harm. And another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before stoning. He said: Stone, and no harm."
"3038","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That he heard him say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims belonging to other than his father or takes as patrons other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"3039","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamarat after the sun declined."
"3040","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the fajr prayer on Friday 'The Revelation of the Prostration' and 'Has there come upon man.'"
"3041","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith ibn Hazn, the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas, gifted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried yogurt, and lizards. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for them and they were eaten at his table, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them as if disliking them. Had they been unlawful they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor would he have commanded eating them."
"3042","Affan narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: So-and-so was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah. The youth kept glancing at women and looking at them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept turning his face away with his hand from behind, repeatedly. The youth kept glancing at them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Son of my brother, this is a day in which whoever controls his hearing, sight, and tongue will be forgiven."
"3043","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while in a tent on the day of Badr: O Allah, I invoke You by Your covenant and Your promise. O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today. Abu Bakr took his hand and said: Enough, O Messenger of Allah, you have pressed your Lord insistently. And he was jumping in his armor, then went out saying: 'The host will be defeated and they will turn their backs.'"
"3044","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was offered the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing, and she is not lawful for me; and what is forbidden by blood kin is forbidden by nursing."
"3045","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Abu Jahl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying and forbade him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threatened him. He said: Do you threaten me? By Allah, I am the greatest in attendants of the people of this valley. So Allah revealed: 'Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays; have you seen if he is upon guidance or commands piety; have you seen if he denies and turns away.' Ibn Abbas said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, had he called his attendants, the Zabniyah would have seized him."
"3046","Affan narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, and he raised it [to the Prophet]: No alliance of the pre-Islamic age but Islam only increased it in sharpness and strength."
"3047","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib reported to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Black Stone is from Paradise, and it was whiter than snow until the sins of the people of polytheism blackened it."
"3048","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep that its owners had discarded, and said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners."
"3049","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas: That Sa'd ibn Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling about a vow upon his mother who died before fulfilling it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"3050","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: That a woman from Khath'am asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage, while al-Fadl ibn Abbas was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of hajj upon His servants has met my father as a very old man unable to hold himself on the mount; shall I perform hajj on his behalf. He said: Yes, perform hajj on behalf of your father."
"3051","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to me, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk, then called for water, rinsed, and said: It has greasiness."
"3052","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did you not make use of its skin. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only its eating was forbidden."
"3053","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"3054","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Abd al-Karim narrated to us, he said: One who heard Ibn Abbas narrated to me, saying: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Duba'ah to stipulate a condition in her ihram."
"3055","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from one of his brothers, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: A man has come to us who denies the decree. He said: Point him out to me - and he was then blind. They said: What will you do with him, O Abu Abbas. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if I get hold of him I will bite his nose until I cut it off, and if his neck falls into my hand I will crush it. For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: As if I see the women of Banu Fihr circumambulating al-Khazraj, their buttocks shaking, as polytheists. This is the first polytheism of this ummah. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, their evil opinion will carry them until they exclude Allah from having decreed good, as they excluded Him from having decreed evil."
"3056","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas, with this hadith. I said: Did Muhammad meet Ibn Abbas. He said: Yes."
"3057","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: It reached me that Ata ibn Abi Rabah said: He heard Ibn Abbas report that a man was wounded in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then had a wet dream, and was ordered to bathe, and died. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: They killed him, may Allah kill them. Was not the cure for ignorance asking."
"3058","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him behind him on his mount. When he settled on it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allahu Akbar three times, praised Allah three times, glorified Allah three times, and declared Allah's oneness once, then lay back on it and laughed. Then he turned to me and said: There is no man who mounts his beast and does as I did but Allah, Blessed and Exalted, turns to him and laughs to him as I laughed to you."
"3059","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri was asked: Is there an obligatory bath on Friday. He said: Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of you comes to Friday, let him bathe. And Tawus said: I said to Ibn Abbas: They mention that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathe on Friday, wash your heads even if you are not junub, and use perfume. Ibn Abbas said: As for bathing, yes; as for perfume, I do not know."
"3060","Abdullah said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting this hadith: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah reported to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the one joined to, and men who imitate women and women who imitate men."
"3061","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Abi Saghirah Abu Yunus narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar: That Kurayb reported to him that Ibn Abbas said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of the night and prayed behind him. He took my hand and pulled me and placed me beside him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to his prayer, I withdrew. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and when he finished he said to me: What is the matter with me, I place you beside me and you withdraw. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is it fitting for anyone to pray beside you when you are the Messenger of Allah whom Allah has given. He said: So I pleased him, and he supplicated Allah for me to increase me in knowledge and understanding. He said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep until I heard him snore. Then Bilal came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the prayer. So he stood and prayed and did not repeat ablution."
"3062","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Balj narrated to us, Amr ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas when nine men came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, either you stand with us or let these men leave us alone. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Rather I will stand with you. He said: And he was then healthy before he went blind. He said: They began and conversed, and we do not know what they said. He said: Then he came shaking his garment saying: Fie and shame; they attacked a man who has ten virtues; they attacked a man to whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall send a man whom Allah will never disgrace, who loves Allah and His Messenger. He said: Whoever aspired to it aspired. He said: Where is Ali. They said: He is in the luggage grinding. He said: And was none of you able to grind. He said: Then he came, sore-eyed, hardly able to see. He said: He spat in his eyes, then shook the banner three times and gave it to him, and he came with Safiyyah bint Huyayy. He said: Then he sent so-and-so with Surat al-Tawbah, then sent Ali behind him and took it from him. He said: None shall take it but a man from me and I from him. He said: And he said to his cousins: Which of you will be loyal to me in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And Ali was sitting with him, but they refused. So Ali said: I will be loyal to you in this world and the Hereafter. He said: You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter. He said: He left him, then turned to a man among them and said: Which of you will be loyal to me in this world and the Hereafter. But they refused. He said: So Ali said: I will be loyal to you in this world and the Hereafter. So he said: You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter. He said: And he was the first to embrace Islam among people after Khadijah. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his garment and placed it over Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, and said: 'Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and purify you thoroughly.' He said: And Ali sold himself, wore the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then slept in his place. He said: And the polytheists were pelting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Abu Bakr came while Ali was sleeping. He said: And Abu Bakr thought he was the Prophet of Allah. He said: So he said: O Prophet of Allah. He said: Ali said to him: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has set out toward the well of Maymun, go after him. He said: So Abu Bakr set out and entered the cave with him. He said: And Ali kept being pelted with stones as the Prophet of Allah was pelted, writhing, having wrapped his head in the garment without exposing it until morning. Then he uncovered his head and they said: You are indeed ignoble; we pelted your companion and he did not writhe, while you writhe, and we found that strange. He said: And he went out with the people in the expedition of Tabuk. He said: Ali said to him: Shall I go out with you. He said: The Prophet of Allah said to him: No. So Ali wept, and he said to him: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that you are not a prophet; it is not fitting that I go but that you are my deputy. He said: And the Messenger of Allah said to him: You are my ally over every believer after me. And he said: Close the doors of the mosque except the door of Ali. He said: So he enters the mosque junub, it being his path, with no path for him besides it. He said: And he said: Whosever master I am, then his master is Ali. He said: And Allah Almighty informed us in the Quran that He was pleased with them, with the companions of the Tree, and knew what was in their hearts; did He tell us that He was angry with them afterward. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar when he said: Permit me to strike his neck. He said: Would you do it; and what do you know, perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish."
"3063","Abu Malik Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, similar to it."
"3064","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr, both said: Ibn Jurayj reported to us, Hasan ibn Muslim reported to me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: I attended the prayer on the day of Fitr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman; all of them prayed it before the sermon, then preached after. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended, as if I look at him settling the men with his hand, then came cutting through them until he reached the women, with Bilal. He said: 'O Prophet, when the believing women come to you pledging not to associate anything with Allah,' and he recited this verse until he finished it. Then he said when he finished it: Are you upon that. One woman said, none besides her among them answering him: Yes, O Prophet of Allah - Hasan did not know who she was. He said: So give charity. He said: Bilal spread his garment, then said: Come, may my father and mother be ransom for you. So they began throwing rings and signet rings into Bilal's garment. Ibn Bakr said: rings."
"3065","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I attended the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on the day of festival, then he preached. He thought he did not make the women hear, so he came to them, exhorted them, and said: Give charity. So the woman began throwing the ring, the earring, and the thing. Then he ordered Bilal, who gathered it in a garment until he carried it away."
"3066","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said once: from Ibn Abbas - I said: He would not go beyond Tawus with it. He said: Rather, it is from Ibn Abbas. He said: Then he heard him mention it afterward without mentioning Ibn Abbas. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Syria from al-Juhfah, the people of Yemen from Yalamlam, and the people of Najd from Qarn; and they are for them and for whoever passes them besides them intending hajj and umrah. And whoever's house is short of the miqat, he enters ihram from his house, until coming to the people of Makkah - I entered ihram from Yalamlam when I came from Abd al-Razzaq."
"3067","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the shrike."
"3068","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought two roasted lizards, with Khalid ibn al-Walid beside him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached his hand to eat, and it was said to him: It is lizard. So he held back his hand. Khalid said to him: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, but it is not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. So Khalid ate while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him."
"3069","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il reported to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praising him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed among eloquence is magic, and indeed among poetry is wisdom."
"3070","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from a man, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every beast of prey with fangs and eating every bird with talons."
"3071","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid who said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: O Abu Abbas, I was with Ibn Umar and he recited this verse and wept. He said: Which verse. I said: 'Whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it.' Ibn Abbas said: When this verse was revealed it grieved the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grievously and angered them greatly, meaning, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined if we are taken for what we say and do; as for our hearts, they are not in our hands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Say: We hear and obey. He said: Then this verse abrogated it: 'The Messenger believes in what was revealed to him from his Lord, and the believers,' to 'Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity; for it what it earned and against it what it acquired.' So they were excused for self-talk and taken for deeds."
"3072","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il reported to us - and al-Aswad said: Isra'il narrated to us - from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood. Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il reported to us - and al-Aswad said: Isra'il narrated to us - from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That Quraysh came to a priestess and said to her: Tell us which of us most resembles the owner of this station. She said: If you drag a cloak over this plain then walk upon it, I will tell you. So they dragged, then the people walked upon it, and she saw the footprint of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This is the closest of you in resemblance to him. They remained after that twenty years, or nearly twenty years, or what Allah willed, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent."
"3073","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays reported to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once once."
"3074","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, and al-Thawri, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I was with Ibn Abbas and Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah would not pass a corner but touched it. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would only touch the Black Stone and the Yemeni. Mu'awiyah said: Nothing of the House is to be abandoned."
"3075","Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, al-Thawri reported to us, from Ibn Khuthaym - and Abu Nu'aym: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram and was cupped while in ihram."
"3076","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That a man fell from his camel while in ihram and it broke his neck - or crushed him, Ayyub doubted - so they asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Wash him with water and lote, shroud him in his garment, do not cover his head, and do not bring perfume near him, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection in ihram."
"3077","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar, and Abd al-Karim al-Jazari reported to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That a man fell from a runaway camel while in ihram and was fatally thrown, then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Ayyub."
"3078","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Sa'd ibn Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a vow upon his mother, and he ordered fulfilling it. Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped in the two jugular veins and between the shoulders; a slave of Banu Bayadah cupped him, and his wage was a mudd and a half. So he spoke to his owners until they reduced half a mudd from him. Ibn Abbas said: And he gave him his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given it."
"3079","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from al-Mundhir ibn al-Nu'man al-Aftas, he said: I heard Wahb narrating from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve thousand will come out from Aden-Abyan aiding Allah and His Messenger; they are the best between me and them. Ma'mar said to me: Go and ask him about this hadith."
"3080","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr, both said: Ibn Jurayj reported to us, he said: Ya'la reported to me that he heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, say: Ibn Abbas reported to us that Sa'd ibn Ubadah - Ibn Bakr said: the brother of Banu Sa'idah - his mother died while he was absent from her, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died while I was absent from her; will it benefit her if I give charity of something on her behalf. He said: Yes. He said: I make you witness that the garden of al-Makhraf is charity on her behalf. And Ibn Bakr said: al-Mikhraf."
"3081","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, Hakim ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril led me at the House and prayed Dhuhr with me when the sun declined, the shadow being like a sandal strap. Then he prayed Asr with me when the shadow of everything was twice it. Then he prayed Maghrib with me when the fasting person breaks fast. Then he prayed Isha with me when the twilight disappeared. Then he prayed Fajr with me when food and drink become forbidden to the fasting person. Then he prayed the next day Dhuhr when the shadow of everything was like it. Then he prayed Asr with me when the shadow of everything became twice it. Then he prayed Maghrib with me when the fasting person breaks fast. Then he prayed Isha with me to the first third of the night. Then he prayed Fajr with me and brightened. Then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you; the time is between these two times."
"3082","Abu Nu'aym narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, and he mentioned it with its chain and meaning, except that he said regarding fajr on the second day - I do not know what he said - and he said regarding isha: He prayed with me when the first third of the night had gone."
"3083","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Umar al-San'ani narrated to me, Wahb ibn Manus al-Adani reported to me, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrate from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he raised his head from bowing said: Allah hears him who praises Him. Then he says: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after."
"3084","Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Wahb ibn Manus, other than this hadith."
"3085","Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, Hisham reported to us, from Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage; had it been ill-gotten, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have given it to him."
"3086","Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from Abu Jamrah al-Duba'i who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, naqir, muzaffat, and hantam."
"3087","Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guardian has no authority over the previously married woman, and the orphan girl is to be consulted; her silence is her consent."
"3088","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Umar ibn Mu'attib, from the freedman of Banu Nawfal, meaning Abu al-Hasan, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a slave who divorced his wife twice then both were freed; may he marry her. He said: Yes. It was said: From whom. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave that ruling. It was said to Ma'mar: O Abu Urwah, who is this Abu Hasan; he has carried a great rock."
"3089","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, he said: Al-Zuhri said, and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah reported to me, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Madinah in Ramadan with ten thousand Muslims, that being eight years and a half after his arrival in Madinah. He marched with those Muslims with him to Makkah, fasting and they fasting, until when he reached al-Kadid, between Usfan and Qudayd, he broke fast and the Muslims with him broke fast, and he did not fast."
"3090","Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, Ma'mar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abbas used to narrate that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered the mosque while Umar was addressing the people, and went on until he came to the house in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, while he was in the house of A'ishah. He uncovered a Hibarah cloak from his face with which he was covered, looked at the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then bent over him kissing him, then said: By Allah, Allah will not combine two deaths upon him; you have died the death after which you will not die."
"3091","Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he heard Abu Hurayrah say: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered the mosque while Umar was speaking to the people, and he mentioned the hadith."
"3092","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah who said: Ibn Abbas did not used to recite in Dhuhr and Asr. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited where he was commanded to recite and was silent where he was commanded to be silent: 'You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example,' and 'Your Lord was never forgetful.'"
"3093","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ayyub reported to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Makkah, refused to enter the House while idols were in it, so he ordered them removed. The image of Ibrahim and Isma'il, upon them be peace, with divining arrows in their hands was taken out, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy them; by Allah, they knew they never cast lots with them at all. He said: Then he entered the House, said takbir in its corners, left, and did not pray in the House."
"3094","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with the baggage from Jam' by night."
"3095","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That he disliked nabidh of unripe dates alone, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Abd al-Qays from muzza, so I dislike unripe dates to be alone."
"3096","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday 'The Revelation of the Prostration' and 'Has there come upon man.' Affan said: Alif-Lam-Mim, The Revelation."
"3097","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abi al-Samit reported to us, he said: Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in the morning prayer on Friday 'The Revelation of the Prostration' and 'Has there come upon man.'"
"3098","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd Rabbih ibn Bariq al-Hanafi narrated to us, Simak Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of my ummah has two predecessors [children who died before him] will enter Paradise. A'ishah said: By my father, what of one who has one predecessor. He said: And whoever has one predecessor, O favored one. She said: What of one who has no predecessor among your ummah. He said: Then I am the predecessor of my ummah; they will not be afflicted with the like of me."
"3099","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Sallam narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Abbas: That they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the sticks of his pulpit: Peoples shall cease abandoning Fridays, or Allah shall seal their hearts, then they shall be written among the heedless."
"3100","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"3101","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Habib, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, narrated to me, from Ikrimah, he said: I saw a man praying in the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would say takbir when he prostrated and when he rose and when he lowered himself, so I disapproved of that and I mentioned it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: May you have no mother, that is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3102","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the house of Maymunah, and I placed wudu water for him at night, and Maymunah said to him: Abdullah ibn Abbas placed this for you, and he said: O Allah, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation."
"3103","Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, my father said: Affan narrated to us, Ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Uthman ibn Mazun died, his wife said: Congratulations to you, O Ibn Mazun, with Paradise. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at her with an angry look and said to her: What makes you know. By Allah, I am indeed the Messenger of Allah and I do not know what will be done with me. Affan said: nor with him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, your horseman and your companion. That was hard upon the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he said that about Uthman, and he was among their best, until Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, and he said: Join our righteous predecessor Uthman ibn Mazun. He said: And the women wept, and Umar began beating them with his whip, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Umar: Leave them to weep, and beware, you women, of the croaking of Satan. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever is from the heart and the eye is from Allah and mercy, and whatever is from the hand and the tongue is from Satan. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat at the edge of the grave, and Fatimah was beside him weeping, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began wiping the eyes of Fatimah with his garment out of mercy for her."
"3104","Bakr ibn Isa Abu Bishr al-Rasibi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I was a boy running with the boys, then I turned and there was the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, behind me coming forward, and I said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has only come to me. He said: So I ran until I hid behind the door of a house. He said: I did not realize until he took hold of me and seized me by the nape and gave me a push, and he said: Go and call Muawiyah for me. He said: And he was his scribe. So I ran and came to Muawiyah and I said: Answer the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for he has a need."
"3105","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, and Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Dawud, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with the people on the day of Fitr two rakahs without adhan, then he gave the khutbah after the prayer, then he took the hand of Bilal and went to the women and addressed them, then he ordered Bilal, after he turned away from them, to come to them and order them to give charity."
"3106","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, carried out lian between al-Ajlani and his wife. He said: And she was pregnant, and he said: By Allah, I have not approached her since we watered after leaving off watering. And al-afr is to water the palm trees after they are left without watering after pollination by two months. He said: And her husband was thin in the legs and forearms, blond in hair, and the one with whom she was accused was Ibn al-Sahma. He said: So she gave birth to a black boy with receding hair, curly, thick in the forearms. He said: So Ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had said to Ibn Abbas: Is she the woman about whom the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If I were to stone anyone without proof I would have stoned her. He said: No, that is a woman who committed openly in Islam."
"3107","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, and he mentioned its meaning, and he said in it: thick in the forearms, thick in the legs, and al-Hashimi said: khadl, and he said: after pollination."
"3108","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eat a shoulder piece then pray and not perform wudu."
"3109","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Said informed us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatadah and Yala ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymunah bint al-Harith while he was in ihram. He said: And in the hadith of Yala ibn Hakim: He consummated with her at a water called Sarif, and when he completed his rites he consummated with her at that water."
"3110","Asbat narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade unripe dates and ripe dates to be mixed together, and raisins and dates to be mixed together. He said: And he wrote to the people of Jurash not to mix raisins and dates."
"3111","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was attended by death, and in the house were men, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Come, let me write for you a document after which you will never go astray. So Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has been overcome by pain, and with you is the Quran, Allahs Book suffices us. So the people of the house differed and disputed, among them one who says: Bring near so he may write for you a document after which you will not go astray, and among them one who says what Umar said. So when they increased idle talk and disagreement before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Get up. Ubaydullah said: And Ibn Abbas used to say: The calamity, all the calamity, is what came between the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and writing that document for them, because of their disagreement and noise."
"3112","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Said ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Medina and found the Jews fasting the day of Ashura, and he said: What is this. And they said: This is a great day, a day on which Allah saved Musa and drowned the family of Pharaoh, so Musa fasted it in gratitude. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am closer to Musa and more entitled to his fasting, so he fasted it and ordered its fasting."
"3113","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that he performed wudu washing each limb once, then he mentioned that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did it. Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ata and others informed me, from Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no sarurah in Hajj. Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ata informed me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: There is no sarurah in Islam."
"3114","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas and Dawud ibn Ali narrated to me that a man called out to Ibn Abbas while the people were around him and said: Is it a sunnah you seek with this nabidh, or is it lighter for you than honey and milk. And Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Abbas and said: Give us to drink. And he said: This nabidh is a drink that has been stirred and crumbled, shall we not give you milk and honey. And he said: Give me to drink from what you give the people to drink. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought, and with him his companions of the Muhajirun and the Ansar, large cups containing nabidh, and when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank he hastened before he was quenched and raised his head and said: You have done well, do thus. Ibn Abbas said: So the approval of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of that is more beloved to me than that its mountain paths should flow upon us with milk and honey."
"3115","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Shatha informed him, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while preaching, saying: Whoever does not find an izar and finds trousers, let him wear them, and whoever does not find sandals and finds khuffs, let him wear them."
"3116","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Hajjaj, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Shatha informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymunah while he was in the state of ihram."
"3117","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us that he heard Tawus and Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas both informing from Ibn Abbas that he said: Dubaa bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I am a heavy woman and I want Hajj, so how do you order me, how shall I enter ihram. He said: Enter ihram and stipulate that my release is where You detain me. He said: So she reached her destination."
"3118","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed women who visit graves and those who take mosques and lamps over them. Hajjaj said: Shubah said: I think he means the Jews."
"3119","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas: How shall I pray when I am in Makkah if I do not pray with the imam. And he said: Two rakahs, the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3120","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Maymunah became junub, and Maymunah washed in a bowl and a remainder remained, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to wash from it, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have already washed from it. And he, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Water is not affected by janabah, or he said: Water does not become impure."
"3121","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Fudayl ibn Amr, he said: I think, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed tamattu. And Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Abu Bakr and Umar forbade mutah. And Ibn Abbas said: What does Urayyah say. He said: He says Abu Bakr and Umar forbade mutah. And Ibn Abbas said: I think they will perish. I say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and they say: Abu Bakr and Umar forbade."
"3122","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have indeed been commanded with the siwak until I thought that a Quran or revelation would descend upon me concerning it."
"3123","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank milk then called for water and rinsed his mouth, then he said: It has fat in it."
"3124","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yala ibn Muslim informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you was revealed concerning Abdullah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays ibn Adi al-Sahmi when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him in the expedition."
"3125","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I collected al-Muhkam in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away while I was a boy of ten years. He said: So I said to him: What is al-Muhkam. He said: Al-Mufassal."
"3126","Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur informed us, from Ibn Sirin, that a funeral passed by al-Hasan and Ibn Abbas, and al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas did not stand, and al-Hasan said to Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood for it. And he said: He stood and he sat."
"3127","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to give permission to the people of Badr and give permission to me along with them, and some of them said: He gives permission to this young boy along with us, while among our sons are those like him. And Umar said: He is of those you have known. He said: So one day he gave them permission and gave me permission along with them, and he asked them about this surah: When the help of Allah and the conquest comes. And they said: He ordered His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when conquest was granted him, to seek His forgiveness and turn to Him. And he said to me: What do you say, O Ibn Abbas. He said: I said: It is not so, but He informed His Prophet, upon him prayer and peace, of the approach of his term, and said: When the help of Allah and the conquest comes, the conquest of Makkah, and you see the people entering the religion of Allah in crowds, that is a sign of your death, so glorify with the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness, indeed He is ever Accepting of repentance. And he said to them: How do you blame me for what you see."
"3128","Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for Hajj, and when he arrived he circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and he did not shorten and did not exit ihram because of the hady, and he ordered whoever had not driven the hady to circumambulate and to run and to shorten or shave, then to exit ihram."
"3129","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah informed me, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Which drink is best. He said: Sweet cold."
"3130","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah informed us, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray thirteen rakahs at night."
"3131","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was playing with the boys, and I hid from him behind a door, and he called me and gave me a push, then he sent me to Muawiyah, and I returned to him and said: He is eating."
"3132","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib, Bahz said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, saying: al-Sab, and Ibn Jafar said: Ibn Jaththamah, gave to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a side of a donkey while he was in ihram, and he returned it. Bahz said: A hindpart of a donkey, or he said: A leg of a donkey."
"3133","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I passed with Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas on one of the roads of Medina, and there were youths who had set up a chicken to shoot at it, each miss going to them. He said: So he became angry and said: Who did this. He said: So they dispersed. And Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed whoever mutilates an animal."
"3134","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: I heard al-Shabi, he said: One who passed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by an isolated grave informed me, and he led them and they lined up behind him. So I said: O Abu Amr, who narrated to you. He said: Ibn Abbas."
"3135","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only said: For one who has land to lend it to his brother is better for him."
"3136","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he was at the Stone with a mihjan striking the Stone with it and kissing it, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims. If a drop of Zaqqum were dropped upon the earth it would spoil the livelihood of the people of this world, so how about one whose food it is and who has no food other than it."
"3137","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman narrating from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: A woman rode the sea and vowed to fast a month, then she died before she fasted, so her sister came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and he ordered her to fast on her behalf."
"3138","al-Qawariri narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Amash, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: If a drop of Zaqqum, and he mentioned it."
"3139","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No deed is better than in these days, meaning the ten days. He said: So it was said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah. He said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, except one who goes out with himself and his wealth then does not return with anything of that."
"3140","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I prayed behind a foolish old man the Zuhr prayer and he said takbir in it twenty-two times, saying takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head from prostration. And Ibn Abbas said: May you have no mother, that is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3141","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade on the day of Khaybar every taloned bird and every fanged beast."
"3142","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Abu Abd al-Samad said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade al-mujaththamah and al-jallalah. Abu Abd al-Samad said: He forbade the milk of al-jallalah and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"3143","Abu Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the milk of al-jallalah and al-mujaththamah and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"3144","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Ibn Bakr said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was offered the daughter of Hamzah to marry her, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing, for what is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by nursing."
"3145","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that a man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, and he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and he ordered him to give charity of a dinar or half a dinar."
"3146","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"3147","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Said informed us, from Qatadah, he said: Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say at distress: There is no god but Allah, the Mighty, the Forbearing, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth and Lord of the Noble Throne. Yazid said: Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Noble Throne."
"3148","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed for the people of Medina Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam. He said: They are for them and for whoever comes upon them of others intending Hajj and Umrah, then from where one begins until that reaches the people of Makkah."
"3149","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu Hassan al-Araj narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then a sacrificial camel was brought and he marked the right side of its hump then wiped the blood from it and garlanded it with two sandals, then he called for his mount and rode it, and when it stood upright with him at al-Bayda he entered ihram for Hajj."
"3150","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This and this are equal, meaning the little finger and the thumb."
"3151","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed. Hajjaj said: Allah cursed men who imitate women and women who imitate men."
"3152","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating that he heard a man of Banu Tamim, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about a mans saying with his finger, meaning thus, in prayer. He said: That is sincerity. And he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, indeed commanded us with the siwak until we thought that something would be revealed to him concerning it, and I indeed saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"3153","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz said: Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, Bahz said: Adi ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out on the day of Adha or the day of Fitr, he said: And my greater thought is that he said the day of Fitr, and he prayed two rakahs, praying neither before them nor after them, then he came to the women, and with him was Bilal, and he ordered them to give charity, and the woman began throwing her earring and her necklace, and Bahz did not doubt, he said the day of Fitr, and he said her necklace."
"3154","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Adi ibn Thabit and Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: One of them raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Jibril used to stuff mud in the mouth of Pharaoh for fear that he would say: There is no god but Allah."
"3155","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Do not take anything with a soul as a target."
"3156","Hashim narrated to us the same, he said: meaning Shubah said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3157","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the nabidh of jars and about gourds and hantam, and Ibn Abbas said: Whoever is pleased to forbid what Allah and His Messenger forbade, let him forbid nabidh."
"3158","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The month is complete, twenty-nine."
"3159","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mushash, he said: I asked Ata ibn Abi Rabah, and he narrated from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the young boys of Banu Hashim and their weak ones to move on from Jam by night."
"3160","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, he said: I heard Muslim al-Batin narrating from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to recite in the Fajr prayer Alif Lam Mim, the revelation, al-Sajdah, and Has there come upon man, and on Friday Surah al-Jumuah and al-Munafiqin."
"3161","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman and Mansur, from Dharr, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, that they said: O Messenger of Allah, we talk to ourselves about something, for one of us to be charcoal would be more beloved to him than to speak of it. He said: So one of them said: Praise be to Allah Who could only manage whispering against you, and the other said: Praise be to Allah Who turned his affair back to whispering."
"3162","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left Medina in Ramadan at the conquest of Makkah, and he fasted until he came to Usfan, then he called for a large cup of drink or a vessel and drank, and Ibn Abbas used to say: Whoever wishes fasts and whoever wishes breaks the fast."
"3163","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: My aunt Umm Hufayd gave to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ghee and aqit and lizards, and he ate of the ghee and the aqit and left the lizards out of disgust, and it was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and if it were forbidden it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3164","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Medina and there were the Jews fasting the day of Ashura, so he asked them about that, and they said: This is the day in which Musa prevailed over Pharaoh. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: You are closer to Musa than they are, so fast it."
"3165","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah, when He created them, knows best what they would have done."
"3166","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya Abu Umar, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dubba and muzaffat and naqir."
"3167","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Affan said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, from Ibn Abbas, and Affan said, meaning in his hadith: al-Hakam informed me, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb, I said: Who is Suhayb. He said: A man of the people of Basra, from Ibn Abbas, that he was on a donkey, he and a boy of Banu Hashim, and he passed in front of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, and he did not leave, and two slave girls of Banu Abd al-Muttalib came and took hold of the knees of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he separated between them, or parted between them, and he did not leave."
"3168","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Said ibn Jubayr, Bahz said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Sab ibn Jaththamah gave to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while at Qudayd and while in ihram, a hindpart of a donkey, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned it dripping with blood."
"3169","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he spent the night with his aunt Maymunah, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came after the last Isha, and prayed four, then slept, then stood and said: Has the boy slept, or a word like it. He said: So he stood praying, and I stood to his left, and he took me and placed me to his right, then he prayed five, then he slept until I heard his snoring, then he went out and prayed."
"3170","Husayn narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my aunt Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Isha then came and prayed four, then slept, then stood and prayed four, and said: Has the little boy slept, or a word like it. He said: So I came and stood to his left, and he placed me to his right, then he prayed five rakahs then two rakahs, then he slept until I heard his snoring, then he went out to prayer."
"3171","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I was aided by al-Saba and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur."
"3172","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, Rawh said: al-Hakam narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: This is an Umrah which we enjoyed, so whoever does not have a hady with him, let him exit ihram completely, for Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"3173","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari al-Tai, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about selling palm trees, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling palm trees until it is eaten from or eaten from it and until it is weighed. He said: So I said: What is weighed. And a man with him said: Until it is estimated."
"3174","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, and a kid goat began wanting to pass in front of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he began advancing and retreating. Hajjaj said: Warding it off and retreating, until he was seen behind the kid."
"3175","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Hakam narrated to me, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night in the house of my aunt Maymunah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Isha then came and prayed four, then he said: Has the little boy slept, or the boy. Shubah said: Or something like this. He said: Then he slept. He said: Then he stood and performed wudu, he said: I do not remember his wudu. He said: Then he stood and prayed, and I stood to his left. He said: So he placed me to his right, then he prayed five rakahs. He said: Then he prayed two rakahs. He said: Then he slept until I heard his snoring, then he prayed two rakahs, then he went out to prayer."
"3176","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Hakam narrated to us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out in Ramadan while raiding Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted until he came to Qudayd, then he called for a cup of milk and drank it. He said: Then his companions broke the fast until they came to Makkah."
"3177","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"3178","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to me, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab narrating that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"3179","Hajjaj, Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, he said: The cousin of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, and he attributed him to his father. He said: And he mentioned that he was taken on the night journey and that he saw Musa, upon him peace, dark, tall, as if of the men of Shanua, and he mentioned that he saw Isa, medium build, inclining to redness and whiteness, curly, and he mentioned that he saw the Dajjal and Malik the keeper of the Fire."
"3180","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, he said: The cousin of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us, he said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, and he attributed him to his father, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned when he was taken on the night journey and said: Musa, dark, tall, as if of the men of Shanua, and he said: Isa, curly, medium build, and he mentioned Malik the keeper of Hell, and he mentioned the Dajjal."
"3181","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu Hassan al-Araj, he said: A man of Banu al-Hujaym said to Ibn Abbas: What is this fatwa which has spread among the people, that whoever circumambulates the House has exited ihram. And he said: The sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, even if you dislike it."
"3182","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, that Abu Hassan al-Araj said: A man of Banu al-Hujaym called Fulan ibn Bujayl said to Ibn Abbas: What is this fatwa which has spread among the people: Whoever circumambulates the House has exited ihram. And he said: The sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, even if you dislike it. Shubah said: I say: shaghabat, and I do not know how it is."
"3183","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, and he mentioned the hadith, and he said: It has spread among the people."
"3184","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I came while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying at Mina, and I was upon a donkey, so I left it in front of the row and entered into the prayer, and I had nearly reached puberty, and no one objected to that."
"3185","And I read to Abd al-Rahman this hadith, he said: I came riding upon a she-ass, and I was on that day nearly reaching puberty, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying with the people, so I passed in front of part of the row, then I dismounted and sent off the she-ass and entered into the row, and no one disapproved of that against me."
"3186","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank from Zamzam while standing."
"3187","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Abu Zumayl narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: When the Haruriyyah went out and separated, I said to them: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of al-Hudaybiyah made peace with the polytheists, and he said to Ali: Write, O Ali, this is what Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has made peace upon. They said: If we knew that you are the Messenger of Allah we would not have fought you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Erase, O Ali. O Allah, You know that I am Your Messenger. Erase, O Ali, and write: This is what Muhammad ibn Abdullah has made peace upon. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah is indeed better than Ali, yet he erased himself, and his erasing that did not erase him from prophethood. Have you left this. They said: Yes."
"3188","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Ibn Abbas wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If people were given by their claims, some people would claim the blood and wealth of people, but the oath is upon the defendant."
"3189","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died and did not bequeath."
"3190","Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a bowl of tharid and said: Eat from around it and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends in its middle. Ibn Jafar said: From its sides, or from its edges."
"3191","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Awanah, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Do not move with it your tongue to hasten with it, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to endure hardship from the revelation, and he used to move his lips. He said: So Ibn Abbas said to me: I move my lips as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to move, and Said said to me: I move as I saw Ibn Abbas moving his lips. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: Do not move with it your tongue to hasten with it. Indeed upon Us is its collection and its recitation. He said: Its collection in your chest, then We recite it. So when We have recited it, follow its recitation, so listen to it and be silent. Then indeed upon Us is its clarification. So after that, when Jibril departed, he recited it as he had taught him."
"3192","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us ahead, the young boys of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, upon our donkeys, on the night of Muzdalifah, and he began patting our thighs and saying: O my sons, do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises. Ibn Abbas said: I do not think anyone stones until the sun rises."
"3193","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, from al-Hasan, meaning al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, that a kid goat fell in front of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, and he did not cut off his prayer."
"3194","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my aunt Maymunah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at night and attended to his need, then washed his face and his hands, then stood and came to the waterskin and loosened its tie, then performed wudu, a wudu between the two wudus, not excessive, yet thorough, then he stood and prayed, and I stood and stretched myself, disliking that he should see that I had been watching him, and I performed wudu, and he stood praying, and I stood to his left, and he took me by my ear and turned me to his right, and the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was completed as thirteen rakahs, then he lay down and slept until he breathed heavily, and when he slept he breathed heavily, then Bilal came to him and announced the prayer to him, so he stood and prayed and did not perform wudu, and he used to say in his supplication: O Allah, place in my heart light, and in my sight light, and in my hearing light, and to my right light, and to my left light, and above me light, and beneath me light, and before me light, and behind me light, and magnify for me light. Kurayb said: And seven in the chest. He said: So I met one of the sons of Abbas and he narrated them to me, and he mentioned my sinews and my flesh and my blood and my hair and my skin. He said: And he mentioned two traits."
"3195","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, that a woman raised a boy of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for him. He said: Yes, and for you a reward."
"3196","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, the same."
"3197","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the whiteness of his armpits would be seen when he prostrated. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father saying: Shubah used to check the people of hadith, and he said one day: What happened to that handsome youth, meaning Shababab."
"3198","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Walah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Any skin that is tanned has become pure."
"3199","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, continued the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"3200","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, he said: Najdah ibn Amir wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about things, and I witnessed Ibn Abbas when he read his letter and when he wrote his reply, and he wrote to him: You asked me, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And you asked: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kill any of the children of the polytheists. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not kill any of them, and you, so do not kill any of them, unless you know of them what al-Khadir knew of the boy when he killed him."
"3201","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from 'Asim from Abu Razin from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When 'When the help of Allah comes and the conquest' was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that his soul had been announced to him, and it was said: 'When the help of Allah comes,' the whole Surah."
"3202","Abu Ahmad and Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn 'Uqbah from Kurayb from Ibn 'Abbas that a woman raised a boy of hers to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is reward."
"3203","Waki' narrated to us: al-Mas'udi narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the weak among his family from Jam' and said: Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises."
"3204","Waki' and 'Abd al-Rahman both said: Sufyan narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from al-Hasan al-'Urani from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When you have stoned the Jamrah, everything has become lawful for you except women. He said: Then a man said: And perfume? 'Abd al-Rahman said: Then a man said to him: O Abu al-'Abbas. And Ibn 'Abbas said: As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smearing his head with musk; is that perfume or not?"
"3205","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed al-'Aqiq as the Miqat for the people of the east."
"3206","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Hassan al-A'raj from Ibn 'Abbas that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, he entered Ihram for Hajj, and he marked his sacrificial animal on the right side of the hump and wiped the blood from it, and hung two sandals on it."
"3207","Waki' narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated to us from his father from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two blessings in which many people are cheated: leisure and health."
"3208","Waki' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from 'Amr ibn Murrah from Abu al-Bakhtari who said: We sighted the crescent of Ramadan at Dhat 'Irq, so we sent a man to Ibn 'Abbas and he asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended it to its sighting."
"3209","Waki' narrated to us from Shu'bah from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Madinah fasting in the month of Ramadan, then when he reached Qudayd he broke his fast, and he remained not fasting until he entered Makkah."
"3210","Waki' narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn 'Abbas that they disputed about the fasting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of 'Arafah, so Umm al-Fadl sent milk to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he drank it."
"3211","Waki' and Muhammad ibn Ja'far both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, Waki' said: at al-Qahuhah, while he was fasting."
"3212","Waki' narrated to us: Hajib ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he heard it from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj who said: I came to Ibn 'Abbas while he was pillowing his cloak in Zamzam, and I said: Tell me about 'Ashura, which day do I fast it? He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram, count, then wake on the ninth fasting. He said: I said: Is that how Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast it? He said: Yes."
"3213","Waki' narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn 'Abbas from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umayr, freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I remain until next year, I shall fast the ninth day."
"3214","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not eat food from its top, but eat from its sides, for blessing descends from its top."
"3215","Waki' and Ibn Ja'far both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from 'Adi ibn Thabit, Ibn Ja'far said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take anything with a soul as a target."
"3216","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan, and 'Abd al-Razzaq said: al-Thawri informed us from Simak ibn Harb from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take anything with a soul as a target. 'Abd al-Razzaq said: He forbade taking anything with a soul as a target."
"3217","Waki' narrated to us from Isra'il from Jabir from Abu al-Duha from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried him and carried his brother, this one in front of him and this one behind him."
"3218","Waki' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the rump of a wild donkey dripping with blood while he was in Ihram, and he returned it."
"3219","Waki' narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, I heard from him, he said: The lizard was mentioned before Ibn 'Abbas, and a man among his companions said: It was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he neither made it lawful nor unlawful. He said: Evil is what you say; rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent making lawful and making unlawful. Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith came to visit her sister Maymunah bint al-Harith bringing food containing lizard meat, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after taking an evening drink, and it was offered to him, and he was told that it contained lizard meat, so he withdrew his hand, and those with him ate it; had it been unlawful he would have forbidden them from it. And he said: It is not in our land, and we find it distasteful."
"3220","Waki' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Qatadah from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This and this are equal, joining his thumb and his little finger."
"3221","Waki' and Abu 'Amir both said: Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."
"3222","Waki' narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas from 'Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi' ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The widow is more entitled to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is to be consulted about herself. He said: And her silence is her consent."
"3223","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Salamah from 'Imran Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Call upon your Lord for us to turn al-Safa into gold for us; if it becomes gold we shall follow you and know that what you say is as you say. So he asked his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and Jibril came to him and said: If you wish, this al-Safa will become gold for them, then whoever among them disbelieves after that, I shall punish him with a punishment with which I punish no one of the worlds; and if you wish, We shall open to them the doors of repentance. He said: O my Lord, rather open to them the doors of repentance."
"3224","Waki' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to perform Hajj and she has died. He said: What do you think, if she had a debt, would you pay it? He said: Yes. He said: Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more deserving of fulfillment."
"3225","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas who said: I attended the 'Id with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and they began with the prayer before the sermon."
"3226","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan who said: I heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abis who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the day of 'Id, and were it not for my place with him I would not have witnessed it due to young age, and he came to the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt and prayed two rak'ahs. He said: Then he delivered the sermon and commanded charity. He said: And he did not mention Adhan or Iqamah."
"3227","'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then delivered the sermon, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar and 'Uthman at the 'Id, without Adhan or Iqamah."
"3228","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Shu'bah from Sulayman from Muslim al-Batin from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There are no days in which deeds are better than these days. It was said: Not even Jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even Jihad in the path of Allah, except a man who went out with himself and his wealth and returned with none of it."
"3229","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: 'Ata' narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbas, he said, and he did not hear it, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me at dawn from Jam' with the heavy baggage of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3230","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me that Sa'id ibn Jubayr informed him that Ibn 'Abbas informed him, he said: A man in Ihram came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he fell from above his head and was crushed to death, and he died. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and Sidr, dress him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah."
"3231","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me from Abu Ma'bad from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No woman shall travel except with a Mahram with her. And a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have been enlisted in such-and-such expedition and my wife is going for Hajj. He said: Go back and perform Hajj with her."
"3232","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us who said: 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Abu Ma'bad, freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, reporting from Ibn 'Abbas, Rawh said: So perform Hajj with her."
"3233","Yahya narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: 'Ikrimah narrated to us from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in Ihram, and he was cupped while he was in Ihram."
"3234","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: 'Ata' informed me from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand with a cloth until he licks it or has it licked."
"3235","Yahya narrated to us from Dawud ibn Qays who said: Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and 'Asr and Maghrib and 'Isha' without rain or travel. They said: O Abu 'Abbas, what did he intend by that? He said: Leniency for his Ummah."
"3236","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Habib ibn Thabit narrated to us from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed with them during an eclipse eight rak'ahs: he recited, then bowed, then rose, then recited, then bowed, then rose, then recited, then bowed, then rose, then recited, then bowed, then rose, then prostrated. He said: And the other was like it."
"3237","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'bah: Qatadah narrated to us from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn 'Abbas who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Why do you not marry the daughter of Hamzah? He said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"3238","Yahya narrated to us: Malik informed us who said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Ibn 'Abbas that a woman from Khath'am said: O Messenger of Allah, the obligation of Allah in Hajj has reached my father as a very old man unable to sit firmly on the mount; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"3239","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas: He invited his brother 'Ubaydullah on the day of 'Arafah to food. He said: I am fasting. He said: You are Imams who are followed; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call for a milk vessel on this day and drink. And Yahya once said: A household who are followed."
"3240","Yahya narrated to us from 'Imran Abu Bakr who said: 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us who said: Ibn 'Abbas said to me: Shall I show you a woman of the people of Paradise? He said: I said: Yes. He said: This black woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I suffer fits and become uncovered, so call upon Allah for me. He said: If you wish, be patient and for you is Paradise, and if you wish, I shall call upon Allah for you to cure you. She said: No, rather I shall be patient; but call upon Allah that I not become uncovered, or that nothing be uncovered from me. He said: So he called for her."
"3241","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'bah who said: Qatadah narrated to me from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn 'Abbas, Yahya said: Shu'bah used to raise it: The dog and the menstruating woman cut off the prayer."
"3242","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: I was told from al-Zuhri from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the bee and the ant and the shrike and the hoopoe. Yahya said: And I saw in the book of Sufyan: from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Labid from al-Zuhri."
"3243","Yahya narrated to us: 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas: I spent the night in the house of my aunt Maymunah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, loosened the waterskin, performed ablution, stood for prayer, and I stood to his left, so he took me by my right and turned me and placed me at his right, and I prayed with him."
"3244","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'bah who said: Qatadah narrated to me; Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us who said: I heard Qatadah who said: I heard Abu Hassan from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then called for his sacrificial camel and marked the right side of its hump and wiped the blood from it and hung two sandals on it, then called for his mount, and when it stood straight with him on al-Bayda', he entered Ihram for Hajj."
"3245","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: Sa'id ibn al-Huwayrith narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself to answer the call of nature, then food was brought and he ate it without touching water."
"3246","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'bah: Abu Bishr narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: Umm Hufayd, the aunt of Ibn 'Abbas, gave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter and dried cheese and lizards, and he ate the clarified butter and dried cheese and left the lizards out of distaste, and it was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had it been unlawful it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3247","Yahya narrated to us from Ajlah who said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrated to us from Ibn 'Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeating speech, and said: Whatever Allah wills and you will. He said: You have made me an equal to Allah; rather whatever Allah alone wills."
"3248","Yahya and Isma'il, in meaning, both said: 'Awf narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Husayn narrated to me from Abu al-'Aliyah al-Riyahi from Ibn 'Abbas, Yahya said: 'Awf did not know whether 'Abdullah or al-Fadl, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of al-'Aqabah while he was standing on his mount: Bring pebbles to me. So I picked for him pebbles of the size of Khadhf, and he placed them in his hand and said: With the likes of these, twice, and he said with his hand, and Yahya indicated that he raised it, and said: Beware of excess, for those before you perished only through excess in religion."
"3249","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was turned toward the Ka'bah, they said: O Messenger of Allah, what about our brothers who died before that, who died praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And Allah would never waste your faith."
"3250","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from Ayyub and Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah, one of them adding to the other, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: Ibn 'Abbas said: The first thing women took of the waist-wrapper was from Umm Isma'il; she took a waist-wrapper to conceal her trace from Sarah. Then he mentioned the Hadith. Ibn 'Abbas said: May Allah have mercy on Umm Isma'il; had she left Zamzam, or he said: had she not scooped from the water, Zamzam would have been a flowing spring. Ibn 'Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He found Umm Isma'il there, and she loved company, so they settled and sent to their families, and they settled with them. And he said in his Hadith: She descended from al-Safa until, when she reached the valley, she raised the edge of her garment, then ran as a weary person runs until she passed the valley, then she came to al-Marwah and stood on it and looked whether she saw anyone, and she saw no one, and she did that seven times. Ibn 'Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is why people run between them."
"3251","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us who said: 'Uthman al-Jazari informed me that Miqsam, freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, informed him from Ibn 'Abbas about His saying: And when those who disbelieved plotted against you to restrain you. He said: Quraysh conferred one night at Makkah; some said: When morning comes, restrain him with bonds, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and some said: Rather kill him; and some said: Rather expel him. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, informed His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, and 'Ali spent that night on the bed of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until he reached the cave, and the idolaters spent the night guarding 'Ali thinking him the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When morning came they rushed upon him, and when they saw 'Ali, Allah turned back their plot. They said: Where is this companion of yours? He said: I do not know. So they followed his tracks, and when they reached the mountain they were confused, and they climbed the mountain and passed by the cave, and they saw a spider's web on its entrance, and they said: Had he entered here there would be no spider's web on its entrance. And he remained in it three nights."
"3252","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us from Qatadah from Abu al-'Aliyah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one should say that I am better than Yunus ibn Matta; he attributed him to his father; he committed a sin, then his Lord chose him."
"3253","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest: Its grass shall not be cut, its game shall not be frightened, its thorny trees shall not be cut, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it. Al-'Abbas said: Except al-Idhkhir, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except al-Idhkhir, for it is lawful."
"3254","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from Ayyub from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said, I do not know except that he raised the Hadith, he said: He used to command killing snakes and say: Whoever leaves them out of fear or dread of reprisal is not of us. He said: And Ibn 'Abbas said: The Jinn snakes are the transformed of the Jinn, as monkeys were transformed from the Children of Isra'il."
"3255","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha' from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Snakes are the transformed of the Jinn."
"3256","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us who said: al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me from Tawus who said: I was with Ibn 'Abbas when Zayd ibn Thabit said to him: Do you give Fatwa that the menstruating woman may depart before her last contact is with the House? He said: Yes. He said: Then do not give Fatwa to that effect. Ibn 'Abbas said to him: If not, then ask such-and-such Ansari woman whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to do that. So Zayd ibn Thabit returned to him laughing and saying: I see you have spoken the truth."
"3257","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us who said: Abu Hadir informed me who said: Ibn 'Umar was asked about the earthen jar in which drink is made. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. So the man went to Ibn 'Abbas and mentioned to him what Ibn 'Umar said. Ibn 'Abbas said: He spoke the truth. The man said to Ibn 'Abbas: Which jar did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid? He said: Everything made of clay."
"3258","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us who said: Ibn Shihab informed me from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah from Ibn 'Abbas from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he went out in the year of the Conquest in the month of Ramadan and fasted until he reached al-Kadid, then he broke his fast."
"3259","Ibn Jurayj informed us who said: 'Ata' informed me who said: We attended with Ibn 'Abbas the funeral of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at Sarif. Ibn 'Abbas said: This is the wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when you lift her bier, do not shake it or disturb it, and be gentle, for he used to divide among eight and not divide for one. 'Ata' said: The one for whom he did not divide is Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab."
"3260","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us who said: Sa'id ibn al-Huwayrith informed me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself and answered the call of nature, then he came and food was offered to him, and he ate without touching water."
"3261","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us who said: 'Ata' informed me that Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the aunt of Ibn 'Abbas, died. He said: So I went with him to Sarif. He said: He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Mother of the Believers, do not shake her or disturb her; be gentle, for with the Prophet of Allah were nine women, and he used to divide among eight and not divide for the ninth, meaning Safiyyah bint Huyayy. 'Ata' said: She was the last of them to die; she died at Madinah."
"3262","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us from Ibn Khuthaym from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Dhakwan, freedman of 'A'ishah, that he sought permission for Ibn 'Abbas to visit 'A'ishah while she was dying, and with her was her nephew 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman. He said: This is Ibn 'Abbas seeking permission to visit you, and he is among your best sons. She said: Leave me from Ibn 'Abbas and his commendation. 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman said to her: He is a reciter of the Book of Allah, learned in the religion of Allah; give him permission to greet you and bid you farewell. She said: Then give him permission if you wish. He said: So he gave him permission, and Ibn 'Abbas entered, then greeted and sat, and said: Rejoice, O Mother of the Believers; by Allah, there is nothing between you and the removal from you of all harm and hardship, or he said: toil, and meeting the loved ones, Muhammad and his party, or he said: his companions, except that your soul leaves your body. She said: And also. Ibn 'Abbas said: You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to him, and he loved none but one who is good, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed your innocence from above seven heavens, so there is no mosque on earth except it is recited in it by night and by day, and your necklace fell at al-Abwa', and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at the dwelling with the people with him seeking it, or he said: looking for it, until the people woke without water, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Then seek clean earth, the verse, and that was a concession for people in general because of you; by Allah, you are blessed. She said: Leave me, O Ibn 'Abbas, from this; by Allah, I wish I were something forgotten, out of mind."
"3263","Sufyan narrated to us from 'Amr from Tawus who said: My most learned of them informed me, he said: But for one to lend his brother is better for him than to give it to him for a known rent."
"3264","Sufyan narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi from Yazid ibn Hurmuz who said: Najdah wrote to Ibn 'Abbas asking him about killing children. So he wrote to him: You wrote asking me about killing children, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not kill them, and you, do not kill them, unless you know of them what the companion of Musa knew of the boy."
"3265","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight together and seven together. I said to Ibn 'Abbas: Why did he do that? He said: He intended not to burden his Ummah."
"3266","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: I came to him at 'Arafah and found him eating pomegranate. He said: Come near and eat; perhaps you are fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast it. And once he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast this day."
"3267","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged the people of al-Ta'if, he freed some of their slaves."
"3268","Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Humayd ibn 'Ali al-'Uqayli informed us: al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim narrated to us from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed when he traveled two rak'ahs, and when he stayed four. He said: Ibn 'Abbas said: Whoever prays four in travel is like whoever prays two in residence. He said: And Ibn 'Abbas said: Prayer was not shortened except once, where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs and the people prayed one rak'ah each."
"3269","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali narrated to me that he heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab reporting that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who gives charity then returns in his charity is like the dog that vomits then eats its vomit."
"3270","Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us from Za'idah from Simak from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, then the Qiblah was changed afterwards."
"3271","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Muhammad ibn 'Ali from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he rose at night and cleaned his teeth, then prayed two rak'ahs, then slept, then rose and cleaned his teeth and performed ablution and prayed two rak'ahs, until he had prayed six, then he prayed Witr with three, and prayed two rak'ahs."
"3272","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us that he witnessed al-Nadr ibn Anas narrating to Qatadah that he witnessed 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas giving Fatwa to people without mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his Fatwa, until a man came and said: I am an Iraqi man, and I make these images. He said: Come near, two or three times. I heard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever makes an image in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it, and he will not breathe."
"3273","Zakariyya ibn 'Adi informed us: 'Ubaydullah informed us from 'Abd al-Karim from Qays ibn Habtar al-Tamimi from Ibn 'Abbas from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the price of wine and the dowry of the prostitute and the price of the dog, and said: If one comes to you seeking the price of the dog, fill his palms with dust."
"3274","Zakariyya informed us: 'Ubaydullah informed us from 'Abd al-Karim from Qays ibn Habtar from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden to you wine and gambling and the Kubbah, and said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"3275","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from 'Amr ibn Sa'id from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to a man about something, and said: Praise belongs to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help; whoever Allah guides, none can misguide him, and whoever He misguides, none can guide him; and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"3276","al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Muslim al-'Abdi narrated to us: Abu al-Mutawakkil narrated to us from Ibn 'Abbas that he spent the night with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, went out, looked at the sky, then recited this verse in Al 'Imran: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth, until he reached: Glory be to You, save us from the punishment of the Fire. Then he returned to the house, cleaned his teeth, performed ablution, then stood and prayed, then lay down, then rose, went out, looked at the sky, then recited this verse, then returned, cleaned his teeth, performed ablution, then stood and prayed. Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us from Simak from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In buried treasure is the fifth."
"3277","Abu Ahmad and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr both said: Isra'il narrated to us from Simak from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of his chamber, Yahya said: It had almost receded from him, and he said to his companions: A man will come to you looking at you with the eye of Satan; when you see him, do not speak to him. Then a blue-eyed man came, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he called him and said: Why do you revile me, you and your companions? He said: Wait as you are until I bring them to you. He said: So he went and brought them, and they began to swear by Allah that they neither said nor did, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: On the day Allah will raise them all, and they will swear to Him as they swear to you, to the end of the verse."
"3278","Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us: Ibn Lahi'ah informed me who said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed me from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited during the eclipse of the sun, and we heard no letter from him."
"3279","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: al-Hakam narrated to us from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted on the day of the conquest of Makkah until he reached Qudayd, then he was brought a cup of milk, so he broke his fast and commanded the people to break their fast."
"3280","Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal informed me: 'Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon with his back to al-Multazam."
"3281","Zayd ibn al-Hubab who said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban informed me who said: I heard 'Amr ibn Dinar saying: One who heard Ibn 'Abbas informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom? He said: To Allah and to His Messenger and to the leaders of the believers."
"3282","'Abd al-A'la narrated to us from Khalid from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was in Ihram."
"3283","'Abd al-A'la narrated to us from Khalid from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while he was in Ihram."
"3284","'Abd al-A'la from Khalid from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave him his wage; had it been unlawful he would not have given him."
"3285","'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us from Matar from 'Ata' that Ibn al-Zubayr prayed Maghrib and gave Salam in two rak'ahs and rose to touch the Stone, and the people glorified Allah, so he said: What is the matter with you? He said: Then he prayed what remained and prostrated two prostrations. He said: That was mentioned to Ibn 'Abbas, and he said: He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3286","Yazid narrated to us: al-Hajjaj informed us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas, and from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"3287","Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, informed us: al-Hajjaj informed us from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd from 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and ate with her a shoulder of meat, then went out to prayer without renewing ablution."
"3288","Yazid narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn 'Abbas and Sa'id ibn Jubayr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers while traveling."
"3289","Yazid narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas that he did not hold that one should stop at al-Abtah, and he says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only stayed there for 'A'ishah."
"3290","Yazid narrated to us who said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Dawud ibn Husayn from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter Zaynab to Abu al-'As, her husband, with her first marriage after two years, without making a new dowry."
"3291","Yazid narrated to us who said: Humayd informed us from al-Hasan who said: Ibn 'Abbas delivered a sermon to the people at the end of Ramadan and said: O people of Basrah, pay the Zakat of your fast. He said: The people began to look at one another. He said: Whoever is here of the people of Madinah, stand and teach your brothers, for they do not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed the charity of Ramadan as half a Sa' of wheat, or a Sa' of barley, or a Sa' of dates, upon the slave and the free, the male and the female."
"3292","Yazid narrated to us: Nafi' informed us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: Ibn 'Abbas wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The oath is upon the defendant, and had people been given by their claims, people would have claimed much wealth and blood."
"3293","Yazid narrated to us: 'Imran ibn Hudayr informed us, and Mu'adh said: 'Imran, meaning Ibn Hudayr, narrated to us from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said: A man stood to Ibn 'Abbas and said: Prayer. He was silent to him, then he said: Prayer. He was silent to him, then he said: Prayer. He said: Do you teach us about prayer? We used to combine the two prayers with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or in the time of the Messenger of Allah; Mu'adh said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3294","Yazid narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah informed us from Qatadah from 'Ikrimah who said: I prayed behind an old man at al-Abtah and he said twenty-two Takbirs. So I came to Ibn 'Abbas and mentioned that to him. He said: May you lose your mother, that is the prayer of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3295","Yazid narrated to us: Sa'id informed us from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr that 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-'Abbas narrated to them that Ibn 'Abbas informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a roasted shoulder, and he ate from it and ate his fill, then prayed without performing ablution from that."
"3296","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from Qariz ibn Shaybah from Abu Ghatfan who said: I entered upon Ibn 'Abbas and found him performing ablution, and he rinsed his mouth and nose, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Snuff water twice thoroughly, or three times."
"3297","Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from one who heard Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the woman and the slave from the spoils less than what the army received."
"3298","Yazid narrated to us: al-Hajjaj informed us from al-Minhal from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim visits his brother, entering upon him when his term has not come, and says: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to cure so-and-so of his pain, seven times, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, cures him of it."
"3299","Yazid who said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, informed us from Muhammad ibn 'Ali and from al-Zuhri from Yazid ibn Hurmuz who said: Najdah al-Haruri wrote to Ibn 'Abbas asking him about killing children, and whether women used to attend war with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whether he assigned them a share. Yazid ibn Hurmuz said: And I wrote the letter of Ibn 'Abbas to Najdah. He wrote to him: You wrote asking me about killing children, saying that the learned man, the companion of Musa, killed the boy; had you known of children what that learned man knew, you would kill, but you do not know, so avoid them, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing them. And you wrote asking me about women, whether they attended war with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whether he assigned them a share; they did attend with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but as for assigning them a share, he did not do so, and he used to give them a small gift."
"3300","Yazid narrated to us: Mansur ibn Hayyan informed us who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas that they both bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade al-Dubba' and al-Hantam and al-Muzaffat and al-Naqir. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you from, refrain."
"3301","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, and Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from Abu Hashim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha, then returned to her, and it was her night. He prayed two rak'ahs, then turned and said: Has the boy slept, while I was listening to him. He said: Then I heard him say in his place of prayer: O Allah, place light in my heart, and light in my hearing, and light in my sight, and light in my tongue, and magnify light for me."
"3302","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that Dubaa bint al-Zubayr wanted to perform Hajj, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Stipulate at your ihram: My release is where You have detained me, for that is yours."
"3303","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Sinan, from Ibn Abbas who said: al-Aqra ibn Habis asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj once or every year. He said: Rather once; whoever adds more, it is voluntary."
"3304","Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, and Rawh said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shuba, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to his family, to Mina, on the night of sacrifice, and we stoned the Jamrah at dawn."
"3305","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Shuba who said: Ibn Abbas saw a man prostrating with his forearms spread out, so Ibn Abbas said: This is how a dog lies down. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated, I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"3306","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, and Hammad said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, with the same meaning, from Shuba, from Ibn Abbas who said: I came, I and al-Fadl, on a donkey, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with the people - al-Khayyat, meaning Hammad, said: in an open space - so we passed in front of him while on it until we passed beyond most of the row, and he did not forbid us nor turn us back."
"3307","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Shuba who said: al-Miswar ibn Makhrama visited Ibn Abbas during an illness he was ill with, and saw on him a garment of istabraq and before him a brazier with images on it. He said to him: O Abu Abbas, what is this garment on you. He said: What is it. He said: Istabraq. He said: By Allah, I did not know of it, and I do not think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it except for arrogance and pride, and we, praise be to Allah, are not like that. He said: Then what is this brazier with images on it. Ibn Abbas said: Do you not see how we have burned them with fire."
"3308","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Banu Talha, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas who said: The name of Juwayriya bint al-Harith was Barra, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed her name and called her Juwayriya. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her while she was in her place of prayer glorifying Allah and supplicating Him. He went for his need, then returned to her after the day had risen and said: O Juwayriya, you have remained in your place. She said: I have remained in this place of mine. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have spoken four words, counting them three times, they are better than what you have said: Glory be to Allah to the number of His creation, and glory be to Allah to the pleasure of Himself, and glory be to Allah to the weight of His Throne, and glory be to Allah to the ink of His words, and praise be to Allah the like of that."
"3309","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat, the people hurried, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a caller who called out: O people, righteousness is not in urging horses and mounts. Then I never saw it raising its foreleg running."
"3310","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, said: One who heard Ikrima narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas who said: The one who captured al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib was Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr, and he is Kab ibn Amr, one of Banu Salima. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How did you capture him, O Abu al-Yasar. He said: A man helped me against him whom I have not seen after nor before, his appearance thus, his appearance thus. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A noble angel helped you against him. And he said to al-Abbas: O Abbas, ransom yourself and your brother's son Aqil ibn Abi Talib and Nawfal ibn al-Harith and your ally Utba ibn Jahdam, one of Banu al-Harith ibn Fihr. He said: Then he refused and said: I was a Muslim before that, and they only forced me. He said: Allah knows best your affair; if what you claim is true, Allah will reward you for that, and as for your outward affair, it was against us, so ransom yourself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had taken from him twenty ounces of gold. He said: O Messenger of Allah, count it for me from my ransom. He said: No, that is something Allah has given us from you. He said: Then I have no wealth. He said: Then where is the wealth you placed in Makkah when you left, with Umm al-Fadl, and no one was with you two other than you two, when you said: If I am struck down in this journey of mine, then for al-Fadl is such, and for Qutham is such, and for Abdullah is such. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, no one among people knew of this other than me and her, and I indeed know that you are the Messenger of Allah."
"3311","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, said: Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: Men shaved on the day of Hudaybiya and others shortened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten. He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten. He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten. He said: And those who shorten. They said: Then why, O Messenger of Allah, did you emphasize mercy for those who shave. He said: They did not doubt. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed."
"3312","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat from a shoulder bone, then stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
"3313","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Ata: that he saw no harm in a man entering ihram in a garment dyed with saffron that had been washed, with no loose dye nor stain in it."
"3314","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from al-Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3315","Yazid narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked on the day of Eid to bring out his family. He said: So we went out, and he prayed without adhan nor iqama, then addressed the men, then came to the women and addressed them, then commanded them with charity. I saw a woman throwing her earring and her ring, giving it to Bilal to give in charity."
"3316","Yazid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best day on which you gather is the seventeenth and the nineteenth and the twenty-first. And he said: I never passed by a company of angels on the night I was taken by night except they said: Upon you is cupping, O Muhammad."
"3317","Yazid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Awn informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas who said: We traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between Makkah and Madinah, while we were safe fearing nothing, and he prayed two rak'ahs."
"3318","Yazid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a kohl container with which he applied kohl at sleep, three times in each eye."
"3319","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymuna bint al-Harith at Sarif while in ihram, then consummated with her after he returned, at Sarif."
"3320","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to apply ithmid kohl every night before he slept, and he used to apply kohl in each eye three strokes."
"3321","Waki narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: You are the best nation brought forth for people. He said: They are those who emigrated with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makkah to Madinah."
"3322","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'a, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, led me at the House twice. Then he said: O Muhammad, this is your time and the time of the prophets before you. He prayed with him Dhuhr when the shade was to the extent of the strap, and he prayed with him Maghrib when the fasting person breaks fast and food and drink become lawful."
"3323","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Dhuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha in Madinah without fear nor rain. I said to Ibn Abbas: Why did he do that. He said: So as not to burden his nation."
"3324","Waki narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymuna. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at night and performed ablution. He said: So I stood and performed ablution, then he stood and prayed, and I stood behind him or on his left, and he turned me until he placed me on his right."
"3325","Waki narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Fajr on Friday Alif Lam Mim, the revelation of al-Sajda, and Has there come upon man. Abd al-Rahman said in his hadith: And in Jumu'a with al-Jumu'a and al-Munafiqin."
"3326","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday in Fajr Alif Lam Mim, the revelation of al-Sajda, and Has there come upon man a period of time."
"3327","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a cloak, protecting himself with its excess from the heat of the ground and its cold."
"3328","Waki narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I observed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated, and the whiteness of his armpits could be seen when he prostrated."
"3329","Waki narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn Abbas who said: The prayer was established and I had not prayed the two rak'ahs, so he saw me praying them, then came near and said: Do you want to pray Subh four. It was said to Ibn Abbas: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes."
"3330","Waki narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil al-Awdi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came, took up the recitation from where Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, had reached."
"3331","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kinana, from his father who said: A commander among the commanders sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about prayer for rain. Ibn Abbas said: What prevented him from asking me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out humble, shabby, submissive, unhurried, supplicating, and prayed two rak'ahs as he prays in Eid; he did not deliver a sermon like this sermon of yours."
"3332","Waki narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic ordained the prayer of residence as four, and in travel two, and in fear one, upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3333","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Adiyy ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the day of Fitr or Adha and prayed with the people two rak'ahs, then departed, and did not pray before them nor after them."
"3334","Waki narrated to us, Qurra ibn Khalid and Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled from Makkah and Madinah fearing none but Allah, shortening the prayer."
"3335","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the conquest, but jihad and intention, and when you are mobilized, go forth."
"3336","Waki narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Thursday, and what is Thursday. Then I looked at his tears flowing on his cheeks as if they were a string of pearls. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the tablet and the inkpot, or the shoulder blade, I will write for you a book after which you will never go astray. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is raving."
"3337","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, who heard Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have nabidh made for him in a waterskin."
"3338","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by the Saba wind, and Ad were destroyed by the Dabur wind."
"3339","Waki narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed li'an for pregnancy."
"3340","Waki narrated to us, Abu Isra'il al-Absi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas and al-Fadl, or one of them from the other, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends Hajj, let him hasten, for the sick may sicken, and the mount may stray, and need may present itself."
"3341","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Jamra, from Ibn Abbas who said: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3342","Waki narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your garments is white, so wear it alive and shroud your dead in it, and the best of your kohls is ithmid."
"3343","Waki narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is to be consulted about herself, and her silence is her consent."
"3344","Waki narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dowry of the prostitute and the price of the dog and the price of wine."
"3345","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays ibn Habtar, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith, who said: The price of the dog and the dowry of the prostitute and the price of wine are unlawful."
"3346","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it. I said to Ibn Abbas: Why. He said: Do you not see that they buy with gold while the food is deferred."
"3347","Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah in the year of Hudaybiya, he passed by Quraysh while they were sitting in Dar al-Nadwa. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These have said that you are emaciated, so walk briskly when you arrive, three circuits. He said: When they arrived, they walked briskly three circuits. He said: The polytheists said: Are these those about whom we say they are emaciated. These were not content with walking until they ran."
"3348","Waki narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sulaym, from Ibn Abi Mulayka: that Ibn Abbas wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The defendant has more right to the oath."
"3349","Waki narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Shufay, who heard Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when traveling, prayed two rak'ahs."
"3350","Waki narrated to us, from Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw al-Fadl ibn Abbas gazing at a woman on the evening of Arafa. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thus with his hand over the boy's eye. He said: This is a day in which whoever guards his sight and his tongue will be forgiven."
"3351","Waki narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward, from Ibn Abi Mulayka who said: Ibn Abbas said to Urwa ibn al-Zubayr: O Urwa, ask your mother: Did your father not come with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and release ihram."
"3352","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a bone with meat on it, then went out to prayer."
"3353","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Razin: that Umar asked Ibn Abbas about this verse: When the help of Allah and the victory comes. He said: When it was revealed, his own death was announced to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3354","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Aliya, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at distress: There is no god but Allah, the Exalted, the Mighty. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth, Lord of the Mighty Throne."
"3355","Waki narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, he was in the house of A'isha. He said: Call Ali for me. A'isha said: Shall we call Abu Bakr for you. He said: Call him. Hafsa said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we call Umar for you. He said: Call him. Umm al-Fadl said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we call al-Abbas for you. He said: Call him. When they gathered, he raised his head and did not see Ali, so he fell silent. Umar said: Leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Bilal came to announce the prayer to him. He said: Command Abu Bakr to pray with the people. A'isha said: Abu Bakr is a man who cannot control himself, and whenever people do not see you they will weep, so if you commanded Umar to pray with the people. Abu Bakr went out and prayed with the people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt some relief, so he came out supported between two men, his feet trailing on the ground. When the people saw him, they glorified Allah to alert Abu Bakr, and he went to step back, so he gestured to him: Stay in your place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he sat. He said: And Abu Bakr stood on his right, and Abu Bakr followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the people followed Abu Bakr. Ibn Abbas said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took up the recitation from where Abu Bakr had reached, and he died in that illness of his, peace be upon him. And Waki once said: Abu Bakr followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the people followed Abu Bakr."
"3356","Hajjaj narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil who said: I traveled with Ibn Abbas from Madinah to Sham, and I asked him: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeath. He mentioned its meaning and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not miss the prayer until he became very heavy. He went out supported between two men, and his feet were trailing on the ground. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died and did not bequeath."
"3357","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while I was ten years old, circumcised, and I had read the decisive Qur'an."
"3358","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Fitr or Adha. He prayed, then addressed, then came to the women and admonished them and reminded them and commanded them with charity."
"3359","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash who said: I asked Ibrahim about a man praying with the imam. He said: He stands on his left. I said: Sumay al-Zayyat narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him on his right. So he took that."
"3360","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have had no contact with my wife since the afar of the palms. He said: And the afar of the palms is that when they are pollinated, they are left forty days, not watered after pollination. Then I found with my wife a man. The husband was yellowish, thin-legged, lank-haired, and the one she was accused with was muscular inclining to black, curly, very curly. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear. Then he performed li'an between them. Then she bore a man resembling the one she was accused with."
"3361","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us: that Ibn Abbas used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dates are not to be sold until they can be eaten."
"3362","Rawh narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Musa, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever dwells in the desert becomes coarse, and whoever follows game becomes heedless, and whoever comes to the ruler is tempted."
"3363","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Za'ida, and Abd al-Samad said: Za'ida narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis. Abd al-Samad said: He and those with him, sixteen months, then the qibla was changed after. Abd al-Samad said: Then the qibla was made toward the House. And Muawiya, meaning Ibn Amr, said: Then the qibla was changed after."
"3364","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi al-Jahm, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer at Dhi Qarad, a row behind him and a row facing the enemy. He prayed with them one rak'ah, then gave salam. So for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it was two rak'ahs, and for each group one rak'ah."
"3365","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Dharr, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril: What prevents you from visiting us more than you visit us. He said: Then was revealed: And we do not descend except by the command of your Lord; to Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us and what is between that, and your Lord is never forgetful. He said: And that was the answer to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3366","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into food and drink. And Abu Nu'aym narrated it to us, from Ikrima, mursal. And Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, making it musnad, from Ibn Abbas."
"3367","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of polytheists. He said: Allah created them when He created them, and He knows best what they would have done."
"3368","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim, who heard it from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood to pray tahajjud at night, said: To You is praise, You are the light of the heavens and the earth and those in them. To You is praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and those in them. To You is praise, You are the King of the heavens and the earth and those in them. To You is praise, You are the Truth, and Your promise is true, and Your meeting is true, and Paradise is true, and the Fire is true, and the Hour is true, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is true, and the prophets are true. O Allah, to You I submit, and in You I believe, and upon You I rely, and to You I turn, and by You I dispute, and to You I bring judgment. Forgive me what I have sent forth and what I have delayed, and what I concealed and what I declared. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer; there is no god but You, or: there is no god other than You."
"3369","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that Awsaja, freedman of Ibn Abbas, informed him, from Ibn Abbas: that a man died and left no one to inherit him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his inheritance to a freedman of his whom the deceased had freed, he to whom his wala belongs and who freed him."
"3370","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived while they were advancing payment for fruits for a year and two years, or two years and three. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advance payment in fruits with a known measure and a known weight and a known term."
"3371","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Za'ida narrated to us, meaning Ibn Qudama, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumra."
"3372","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Makhrama ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymuna. I said: I will observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A pillow was laid for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he slept lengthwise on it, and his family slept. Then he stood at half the night, or before it, or after it, and began wiping sleep from himself. Then he recited the last ten verses of Al Imran until he finished. Then he stood and went to a hanging waterskin, took it, performed ablution, then stood to pray. I stood and did the like of what he did, then I came and stood beside him. He placed his hand on my head, then took my ear and began twisting it. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then performed witr."
"3373","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Wa'la, from Ibn Abbas: that a man gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a skin of wine. He said: Wine has been forbidden. He called a man and spoke secretly to him. He said: What did you command him. He said: I commanded him to sell it. He said: He who forbade drinking it forbade selling it. He said: Then it was poured out."
"3374","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman, from Malik, and Ishaq narrated to me, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that he said: The sun eclipsed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people with him. He stood a long standing, he said: Like Surat al-Baqara. He said: Then he bowed a long bowing, then raised and stood a long standing, shorter than the first. Then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing. Then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing. Then he stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing. Then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing. Then he prostrated. Then he finished, and the sun had cleared. He said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. When you see that, remember Allah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you take something in this station of yours, then we saw you draw back. He said: I saw Paradise, or: I was shown Paradise - and Ishaq had no doubt, he said: I saw Paradise - and I reached for a cluster from it, and had I taken it, you would have eaten from it as long as the world remains. And I saw the Fire, and I never saw like today a more terrible sight. And I saw that most of its inhabitants were women. They said: Why, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Due to their ingratitude. He said: Do they disbelieve in Allah the Mighty and Majestic. He said: No, but they are ungrateful to the husband and ungrateful for kindness. If you do good to one of them all her life, then she sees something from you, she says: I never saw any good from you at all."
"3375","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: al-Fadl was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A woman from Khath'am came to ask him for a ruling. Al-Fadl began looking at her and she at him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began turning al-Fadl's face to the other side. She said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation on His servants in Hajj has reached my father as an old man unable to remain firm on the mount; shall I perform Hajj for him. He said: Yes. That was in the Farewell Hajj."
"3376","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I do not know whether I heard it from Sa'id ibn Jubayr or was informed of it from him, he said: I came to Ibn Abbas at Arafa while he was eating pomegranate. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast at Arafa, and Umm al-Fadl sent him milk, and he drank it."
"3377","Isma'il narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to me, and once he said: narrated to us, he said: One of the two sons of al-Abbas narrated to me, either al-Fadl or Abdullah, who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man came and said: My father - or my mother, Yahya said, and my stronger thought is that he said: my father - is old and has not performed Hajj; if I carry him on a camel he will not remain firm on it, and if I tie him to it I will not be safe for him; shall I perform Hajj for him. He said: Would you pay a debt if it were upon him. He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj for him."
"3378","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abbas or from al-Fadl ibn Abbas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning."
"3379","Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Ikrima who said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced me and said: O Allah, teach him the Book."
"3380","Isma'il narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha who said: Ammar, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixty-five years old."
"3381","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the privy, and food was brought near to him. They offered him ablution. He said: I was only commanded with ablution when I stand for prayer."
"3382","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the privy, and food was brought near to him. They said: Shall we bring you ablution. He said: Shall I pray that I should perform ablution."
"3383","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever makes an image will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe into it, and will be punished, and will never breathe into it. Whoever claims a false dream will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to tie two barley grains, or he said: between two barley grains, and will be punished, and will never tie between them. Whoever listens to the talk of people who dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection. Isma'il said: Meaning lead."
"3384","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymuna while in ihram, and consummated with her as lawful at Sarif, and she died at Sarif."
"3385","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrima who said: Ibn Abbas said about the grandfather: As for he to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend from this nation I would have taken him, then he judged him as a father, meaning Abu Bakr."
"3386","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women."
"3387","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that he said about prostration in Sad: It is not among the obligatory prostrations, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it."
"3388","Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniya narrated to us, he said: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, he said: I asked Mujahid about the prostration in Sad. He said: Yes, I asked Ibn Abbas about it. He said: Do you recite this verse: And from his offspring Dawud and Sulayman, and at its end: So by their guidance follow. He said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to follow Dawud."
"3389","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymuna. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray at night. I stood to pray with him. I stood on his left. He said to me thus, taking my head, and placed me on his right."
"3390","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I was informed from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The angel came with her until he reached the place of Zamzam, then struck with his heel, and a spring gushed forth. The woman hastened and began scooping into her waterskin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Umm Isma'il; had she not hastened, Zamzam would have been a flowing spring."
"3391","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from a shaykh of Banu Sadus who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about kissing for the fasting person. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take from the heads while fasting."
"3392","Ibn Ja'far narrated it to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Abbas, and he mentioned it."
"3393","Isma'il narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the day of Ashura. He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram, count; when you wake on the ninth, wake fasting. Yunus said: I was informed from al-Hakam that he said: I said: Is that how Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted. He said: Yes."
"3394","Isma'il and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Awf narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, Ibn Ja'far said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to me, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas, and a man asked him and said: O Ibn Abbas, I am a man whose livelihood is only from the work of my hand, and I make these pictures. He said: I will not narrate to you except what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes a picture, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will punish him on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes the spirit into it, and he will never breathe into it. He said: The man was greatly alarmed, his face turned yellow. Ibn Abbas said to him: Woe to you, if you insist on making, upon you is this tree and everything without a soul in it."
"3395","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from a man who said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to release ihram, so we released it. Garments were worn, censers burned bright, and women were married."
"3396","Isma'il narrated to us, Layth informed us, he said: Tawus said, Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray inside it, but he faced its corners."
"3397","Isma'il narrated to us, Layth informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Dhuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha in travel and residence."
"3398","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast at Arafa, and Umm al-Fadl sent him milk, and he drank it."
"3399","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrima who said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited where he was commanded to recite, and was silent where he was commanded to be silent. And your Lord is never forgetful. And there has been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"3400","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymuna while in ihram."
"3401","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten, in a ninth remaining, or a fifth remaining, or a seventh remaining."
"3402","Bahz narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, al-Ja'd the seller of adornments Abu Uthman narrated to us, Abu Raja narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in what he reports from his Lord, mighty and majestic: He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, wrote the good deeds and the evil deeds then explained that; whoever intends a good deed then does not do it, Allah writes it for him with Him as a complete good deed, and if he does it, it is written for him as ten good deeds up to seven hundredfold up to many multiples, and if he intends an evil deed then does not do it, Allah writes it for him with Him as a complete good deed, and if he does it, it is written for him as one evil deed."
"3403","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, tore meat from a shoulder then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"3404","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Azra, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and Abd al-Samad said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from a companion of his, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in the Friday prayer Surah al-Jumu'a and Surah al-Munafiqin."
"3405","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada informed us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the husband of Barira was a black slave called Mughith, and I used to see him following her in the streets of Madina squeezing his eyes over her. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning her four rulings: he ruled that wala belongs to the one who emancipates, and he gave her the choice, and he ordered her to observe the waiting period. Hammam once said: the waiting period of a free woman. He said: And charity was given to her as alms, so she gifted some of it to A'isha, and she mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"3406","Bahz narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among them al-Ashajj the brother of Banu Asr, and they said: O Prophet of Allah, we are a clan of Rabi'a, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in the sacred month, so command us with a matter that if we act upon it we will enter Paradise and we will call to it those behind us. So he commanded them with four and forbade them four: he commanded them to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and to fast Ramadan, and to perform Hajj to the House, and to give the fifth of the spoils, and he forbade them four: drinking in hantam, dubba, naqir, and muzaffat. They said: In what then shall we drink, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you are the water-skins of leather whose mouths are tied shut."
"3407","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada mention, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn Abbas, and from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among them al-Ashajj the brother of Banu Asr, and he mentioned its meaning."
"3408","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, and my father narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, Affan said: Qatada informed us, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about witr, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: One rak'a at the end of the night. He said: And I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: One rak'a at the end of the night."
"3409","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died while his armor was mortgaged with a Jew for thirty sa's of barley which he took as food for his family."
"3410","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf ibn Abi Jamila narrated to us, from Yazid al-Farisi, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in sleep at the time of Ibn Abbas. He said: And Yazid used to write copies of the Quran. He said: So I said to Ibn Abbas: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in sleep. Ibn Abbas said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah used to say: Satan cannot take my likeness, so whoever sees me in sleep has indeed seen me. So can you describe to us this man whom you saw? He said: I said: Yes, I saw a man between two men, his body and flesh brownish toward whiteness, handsome in smile, black-eyed with kohl-like eyes, beautiful round-faced, his beard had filled from here to here until it almost filled his chest. Awf said: I do not know what else was with this of description. He said: So Ibn Abbas said: Had you seen him awake you could not have described him beyond this."
"3411","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, between Makka and Madina fearing none except Allah, mighty and majestic, praying two rak'as."
"3412","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Maymuna bint al-Harith while he was in ihram."
"3413","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married while he was in ihram."
"3414","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prostrated the whiteness of his armpits could be seen while he was prostrating."
"3415","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, freed on the day of Ta'if whoever came out of the slaves of the polytheists."
"3416","Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Salm, from one of his companions, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no musa'a in Islam; whoever practiced musa'a in Jahiliyya, I have attached him to his paternal kin, and whoever claims his child born out of wedlock, he neither inherits nor is inherited from."
"3417","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a wild donkey while he was in ihram, so he returned it and said: Were it not that we are in ihram we would have accepted it from you."
"3418","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the dyed garment so long as there was in it no shedding nor deterrent discoloration."
"3419","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash, he said: Abbad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Abu Talib fell ill, a group of Quraysh entered upon him, among them Abu Jahl, and they said: O Abu Talib, your nephew reviles our gods, saying and saying and doing and doing, so send for him and forbid him. He said: So Abu Talib sent for him, and near Abu Talib was the place of one man, so he feared that if the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon his uncle he would be gentler to him, so he jumped up and sat in that place. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered he found no seat except by the door, so he sat. Abu Talib said: O son of my brother, your people complain of you, claiming that you revile their gods and say and say and do and do. He said: O uncle, I only want them upon one word by which the Arabs will submit to them and the non-Arabs will pay them jizya thereby. They said: And what is it? Yes, by your father, ten. He said: There is no god but Allah. He said: So they stood brushing off their garments while saying: Has he made the gods one god? This is indeed a strange thing. He said: Then he recited until he reached: before they taste My punishment."
"3420","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A woman came to him and said: My mother died with a month of Ramadan fasting due upon her, shall I make it up for her? He said: What do you think, had there been a debt upon her, would you pay it? She said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah, mighty and majestic, is more deserving to be paid."
"3421","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The previously married woman is more entitled to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is consulted concerning herself, and her silence is her consent."
"3422","Ya'la and Muhammad with the same meaning said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Zabyan, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Which of the two readings do you count as first? They said: The reading of Abdullah. He said: No, rather it is the last; the Quran was presented to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, every year once, and in the year in which he died it was presented to him twice, and Abdullah witnessed it, so he knew what of it was abrogated and what was altered."
"3423","Ya'la narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning the mukatab who is killed: blood-money of a free man for what he has paid of his contract, and what remains the blood-money of a slave."
"3424","Ya'la narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ikrima, who said: I was sitting with Zayd ibn Ali in Madina when an old man called Shurahbil Abu Sa'd passed, and he said: O Abu Sa'd, whence have you come? He said: From the Commander of the Believers; I narrated a hadith to him, and he said: That this hadith be true is dearer to me than red camels. He said: Narrate it to the people. He said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim whose two daughters reach him and he treats them kindly as long as they accompany him or he accompanies them except that they admit him into Paradise."
"3425","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the most generous of people in goodness, and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril met him, and Jibril used to meet him every night in Ramadan until it ended, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, presenting the Quran to him; and when Jibril met him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was more generous in goodness than the blowing wind."
"3426","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us, from Abdullah with the same meaning, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wear white of your garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them, and indeed the best of your kohls is ithmid, for it grows hair and clears vision."
"3427","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, who said: I wrote to Ibn Abbas, and he wrote to me: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The oath is upon the one claimed against, and had people been given by their claims, people would have claimed the wealth and blood of people."
"3428","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata al-Attar narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning a man who approaches his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He gives a dinar in charity, and if he does not find, then half a dinar."
"3429","Abu Kamil and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Jamra, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed in Makka thirteen years and in Madina ten years receiving revelation, and he died at sixty-three years."
"3430","Abu Kamil and Yunus said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to deliver the sermon leaning against a trunk, and when the minbar was made and he moved to it, the trunk moaned, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to it and embraced it, and it calmed, and he said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection."
"3431","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, the like of it."
"3432","al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, and from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to deliver the sermon leaning against the palm trunk, and he mentioned its meaning."
"3433","Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, picked meat from a bone then prayed and did not touch water."
"3434","Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: If they come to you then judge between them or turn away from them, and if you turn away from them they will not harm you at all, and if you judge then judge between them with justice; Allah loves the just: He said: Banu al-Nadir, when they killed a victim of Banu Qurayza, paid them half the blood-money, and when Banu Qurayza killed a victim of Banu al-Nadir, they paid them the full blood-money, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made the blood-money equal between them."
"3435","Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to me, from Ikrima and Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the postpartum woman and the menstruating woman bathe and enter ihram and perform all the rites except that she does not circumambulate the House until she is pure."
"3436","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to prostrate in Sad."
"3437","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Rushdayn ibn Kurayb informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I stood at his side on his left, so he took me and placed me on his right. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: I was then ten years old."
"3438","Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: We were invited to food, and among us were Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Miqsam the freedman of Ibn Abbas, and when the food was placed Sa'id said: All of you have heard what was said about food. Miqsam said: Narrate, O Abu Abdullah, to whoever has not heard. He said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When food is placed, do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends upon its middle, but eat from its edges."
"3439","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Tawus report from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, that he witnessed the judgment of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in that: Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabigha came and said: I was between two wives when one of them struck the other with a tent-pole and killed her and her fetus, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning her fetus a ghurra, a slave, and that she be killed. I said to Amr: Ibn Tawus informed me from his father such-and-such, and he said: You have made me doubt. Ibn Bakr said: I was between my two wives when one of them struck the other."
"3440","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed us, from Ibn Abbas, that Khidham Abu Wadi'a married his daughter to a man, so she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and complained to him that she had been married while unwilling, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took her away from her husband and said: Do not coerce them. He said: So after that she married Abu Lubaba al-Ansari, and she was previously married."
"3441","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it, with addition: Then she came to him afterward and informed him that he had touched her, so he prevented her from returning to her first husband, and he said: O Allah, if his faith is that he make her lawful for Rifa'a, then let his marriage to her never be completed again. Then she came to Abu Bakr and Umar during their caliphates, and both prevented her."
"3442","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me that Tawus informed him, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed while circumambulating the Ka'ba by a man leading a man by a nose-ring in his nose, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut it with his hand and ordered him to lead him by his hand."
"3443","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me that Tawus informed him, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed while circumambulating the Ka'ba by a man who had tied his hand to another man with a strap or a thread or something else, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut it with his hand then said: Lead him by his hand."
"3444","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliya, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by people shooting and said: Shoot, O sons of Isma'il, for your father was an archer."
"3445","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Yahya ibn Abdullah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and mentioned the hadith, and he said: I heard your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The slain will come on the Day of Resurrection holding his head, either he said with his left or with his right, his jugular veins gushing, before the Throne of the Most Merciful, blessed and exalted, saying: O Lord, ask this one for what he killed me."
"3446","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: It reached me that the Prophet when he prostrated the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"3447","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, the like of that, from the Prophet."
"3448","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Teach and ease and do not make difficult, and when you become angry then be silent, and when you become angry then be silent, and when you become angry then be silent."
"3449","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have had no contact with my wife since the afar of the palms, or its ighfar. He said: And the afar of the palms, or its ighfar, is that they were pollinated then left unwatered forty days without watering after pollination. He said: So I found a man with my wife, and her husband was yellowish, thin-legged, lank-haired, while the one she was accused with was a bulky man toward blackness, curly and crisp-haired. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, make clear, O Allah, make clear. Then he performed li'an between them, and she bore a child resembling the one she was accused with."
"3450","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Shall I not inform you of the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So he called for water and began to scoop with his right hand then pour upon the left."
"3451","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Sumay' al-Zayyat, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: I stood beside the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at his left, so he turned me and placed me at his right."
"3452","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a dead sheep belonging to Maymuna and said: Why did you not make use of its hide? They said: And how, while it is dead? He said: Only its meat was forbidden. Ma'mar said: And al-Zuhri used to reject tanning and say: It is used in every case."
"3453","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution then cut meat from a shoulder and ate, then went to prayer and did not perform ablution."
"3454","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, and Abd al-A'la, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Hajj, or he said on the day of the Conquest, while he was praying, I and al-Fadl riding together on a donkey, so we cut across the row and dismounted from it then entered the row, while the donkey passed in front of them and did not interrupt their prayer. And Abd al-A'la said: I was the rider behind al-Fadl on a donkey, so we came while the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying with the people at Mina."
"3455","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he saw images in the House, meaning the Ka'ba, did not enter and ordered them effaced, and he saw Ibrahim and Isma'il, upon them be peace, with divining arrows in their hands, so he said: May Allah kill them; by Allah, they never cast lots with arrows at all."
"3456","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek it in the last ten, in a ninth remaining, or a fifth remaining, or a seventh remaining."
"3457","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A slave of Banu Bayada cupped the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him his wage, and had it been forbidden he would not have given him; he said: And he ordered his masters to lighten some of his tax."
"3458","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the effeminate among men and the masculine among women."
"3459","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrima ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was in the house of Maymuna, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood praying at night, so I stood with him on his left, and he took my hand and placed me at his right, then he prayed thirteen rak'as; I estimated the length of his standing in each rak'a as Surah al-Muzzammil."
"3460","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out in the year of the Conquest to Makka in the month of Ramadan, and he fasted until he reached al-Kudayd, then he broke his fast. Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out in the year of the Conquest to Makka in the month of Ramadan, and he fasted until he passed by a pond on the road, and that was at midday zenith. He said: So the people thirsted and stretched their necks and their souls yearned for it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called for a cup with water in it and held it upon his hand until the people saw it, then he drank, and the people drank."
"3461","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, Ibn Bakr said: Then I heard him afterward, meaning Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: There was a sheep or a domestic goat belonging to one of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it died, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why did you not make use of its hide or its skin?"
"3462","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed me that Miqsam the freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him, he said: I was with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when Sa'd and Ibn Umar asked him about wiping over the leather socks, so Umar ruled for Sa'd. Ibn Abbas said: So I said: O Sa'd, we have known that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped over his leather socks, but was it before al-Ma'ida or after it? He said: Rawh said: Or after it. He said: No one will inform you that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped over them after al-Ma'ida was revealed. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, fell silent."
"3463","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was eating a shank, the caller to prayer came to him, so he put it down and stood for prayer and did not touch water."
"3464","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed me that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him that he heard Ibn Abbas and saw Abu Hurayra perform ablution, and he said: Do you know from what I perform ablution? He said: No. He said: I perform ablution from crumbs of dried yogurt I ate. Ibn Abbas said: I do not care from what you performed ablution; I bear witness that I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eat meat from a shoulder then stand for prayer and not perform ablution. He said: And Sulayman was present for that from both of them together."
"3465","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: My knowledge and what occurs to my mind is that Abu al-Sha'tha informed me that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe with the leftover water of Maymuna. Abd al-Razzaq said: And that is because I asked him about two junubs emptying water together."
"3466","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: Which time is dearer to you that I pray Isha, as imam or alone? He said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed Isha one night until the people slept and woke and slept and woke, then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: The prayer. Ata said: Ibn Abbas said: So the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out as though I look at him now, his head dripping water, placing his hand upon the side of his head, and he said: Were it not to burden my umma I would have ordered them to pray it thus."
"3467","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Sha'tha informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eight together and seven together."
"3468","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me that Tawus informed him that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he rose at night, and he mentioned similar to the supplication of Sufyan, except that he said: Your promise is true, and Your word is true, and meeting You is true, and he said: And what I concealed and what I declared; You are my God, there is no god but You."
"3469","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the most generous of mankind; it was only that when the month of Ramadan entered, Jibril, peace be upon him, studied with him, and he was more generous than the wind."
"3470","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, who said: Ibn Abbas used to narrate that Abu Bakr uncovered the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was dead, a Hibara cloak spread over him, and he looked at the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then bent over him and kissed him."
"3471","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that he mentioned the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about bathing on Friday. Tawus said: So I said to Ibn Abbas: And touching perfume or oil if one's family has it? He said: I do not know it."
"3472","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Khidash narrated to me that Ibn Abbas said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, overlooked the graveyard, which was upon his first road, he pointed with his hand behind the braid, or he said behind the braided hair, Abd al-Razzaq doubted, and said: What an excellent graveyard is this. So I said to the one who informed me: Did he specify the ravine? He said: Thus he said. He did not inform me that he specified anything except thus he pointed with his hand behind the braid or the braided hair, and we used to hear that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, specified the ravine facing the House."
"3473","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abd al-Karim and others informed me, from Miqsam the freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that Ibn Abbas informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed for the menstruant the rate of a dinar, and if he has intercourse with her when the blood has ceased but she has not bathed, then half a dinar, all that from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3474","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Muhammad ibn Jubayr say: Ibn Abbas used to forbid anticipating the fasting of Ramadan when the crescent of Ramadan was not seen, and say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you do not see the crescent, complete thirty nights."
"3475","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I have not known the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to seek out fasting a day seeking its merit over others except this day, for the day of Ashura, or Ramadan. Rawh said: Or the month of Ramadan."
"3476","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said: Abdullah ibn Abbas invited al-Fadl ibn Abbas on the day of Arafa to food, and he said: I am fasting. Abdullah said: Do not fast, for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a milking vessel with milk on the day of Arafa and he drank from it, so do not fast, for the people follow your example."
"3477","Ibn Bakr and Rawh said: The people follow your example. Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Umar informed me that Ata informed him that Ibn Abbas invited al-Fadl."
"3478","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu Ma'bad the freedman of Ibn Abbas informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that raising the voice with remembrance when people leave the obligatory prayer was at the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and that he said: Ibn Abbas said: I used to know when they left by that when I heard it."
"3479","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I spent a night at my aunt Maymuna's, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood praying voluntary prayer at night, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to the water-skin and performed ablution, then stood praying. So I stood when I saw him do that, and performed ablution from the water-skin, then I stood at his left side, and he took my hand from behind his back adjusting me thus from behind his back to the right side."
"3480","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas informed me, from Ikrima and from Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas said: Shall I not narrate to you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while traveling? He said: We said: Yes. He said: When the sun declined while he was in his dwelling, he combined Zuhr and Asr before riding, and if it had not declined for him in his dwelling, he traveled until when Asr came he dismounted and combined Zuhr and Asr, and when Maghrib came while in his dwelling, he combined it with Isha, and if it had not come while in his dwelling, he rode until when Isha came he dismounted and combined them."
"3481","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it. He said: Ibn Abbas said: And I deem everything in the position of food."
"3482","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade meeting the caravans and that a townsman sell for a Bedouin. He said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What is his saying: a townsman for a Bedouin? He said: Let him not be his broker."
"3483","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrima, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Abu Jahl said: If I see Muhammad praying at the Ka'ba I shall tread upon his neck. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Had he done so the angels would have seized him openly."
"3484","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My Lord, mighty and majestic, came to me tonight in the best form, I think meaning in sleep, and said: O Muhammad, do you know concerning what the highest assembly disputes? He said: I said: No. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So He placed His hand between my shoulders until I felt its coolness between my breasts, or he said my throat, and I knew what is in the heavens and what is in the earth. Then He said: O Muhammad, do you know concerning what the highest assembly disputes? He said: I said: Yes, they dispute concerning expiations and degrees. He said: And what are the expiations and degrees? He said: Remaining in the mosques, and walking on foot to the congregations, and completing ablution in hardship, and whoever does that lives in good and dies in good and is of his sin as on the day his mother bore him. And say, O Muhammad, when you pray: O Allah, I ask You for good deeds and abandoning evils and loving the poor, and when You intend trial for Your servants, take me to You untempted. He said: And the degrees are giving food and spreading peace and praying at night while people sleep."
"3485","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the chiefs of Quraysh gathered in the Hijr and pledged by al-Lat and al-Uzza and Manat the third other that if we see Muhammad we shall rise against him as one man and not leave him until we kill him. He said: So Fatima came weeping until she entered upon her father and said: These chiefs of your people in the Hijr have pledged that if they see you they will rise against you and kill you; there is not a man among them but knows his share of your blood. He said: O daughter, bring ablution water. So he performed ablution then entered the mosque upon them, and when they saw him they said: It is he. They lowered their eyes and were transfixed in their seats, and did not raise their eyes to him, and not a man of them rose. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came until he stood over their heads, and he took a handful of dust and threw it at them and said: The faces are disfigured. He said: No pebble struck a man of them but he was killed as a disbeliever on the day of Badr."
"3486","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, who said: I know it only from Ibn Abbas, that the banner of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was with Ali ibn Abi Talib, and the banner of the Ansar was with Sa'd ibn Ubada, and when fighting grew fierce the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be under the banner of the Ansar."
"3487","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas, and he was asked: Did you witness the Eid with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, and were it not for my kinship to him I would not have witnessed it due to youth. So he prayed two rak'as then delivered the sermon, then he came to the banner which was by the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt, and he admonished the women and reminded them and ordered them to give charity, so they reached toward their ears and throats and gave it in charity. He said: So they handed it to Bilal."
"3488","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that he did not hold that one should stop at al-Abtah, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only stayed there for A'isha."
"3489","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The mukatab is compensated according to the portion he has paid with the blood-money of a free man, and what remains with the blood-money of a slave."
"3490","Yazid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrima ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I came to my aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith and spent the night with her, and that night I found to belong to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Isha then entered his house and placed his head upon a cushion of leather stuffed with fiber. So I came and placed my head upon a side of it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke and looked, and night was upon him, so he glorified Allah and magnified Him until he slept. Then he awoke when half the night had gone, or he said two-thirds, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and relieved himself, then he came to a water-skin hung upon a wooden frame with water in it, and he rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water three times and washed his face three times and his forearms three by three and wiped his head and ears then washed his feet. Yazid said: I think he said three by three. Then he came to his prayer place, so I stood and did as he did, then I came and stood at his left, intending to pray following his prayer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, waited until when he knew I intended to pray following his prayer, he turned to his right and took my ear and turned me until he placed me at his right. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed two rak'as as long as night was upon him in his view. When he thought dawn had drawn near, he stood and prayed six rak'as and made witr with the seventh. When dawn brightened, he stood and prayed two rak'as, then he laid his side down and slept until I heard his snoring. Then Bilal came to him and announced the prayer, so he went out and prayed and did not touch water. So I said to Sa'id ibn Jubayr: How fine is this! Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: By Allah, I said that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: Be quiet; it is not for you nor your companions; it is for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he was safeguarded."
"3491","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man when he stones the Jamra, may he perfume himself? He said: As for me, I saw musk in the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; is it of perfume or not?"
"3492","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Narrate to me about riding between al-Safa and al-Marwa, for your people claim it is sunna. He said: They told truth and lied. I said: What is their truth and lie? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Makka, and they came out until the cloistered maidens came out, and none was struck in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode and circumambulated while riding, and had he dismounted walking would have been dearer to him."
"3493","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, between Makka and Madina fearing none except Allah, mighty and majestic, praying two rak'as."
"3494","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatada, from Musa ibn Salama, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about prayer at al-Batha when I miss prayer in congregation, and he said: Two rak'as; that is the sunna of Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3495","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Rather the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the mosque while upon his camel with Usama ibn Zayd behind him, and he asked for drink, so we gave him nabidh to drink, and he drank then handed his remainder to Usama ibn Zayd and said: You have done well and beautifully; do thus. We do not wish to change that."
"3496","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Mis'ar informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it. Mis'ar said: And I think he said: Or fodder."
"3497","Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I gave the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Zamzam to drink, and he drank while standing."
"3498","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Sa'd informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raised his head from bowing said: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and the earth and filling whatever You will after."
"3499","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you eats food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked."
"3500","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, that he heard Ikrima say: Ibn Abbas used to say: And We made the vision which We showed you only a trial for people: He said: A thing the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was shown awake which he saw with his eye when he was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis."
"3501","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ata say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would love to have another like it along with it, and nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents. Then Ibn Abbas said: I do not know whether it is from the Quran or not."
"3502","Rawh narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me that Said ibn Jubayr narrated to him, Ibn Abbas said: I came to my maternal aunt Maymunah and found that night to be her night with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned something like the hadith of Yazid except that he said: until when the first dawn rose the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, waited a little, until when the morning light became clear to him he stood and prayed the witr as nine rakahs, giving salams in every two rakahs, until when he finished his witr he waited a little, until when it was morning in his own view the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and bowed the two rakahs of Fajr for the Subh prayer, then he laid his side down and slept until I heard his heavy breathing. He said: then Bilal came and woke him for the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and prayed the Subh."
"3503","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas used to say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed in Makkah thirteen years and died when he was sixty-three years old."
"3504","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, his mother has died, so will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: I have a garden of date-palms and I call you to witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf."
"3505","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, that Ibn Abbas used to mention that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave a concession to the menstruating woman to depart before performing the circumambulation if she had already performed the circumambulation of al-Ifadah."
"3506","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for a ruling about a vow incumbent upon his mother who died before fulfilling it, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"3507","Rawh narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah ibn Raqabah, from Talhah al-Iyami, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3508","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Yala informed me that he heard Ikrimah, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, say: Ibn Abbas informed us that the mother of Sad ibn Ubadah died while he was absent from her, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died while I was absent from her, so will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: I call you to witness that my fruitful walled garden is charity on her behalf."
"3509","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi al-Aliyah al-Bara, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for Hajj and arrived when four days of Dhu al-Hijjah had passed, and he prayed Subh with us at al-Batha, then he said: Whoever wishes to make it an Umrah, let him make it so."
"3510","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abi Sinan, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Aqra ibn Habis asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Is Hajj every year? He said: No, rather one Hajjah, and whoever performs Hajj after that, it is voluntary, and had I said yes it would have become obligatory, and had it become obligatory you would not have heard nor obeyed."
"3511","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, blessed and exalted, will surely raise the Stone on the Day of Resurrection having two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, testifying for whoever touched it rightfully."
"3512","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions performed Umrah from al-Jiirranah, and they bared their shoulders and placed their upper garments under their armpits and cast them over their shoulders, then they walked briskly."
"3513","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the night of Muzdalifah: O sons of my brother, O Banu Hashim, hasten before the crowding of the people, and let none of you stone al-Aqabah until the sun rises."
"3514","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Kamil informed us, from Habib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymunah. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke during the night, then he mentioned the hadith. He said: then he bowed. He said: I saw him say in his bowing: Glory to my Lord the Most Great. Then he raised his head and praised Allah as much as he willed to praise Him. He said: then he prostrated, and he would say in his prostration: Glory to my Lord the Most High. He said: then he raised his head, and he would say between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, mend me, raise me, provide for me, and guide me."
"3515","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abi al-Bakhtari, he said: We sighted the crescent of Ramadan at Dhat Irq, so we sent to Ibn Abbas asking him, and he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has extended it for its sighting, so if it is obscured from you, complete the number."
"3516","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed in Makkah thirteen years and died when he was sixty-three."
"3517","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sent at forty years of age, and he stayed in Makkah thirteen years with revelation coming to him, then he was commanded to emigrate, so he emigrated for ten years, and he died when he was sixty-three years old, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3518","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu Hadir informed me, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about the earthen jar in which nabidh is made, and he said: Allah and His Messenger forbade it. So the man went to Ibn Abbas and mentioned to him what Ibn Umar had said, and Ibn Abbas said: He spoke the truth. The man said to Ibn Abbas: Which jar did he forbid? He said: Everything made of clay."
"3519","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the verse of debt was revealed, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The first to deny was Adam, upon him prayer and peace. He said it three times. When Allah created Adam, upon him prayer and peace, He wiped his back and brought forth from him all that He would scatter until the Day of Resurrection, and He began to present them to him, and he saw among them a man shining, so he said: O my Lord, which of my sons is this? He said: This is your son Dawud. He said: O my Lord, how long is his life? He said: Sixty years. He said: O my Lord, increase his life. He said: No, unless you add to him from your own life. The life of Adam was a thousand years, so he gave him forty years from his life, and Allah, mighty and majestic, wrote a document against him and had the angels witness it. When Adam, upon him peace, was approached and the angels came to him to take his soul, he said: My term has not come, forty years of my life remain. They said: You gave them to your son Dawud. He said: I did not do so nor did I give him anything, and Allah, mighty and majestic, produced the document against him and established the angels as witnesses against him."
"3520","Rawh narrated to us, Zamah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abi Sinan al-Duali, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has prescribed Hajj upon you. Then al-Aqra ibn Habis said: Forever, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Rather one Hajjah, and had I said yes it would have become obligatory."
"3521","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: A sheep belonging to Maymunah died, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why did you not make use of its skin? They said: It is dead meat. He said: Tanning the hide is its purification."
"3522","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi Mijlaz, that a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I stoned with six or seven. He said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned the jamrah with six or seven."
"3523","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while in ihram, on his head, because of a headache he felt."
"3524","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Tawus: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while in ihram, on his head."
"3525","Rawh and Abu Dawud, with the same meaning, both said: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi Hassan al-Araj, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then he marked the sacrificial animal on the right side of the hump, then he wiped the blood from it and garlanded it with two sandals, then he mounted his she-camel, and when it stood upright with him at al-Bayda he entered ihram. He said: So he entered ihram at noon. Abu Dawud said: For Hajj."
"3526","Rawh narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, he said: Ibn Umar used to perform ablution three times, attributing it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Ibn Abbas used to perform ablution once each time, attributing it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3527","Rawh and Affan both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Qays, Affan said in his hadith: Hammad informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Zamzam, so we drew a bucket for him and he drank, then he rinsed his mouth into it, then we poured it into Zamzam, then he said: Were it not that you would be overcome in it, I would have drawn with my own hands."
"3528","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, that a Bedouin said to Ibn Abbas: What is the matter that the household of Muawiyah give water and honey to drink, and the household of so-and-so give milk to drink, while you give nabidh to drink? Is it miserliness on your part or need? Ibn Abbas said: There is neither miserliness in us nor need, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us with his companion behind him Usamah ibn Zayd, and he asked for drink, so we gave him to drink from this, meaning the nabidh of the water-service, and he drank from it and said: You have done well, do thus."
"3529","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to the water of Zamzam and we gave him to drink, and he drank standing."
"3530","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Abi Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or together with her maternal aunt."
"3531","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with three: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, Say O you disbelievers, and Say He is Allah the One."
"3532","Rawh narrated to us, Said and Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Tufayl, he said: Muawiyah would not pass any corner of the House without touching it, so Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to touch only these two corners. Muawiyah said: Nothing of its corners is to be left untouched. Abd al-Wahhab said: The Yamani corner and the Stone."
"3533","Rawh narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Abi al-Tufayl, he said: I was with Muawiyah and Ibn Abbas while they were circumambulating the House, and Ibn Abbas would touch the two corners while Muawiyah would touch all the corners, so Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would touch only these two corners, the Yamani and the Black. Muawiyah said: Nothing of it is to be left untouched."
"3534","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abi al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walked briskly around the House and that it is a sunnah. He said: They spoke truly and falsely. I said: How did they speak truly and falsely? He said: They spoke truly, he did walk briskly around the House, and they spoke falsely, it is not a sunnah. Quraysh said at the time of al-Hudaybiyah: Leave Muhammad and his companions until they die the death of the naghaf worm. When they made peace with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on condition that they come the next year and stay in Makkah three days, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came the next year while the polytheists were on the side of Quayqian, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Walk briskly around the House three times. But it is not a sunnah."
"3535","Yunus and Surayj both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abi Asim al-Ghanawi, from Abi al-Tufayl, then he mentioned the hadith."
"3536","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Quraysh said: Muhammad and his companions have been weakened by the fever of Yathrib. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived for his year in which he performed Umrah, he said to his companions: Walk briskly around the House so that the polytheists see your strength. When they walked briskly, Quraysh said: They have not been weakened."
"3537","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Black Stone is from Paradise, and it was whiter than snow until the sins of the people of polytheism blackened it."
"3538","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rinsed his mouth from milk and said: It has fat in it."
"3539","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among the most generous of people, and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril would meet him, meeting him every night and studying the Quran with him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Jibril met him, was more generous than the sent wind."
"3540","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abi Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was aided by al-Saba and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur."
"3541","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, that Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to him, from his father, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me that he spent the night with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he awoke during the night and took his tooth-stick and cleaned his teeth with it, then he performed ablution while reciting: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth, until he recited these verses and finished at the end of the surah, then he prayed two rakahs and lengthened the standing, bowing, and prostration in them, then he left until I heard the breathing of sleep, then he awoke and cleaned his teeth and performed ablution while reciting, until he did that three times, then he prayed witr with three. Then Bilal the caller to prayer came to him, so he went out to the prayer while saying: O Allah, place light in my heart, place light in my hearing, place light in my sight, place light before me and light behind me, place light on my right and light on my left, and light above me and light beneath me. O Allah, magnify light for me."
"3542","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abi Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The first to pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after Khadijah was Ali. And he said once: He accepted Islam."
"3543","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrate from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died when I was fifteen years old."
"3544","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, al-Hakam and Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird."
"3545","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, and Hasan ibn Musa, Thabit narrated to us, he said: Hilal narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would spend nights, Abd al-Samad said: successive nights, with his stomach empty, while his family found no supper, and most of their bread was barley bread."
"3546","Abd al-Samad and Hasan both said: Thabit narrated to us, he said, Hasan said Abu Zayd, Abd al-Samad said: Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis, then he came back in his night and told them of his journey, of the sign of Bayt al-Maqdis, and of their caravan. Some people said, Hasan said: We believe Muhammad in what he says, then they apostatized as disbelievers, so Allah struck their necks along with Abu Jahl. Abu Jahl said: Muhammad frightens us with the tree of al-Zaqqum, bring dates and butter so we may eat heartily. He saw the Dajjal in his form with the vision of the eye, not the vision of sleep, and he saw Isa and Musa and Ibrahim, the prayers of Allah upon them. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the Dajjal, and he said: Bright white and thick. Hasan said: He said: I saw him huge, bright white and thick, one of his eyes standing as though a brilliant star, as though the hair of his head were the branches of a tree. I saw Isa as a young man, white, curly-headed, sharp-sighted, full-chested in build. I saw Musa dark and brown, with abundant hair, Hasan said: hair, strong in build. I looked at Ibrahim, and I would not look at any limb of his limbs without seeing it as from myself, as though he were your companion. Jibril, upon him peace, said: Greet Malik, so I greeted him."
"3547","Abd al-Samad and Hasan both said: Thabit narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, he was asked, Hasan said: I asked Ikrimah about the fasting person, does he get cupped? He said: It was only disliked because of weakness. And he narrated from Ibn Abbas, Hasan said: then he narrated from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while in ihram because of a morsel he had eaten from a poisoned sheep poisoned by a woman from the people of Khaybar. The end of the hadiths of Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both."
